0b749825-1907-40cf-805b-afe41a30330a	default	decision	The chart-perception selector must distinguish structural pane boundaries from in-pane price gridlines using features beyond variant support and consensus. Durable selector principles: (1) a candidate line coincident with a numeric price-axis tick label is an in-pane gridline, not a pane boundary; (2) a true pane boundary is marked by a content-type change immediately below (e.g., candles→volume bars, or a new scale axis); (3) variant support and consensus are necessary but not sufficient — the in-pane gridline can have higher support/consensus than the true separator; (4) max_length is not a reliable discriminator; (5) the uncertainty reporter must flag near-ties where the selected candidate is coincident with a price-axis label rather than silently promoting it. These are general principles applied to any chart layout, not hard-coded y-values.	6b544c7a0416896edbdbc1453a0cb870aa7dfe31f535bbb523d0674a89fef4f5	active	69476279-0085-4c23-bd9d-61561a12f045	\N	2026-09-19 22:57:57.600038-04	2026-09-19 22:57:57.600038-04
