55	chat-a75c8e0b-516d-4e77-932e-0ee779c79575	step-05	write_file	{"path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\goBackend\\\\README.md", "content": "# goBackend\\n\\n## Purpose\\n\\n`goBackend` is a small Go HTTP API that provides read-only access to a PostgreSQL database. It uses the standard `net/http` package and a `pgx` connection pool.\\n\\nEndpoints:\\n\\n- `GET /health`\\n- `GET /api/customers?id=<int>`\\n- `GET /api/schemas`\\n- `GET /api/tables?schema=<schema>&name=<substring>&limit=<int>`\\n\\nThe server also includes CORS middleware with a hardcoded allowlist for local and private frontend origins.\\n\\n## Directory structure\\n\\n```text\\ngoBackend/\\n├── main.go                  # GoLand IDE template; not the server entry point\\n├── cmd/\\n│   └── server/\\n│       └── main.go          # Server entry point: loads .env, config, DB pool, routes, CORS\\n├── internal/\\n│   ├── config/\\n│   │   └── config.go        # Reads DATABASE_URL and PORT\\n│   ├── db/\\n│   │   └── db.go            # Creates and pings pgxpool\\n│   └── handlers/\\n│       ├── health.go        # App struct and /health handler\\n│       ├── customers.go     # /api/customers handler\\n│       ├── schemas.go       # /api/schemas handler\\n│       └── tables.go        # /api/tables handler\\n├── .env                     # Local environment configuration\\n├── go.mod\\n├── go.sum\\n└── .idea/                   # GoLand IDE settings\\n```\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\nModule: `goBackend`\\n\\nGo version: `1.26`\\n\\nRuntime libraries imported by source:\\n\\n- `github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 v5.9.1` — PostgreSQL driver and `pgxpool`\\n- `github.com/joho/godotenv v1.5.1` — `.env` loading\\n\\nSupporting modules present in `go.mod` / `go.sum`:\\n\\n- `github.com/jackc/pgpassfile v1.0.0`\\n- `github.com/jackc/pgservicefile v0.0.0-20240606120523-5a60cdf6a761`\\n- `github.com/jackc/puddle/v2 v2.2.2`\\n- `golang.org/x/sync v0.17.0`\\n- `golang.org/x/text v0.29.0`\\n\\nNote: `go.mod` currently lists all modules as indirect; running `go mod tidy` may reclassify directly imported modules.\\n\\n## Configuration / environment variables\\n\\n| Variable | Required | Default | Description |\\n|---|---:|---:|---|\\n| `DATABASE_URL` | Yes | None | PostgreSQL connection string. The server exits if this is missing. |\\n| `PORT` | No | `8080` | HTTP listen port. |\\n\\nThe repository includes a local `.env` file. Keep real credentials out of version control.\\n\\n## Build, run, and test\\n\\nPrerequisites: Go `1.26` or newer and a reachable PostgreSQL database.\\n\\n```bash\\n# Run directly\\ngo run ./cmd/server\\n\\n# Build a binary\\ngo build -o goBackend ./cmd/server\\n./goBackend\\n\\n# Run tests (no *_test.go files are currently present)\\ngo test ./...\\n```\\n\\nExample health check:\\n\\n```bash\\ncurl http://localhost:8080/health\\n```\\n\\nIf `PORT` is set, replace `8080` with that port."}	{"ok": true, "path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\goBackend\\\\README.md", "tool": "write_file", "bytes": 2705, "sha256": "13e2792f6ab49a81bab2b634163303265332c6fad3c48d3d3ecfcfa0bd797ce7", "created": true}	f	2026-09-16 19:38:21.342734-04
