 the price pane are at **765, 762.5, 760, 758, 755, 752.5, 750, 747.5** — i.e. **8 gridlines**, spaced 2.50 apart, with the bottom one at 747.50 and the second‑from‑bottom at **750.00**.\\n\\nIn the geometric‑consensus image (image 2) the yellow lines that actually render are a subset of these plus the pane borders: I can place them at roughly **760, 755, 750, and 747.5** inside the price pane, plus the top/bottom borders of each indicator pane. So in image 2 you see about **4 interior price gridlines + 5 pane‑separator lines**.\\n\\n**1) Lowest wick relative to gridlines**\\nThe lowest wick tip in the price pane is the long lower wick of the sharp red drop on the right side of the chart. Its tip sits between the **752.50** and **755.00** gridlines — visually a touch *below* the 752.50 line, in the **≈752–753** zone. It is clearly **above the 750.00 gridline**.\\n\\n**2) Gridline count / positions**\\nPrice pane: 8 gridlines at 765 / 762.5 / 760 / 758 / 755 / 752.5 / 750 / 747.5. Consensus image: ~4 of those rendered as yellow lines (≈760, 755, 750, 747.5) plus the pane borders.\\n\\n**3) Does any wick extend below the second‑to‑last gridline (750.00)?**\\n**No.** The lowest wick (≈752–753) stays above the 750.00 line, so it does not cross below the second‑from‑bottom gridline. The only things that go below 750 are the axis label region and the indicator panes, not any price wick.\\n\\n**4) Lowest red/dark wick tip in the color image**\\nIt is the lower wick of the final red candle in the sharp sell‑off (right edge of the price pane). Position: **above the 750 gridline**, sitting just under the 752.5 gridline (≈752–753). It is *not* at or below 750.\\n\\n**Bottom line on the precision question:** the lowest wick is **ABOVE the 750 gridline** (roughly 752–753), not at or below it.\\n\\nCaveat: I'm reading pixel positions off a compressed screenshot, so the \\"≈752–753\\" estimate carries a small margin (±~0.3–0.5). The qualitative conclusion — above 750, below 752.5 