78	chat-ed0880fd-fdcf-46b9-b6ac-1b9ca7affbf6	step-02	vision_image	{"paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916.jpg", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\geometry_overlay.png"], "prompt": "This is a QQQ stock chart screenshot. I need you to:\\n1. Read ALL visible price axis labels (the numbers on the right or left side of the chart) and report their approximate pixel y-positions if you can estimate them.\\n2. Identify the main price pane boundaries (top and bottom edges of the candlestick area).\\n3. Identify any secondary panes (volume, indicators) and their boundaries.\\n4. Report the time axis labels visible at the bottom.\\n5. Note any UI elements, annotations, or text overlays.\\n6. Describe the overall layout: how many panes, what's in each.\\n\\nBe precise about the price labels you can read - I need exact numbers to build a pixel-to-price mapping."}	{"ok": true, "tool": "vision_image", "paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916.jpg", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\geometry_overlay.png"], "answer": "Below is my read of the screenshot. **Caveat up front:** I'm estimating pixel coordinates by eye from a portrait‑oriented image of unknown exact dimensions, so treat the y‑values as approximate (±10–20 px). Use them to *seed* your pixel‑to‑price fit, then refine with your own pixel picker. The price labels themselves are read directly off the axis and are reliable.\\n\\n## 1. Price axis labels (right side, top pane) and estimated y‑positions\\n\\n| Label | Est. y (px) | Note |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 712.00 | ~190 | top gridline |\\n| 710.00 | ~310 | |\\n| 708.00 | ~430 | |\\n| 706.00 | ~550 | |\\n| 704.69 | ~660 | **green current‑price tag** (not a gridline) |\\n| 704.00 | ~670–700 | gridline just below the green tag |\\n| 702.00 | ~790–820 | |\\n| 700.00 | ~910–940 | bottom gridline of price pane |\\n\\nThe 2.00‑unit gridlines are evenly spaced (~120 px apart), i.e. **≈ 60 px per 1.00 price unit**. Using two anchors (712 @ ~190, 700 @ ~910):\\n\\n> **price ≈ 700 + (910 − y) / 60**  (equivalently y ≈ 910 − 60·(price − 700))\\n\\nSanity check: y=190 → 712 ✓; y=550 → 706 ✓.\\n\\n## 2. Main price pane (candlestick area) boundaries\\n- **Top edge:** ~y 150 (just under the header bar)\\n- **Bottom edge:** ~y 1000 (where the volume bars end and the next pane begins)\\n- Contains: candlesticks, the downward black trendline, the blue/red/orange moving averages, the dashed horizontal level near 704, and the volume histogram overlaid at the lower part of this pane (~y 750–1000).\\n\\n## 3. Secondary panes (top → bottom)\\n1. **Price + volume pane** — ~y 150–1000 (described above).\\n2. **Block‑indicator pane** (red/green/orange stacked blocks) — axis **100** at top (~y 1080) and **0** at bottom (~y 1380).\\n3. **Oscillator pane** (red/green bars with dot markers and a flat center line) — axis **0.0000** (~y 1500).\\n4. **Bottom trend/ADX‑style pane** (green vs. red shaded background with two crossing lines) — axis **20.00** visible near the bottom (~y 1750+); pane is cut off by the image edge.\\n\\n## 4. Time axis labels\\n**None visible.** The screenshot is cropped before the bottom time/date axis — the lowest visible content is the 4th indicator pane, not a time ruler. So I cannot give you time‑axis tick values from this image.\\n\\n## 5. UI elements / annotations / text overlays\\n- Top‑left: logo + **\\"Invesco QQQ Trust, Series 1\\"**; a moon (dark‑mode) icon and a wavy‑line icon.\\n- Top‑right: **\\"USD\\"** currency dropdown.\\n- Header price line: **704.69  +0.18 (+0.03%)** in green.\\n- A small **\\"5\\"** dropdown (top‑left of plot, likely an interval/tool selector).\\n- Right axis: purple **\\"Overnight 709.18\\"** tag (near the 710 line) and the green **704.69** last‑price tag.\\n- A **dashed horizontal line** around 704 (prior‑close / reference level) with a small arrow marker on the right.\\n- A **black descending trendline** across the top of the price pane.\\n- **Second image only:** extra **yellow horizontal lines** overlaid across all panes (a measurement/level tool), not present in the first image.\\n\\n## 6. Overall layout summary\\n**Four stacked panes** in a single TradingView‑style chart:\\n1. **Price (candles + MAs + trendline + volume histogram)** — the primary pane, right‑axis scaled 700–712.\\n2. **Block‑type indicator** — 0–100 scale.\\n3. **Oscillator** — centered on 0.0000.\\n4. **Trend/ADX‑type indicator** — 20.00 scale, partially cut off.\\n\\nNo time axis is shown (cropped). The two images are the same chart; the second simply has yellow level lines added.\\n\\n**For your pixel‑to‑price mapping:** use the linear fit `price = 700 + (910 − y)/60` as the starting model, then re‑anchor it to two or three labels you click yourself (e.g., 712.00 and 700.00) to remove my estimation error. If you can tell me the exact image width×height in pixels, I'll recompute the y‑positions more tightly.", "image_count": 2}	f	2026-09-16 23:31:38.976762-04
79	chat-ed0880fd-fdcf-46b9-b6ac-1b9ca7affbf6	step-03	vision_image	{"paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916.jpg", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\focus_scan_01_8x.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\focus_scan_05_8x.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\artifact_suppressed.png"], "prompt": "This is a QQQ candlestick chart. I need you to:\\n1. Describe the lowest visible wick endpoint in the main price pane - where does the lowest wick tip sit relative to the gridlines?\\n2. Are there any thin vertical traces (wicks) that appear to continue through broad same-color candle bodies? Specifically look at the red candle bodies in the lower portion of the price pane - do you see thin darker red lines continuing below the broad red fills?\\n3. What is the approximate price level of the lowest wick tip based on the visible axis labels?\\n4. In the focus crops (images 2 and 3), can you see a thin vertical trace continuing through a broad fill? Describe what you see.\\n5. In the artifact-suppressed view (image 4), does the lowest wick endpoint become clearer or more ambiguous?\\n\\nBe specific about what you see vs. what you infer. Note any uncertainty."}	{"ok": true, "tool": "vision_image", "paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916.jpg", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\focus_scan_01_8x.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\focus_scan_05_8x.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\artifact_suppressed.png"], "answer": "Here's what I can actually see versus what I'm inferring, question by question.\\n\\n**1. Lowest visible wick endpoint in the main price pane**\\nIn the main pane (images 1 and 4), the lowest wick tip I can trace belongs to one of the red candles in the lower‑left cluster. Its tip sits roughly at the **702.00 gridline, or a hair below it** — i.e., between the 702.00 and 700.00 lines but much closer to 702.00. It does not reach the 700.00 line. I'm reading this off the right‑hand axis spacing; I'm not certain of the exact sub‑gridline value.\\n\\n**2. Thin vertical traces continuing through broad same‑color bodies**\\nYes. In the lower portion of the price pane, several red candles show a **thin darker‑red vertical line that runs down through the broad red fill** rather than stopping at the body's lower edge. The same pattern is visible on the teal/green candles (a thin dark‑teal line passing through the broad teal fill). Normally a wick terminates at the body boundary, so a line continuing *through* the fill reads as a rendering/overlay artifact (wick line drawn on top of the body) rather than a true price wick. I'm confident the thin line is present; I'm inferring that it's an artifact rather than a genuine extended wick.\\n\\n**3. Approximate price of the lowest wick tip**\\nBased on the visible axis labels (700.00 / 702.00 / 704.00), the lowest wick tip is approximately **701–702**, i.e., right around the 702.00 gridline and slightly under it. Uncertainty: ±~0.5–1.0, since I'm interpolating between gridlines.\\n\\n**4. Focus crops (images 2 and 3)**\\nBoth crops clearly show the \\"thin line through broad fill\\" pattern:\\n- **Image 2:** left = broad red fill with a thin red vertical line at its top (upper wick); right = broad teal fill with a thin dark‑teal vertical line running from the top, *through* the body, to the bottom.\\n- **Image 3:** broad teal fill with a thin vertical line continuing straight through it top‑to‑bottom; adjacent red fill with a thin red line at its top edge.\\nSo yes — the thin vertical trace visibly continues through the broad same‑color fill in both crops. This is the clearest evidence of the through‑body line.\\n\\n**5. Artifact‑suppressed view (image 4)**\\nImage 4 looks **visually identical to image 1** — same candles, same wicks, same through‑body thin lines. I do not see a meaningful change in the lowest wick endpoint: it is neither clearer nor more ambiguous than in image 1. If image 4 was intended to be a different (suppressed) render, the suppression isn't producing a visible difference in the region I'm examining. Flagging this as uncertainty: I can't confirm image 4 differs from image 1.\\n\\n**Summary of confidence**\\n- High confidence: through‑body thin vertical lines exist (Q2, Q4); lowest wick is near 702 (Q1, Q3).\\n- Lower confidence / uncertain: exact sub‑gridline price of the lowest tip; whether image 4 is genuinely a different view (it appears identical to image 1).\\n\\nIf you want, I can zoom into a specific candle or compare pixel rows between image 1 and image 4 to settle whether the \\"suppressed\\" view actually changed anything.", "image_count": 4}	f	2026-09-16 23:40:39.167478-04
80	chat-ed0880fd-fdcf-46b9-b6ac-1b9ca7affbf6	step-03	vision_image	{"paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916.jpg", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\occlusion_crop_01_zoom4x.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\occlusion_crop_05_zoom4x.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\occlusion_crop_10_zoom4x.png"], "prompt": "I need precise price estimation from this QQQ chart.\\n\\nImage 1 is the full chart. Images 2-4 are 4x zoom crops of specific occlusion regions.\\n\\nFor the FULL CHART (image 1):\\n1. Read the exact price axis labels visible on the right side. List them top to bottom with their approximate y-pixel positions.\\n2. Identify the lowest wick tip in the main price pane. Which candle does it belong to? What gridline is it closest to?\\n3. Is there a wick that extends BELOW the bottom of a broad red candle body? If so, how far below (in terms of gridline spacing)?\\n\\nFor the ZOOM CROPS (images 2-4):\\n4. In each crop, describe exactly what you see: is there a thin vertical line continuing through a broad fill? How far does it extend below the fill's bottom edge?\\n5. Can you estimate the price level of the lowest point in each crop based on the visible context?\\n\\nBe precise. Distinguish what you can see clearly from what you're estimating."}	{"ok": true, "tool": "vision_image", "paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916.jpg", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\occlusion_crop_01_zoom4x.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\occlusion_crop_05_zoom4x.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\occlusion_crop_10_zoom4x.png"], "answer": "Below is what I can read with confidence versus what I'm estimating. I've kept the two separate because the resolution of these crops limits sub‑gridline precision.\\n\\n## Image 1 — full chart\\n\\n**1. Right‑side price axis labels (top → bottom), approximate y‑pixel positions**\\n(Positions are estimates from the rendered image; treat the *labels* as exact, the *pixels* as approximate.)\\n\\n| Label | Approx. y‑px |\\n|---|---|\\n| 712.00 | ~190 |\\n| 710.00 | ~300 |\\n| 708.00 | ~410 |\\n| 706.00 | ~520 |\\n| 704.69 (green \\"last\\" tag) | ~620 |\\n| 704.00 | ~650 |\\n| 702.00 | ~760 |\\n| 700.00 | ~870 |\\n\\nThere's also a purple **Overnight 709.18** tag floating at ~y=330, and the green current‑price tag **704.69** at ~y=620. Gridline spacing ≈ 110 px per 2.00, i.e. ~55 px per 1.00.\\n\\n**2. Lowest wick tip in the main price pane**\\n- It belongs to the **red candle immediately left of the last two teal/green candles** (the one with the long lower shadow in the down‑leg).\\n- Its tip lands **closest to the 704.00 gridline** (just at/above it). I read it as ≈ 704.0–704.3. *Estimate* on the exact value.\\n\\n**3. Wick below a broad red body**\\n- Yes. The broad red candle whose body sits roughly **702.5–704.0** has a lower wick that continues **below its body bottom**, down toward the 704.00 line — i.e. about **half a gridline spacing (~1.00)** below the body's lower edge. *Estimate*; the \\"below the body\\" relationship is clear, the exact distance is not.\\n\\n## Zoom crops 2–4\\n\\n**4. What I see in each**\\n- **Crop 2:** A broad **red** fill (left) and a broad **teal** fill (right). A **thin red vertical line** runs up through the red body (clearly above its top edge); a **thin teal vertical line** runs through the teal body, extending both above and below it. I do **not** see the red wick clearly extending *below* the red body in this crop — it reads as a top‑side wick. The teal wick's lower extension below the teal body is visible but short.\\n- **Crop 3:** Red body (left), teal body (right). A **thin teal vertical line** crosses the teal body, extending above and below it. The red body's top edge aligns with a horizontal reference line; I see no long red lower wick here.\\n- **Crop 4:** This is the **volume histogram**, not the price pane — two red bars of increasing height plus a teal sliver at the right edge. No wick lines here.\\n\\n**5. Price level of the lowest point in each crop**\\n- **Crop 2:** lowest visible point ≈ the bottom of the red/teal bodies, consistent with the **~702–704** band from the full chart. *Estimate.*\\n- **Crop 3:** same band, **~702–704**. *Estimate.*\\n- **Crop 4:** not price‑scalable (volume pane); no price level can be read.\\n\\n## Clear vs. estimated — summary\\n- **Clear:** axis label values and order; that a thin vertical wick line passes through broad candle bodies in crops 2–3; that crop 4 is volume; the identity of the candle with the lowest wick (red, left of the last two green).\\n- **Estimated (resolution‑limited):** exact sub‑gridline price of wick tips (≈704.0–704.3), the precise \\"below‑body\\" distance (~0.5 gridline), and the per‑crop price levels.\\n\\nIf you want, tell me the exact pixel dimensions of the source image and I'll recompute the y‑positions and convert wick‑tip pixels to price using the 700.00/712.00 anchors for a tighter number.", "image_count": 4}	f	2026-09-16 23:43:17.489875-04
81	chat-ed0880fd-fdcf-46b9-b6ac-1b9ca7affbf6	step-03	vision_image	{"paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916.jpg", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\occlusion_overlay.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\03_color_traces.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\04_vertical.png"], "prompt": "Final perception validation for a QQQ chart. I need you to answer three specific questions:\\n\\n1. THIN TRACE THROUGH FILL: In the main price pane, do you see any thin vertical lines (wicks) that genuinely continue THROUGH broad same-color candle bodies? Look at the red candles in the lower portion. Is the thin line the same color as the broad fill, or a different shade? Does it extend below the fill's bottom edge, or is it contained within the fill?\\n\\n2. INTRADAY LOW: What is the lowest price level visible in the main price pane? Read the axis labels carefully. Is the lowest point at the bottom of a candle body, or at the tip of a wick that extends below the body? Give your best estimate of the price.\\n\\n3. NAIVE vs. OCCLUSION-AWARE: If you only looked at the broad candle bodies (ignoring thin lines), what would you estimate the intraday low to be? Does the presence of thin traces through the fills change that estimate?\\n\\nBe precise. State your confidence level for each answer."}	{"ok": true, "tool": "vision_image", "paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916.jpg", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\occlusion_overlay.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\03_color_traces.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\04_vertical.png"], "answer": "Here is my perception read of the main price pane (the four screenshots show the same price pane; only the second has selection rectangles, and those sit in the *volume* pane, so they don't affect the price reading).\\n\\n**1. Thin trace through fill — YES, same color, extends beyond the body.**\\nIn the lower cluster of red (bearish) candles I can see thin vertical red lines that are the *same* red hue as the broad candle bodies — not a different shade. These thin lines are the high‑low wicks: they run from the candle's high down through the body region and out the bottom, so they are not contained within the fill. They clearly extend **below** the bottom edge of the broad red bodies (and above the top edge). So the \\"thin line through the fill\\" is real, monochromatic with the body, and protrudes past both ends.\\n*Confidence: High (~85–90%) that the wicks are same‑colored and extend beyond the body edges. I cannot be 100% certain of exact pixel alignment at this resolution, but the protrusion below the body is unambiguous.*\\n\\n**2. Intraday low — at a wick tip, not a body bottom; ≈ 702.0–702.5.**\\nReading the right‑hand axis (700.00 / 702.00 / 704.00 …), the lowest visible point in the price pane is the **tip of a lower wick** on one of the red candles, not the bottom of a broad body. That wick tip sits just at / slightly above the 702.00 gridline. My best estimate of the intraday low is **~702.0–702.5**. The broad red bodies' bottoms are a touch higher (~702.5–703.0).\\n*Confidence: Medium (~60–70%) on the \\"wick tip is the low\\" conclusion; Low‑Medium (~50%) on the precise number, since I'm interpolating between the 700 and 702 gridlines from a screenshot, not from OHLC data. Treat 702.0–702.5 as a visual estimate, not a quote.*\\n\\n**3. Naive (bodies‑only) vs. occlusion‑aware — yes, the thin traces lower the estimate.**\\nIf I ignored all thin lines and used only the broad candle bodies, the lowest body bottom reads around **~702.5–703.0**. Accounting for the wicks (the thin traces that pass through/extend past the fills) pulls the estimated low down to **~702.0–702.5**. So the thin traces do change the estimate, by roughly **0.3–0.5** of a point, in the downward direction.\\n*Confidence: Medium‑High (~75%) that the wicks shift the low lower than the body‑only read; the magnitude of the shift is a rough visual estimate.*\\n\\n**Caveat:** This is a visual read of a rendered chart image, not a parse of the underlying OHLC series. For an exact intraday low you should pull the actual low value from the data feed; my figures are perception estimates with the confidence levels stated above.", "image_count": 4}	f	2026-09-16 23:47:17.839039-04
82	chat-ed0880fd-fdcf-46b9-b6ac-1b9ca7affbf6	step-04	vision_image	{"paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916.jpg", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\artifact_suppressed.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\reconstruction.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\focus_scan_01_8x.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\focus_scan_02_8x.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\focus_scan_05_8x.png"], "prompt": "These are six views of the same QQQ chart: image 1 is the original screenshot; image 2 is an artifact-suppressed derived view; image 3 is a pixel-faithful reconstruction; images 4-6 are 8x focus crops around geometric occlusion candidates. The geometric analyzer reports the primary price pane as y=154 to y=887, with visible price axis approximately 712.00 at top and 700.00 at bottom, giving about 61.08 pixels per 1.00 price unit. It detected thin vertical traces continuing through broad same-color fills, with the lowest reported endpoints near: candidate 1 red x=552 y_end=836, candidate 2 red x=510 y_end=833, and candidate 10 red x=232 y_end=840. Please inspect all views and report: 1) the lowest visible wick endpoint in the main price pane, including candle color/position if identifiable; 2) whether any thin trace genuinely continues through a broad same-color fill, especially in the focus crops; 3) the approximate price of the lowest visible wick endpoint using the visible axis; 4) whether the artifact-suppressed, reconstruction, or focus-crop views change the read compared with the original; 5) explicitly state whether you agree or disagree with the geometric analyzer's claim that the lowest wick endpoints are near y=833-840 and therefore near 700.7-700.9, or whether the visible low appears closer to 702 or another level. Do not assume a hidden wick exists; report only what is visible and distinguish clear evidence from inference."}	{"ok": true, "tool": "vision_image", "paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916.jpg", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\artifact_suppressed.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\reconstruction.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\focus_scan_01_8x.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\focus_scan_02_8x.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260916-232722-2a0a3ca9-QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916-light\\\\focus_scan_05_8x.png"], "answer": "I inspected all six views (original, artifact‑suppressed, pixel‑faithful reconstruction, and the three 8× focus crops) and read the price pane against the visible axis (712.00 top → 700.00 bottom). Findings, with clear evidence separated from inference:\\n\\n**1) Lowest visible wick endpoint in the main price pane.**\\nThe lowest wick I can actually see is the long lower wick of a **red (bearish) candle** in the right‑center of the pane (roughly the 4th–5th candle from the right edge), with a comparable **teal/green lower wick** on the candle immediately to its right reaching a similar depth. Both tips stop at about the **702.00 gridline** (a touch below it at most). I do not see any wick tip extending materially below that level in any view.\\n\\n**2) Thin trace through a broad same‑color fill.**\\nYes — in the focus crops a thin same‑color vertical line runs down through the broad body fill (e.g. the red vertical line over the red body in crop 4, the teal vertical line over the teal body in crop 6). However, this is just the **wick line of the same candle drawn on top of its body**, i.e. normal chart rendering. It is *not* evidence of a separate, hidden wick continuing deeper behind the fill. I treat this as a rendering artifact, not a real occluded wick.\\n\\n**3) Approximate price of the lowest visible wick.**\\nUsing the visible axis, the lowest wick tip sits at roughly **701.5–702.0** (at/just below the 702.00 line). I would not place it below ~701.5 on the evidence I can see.\\n\\n**4) Do the derived/reconstruction/crop views change the read?**\\nNo. The artifact‑suppressed view, the pixel‑faithful reconstruction, and the 8× crops all show the **same** wick tips as the original. The crops only magnify the wick‑over‑body rendering noted in (2); they do not reveal a lower endpoint than the original screenshot. So the read is unchanged across views.\\n\\n**5) Agreement with the geometric analyzer.**\\nI **disagree** with the analyzer's conclusion. Its reported endpoints (y≈833–840) map to about **700.7–700.9**, which is very close to the 700.00 axis line. I do not see any wick reaching that low in any of the six views; the visible low is clearly higher, near **702**. The analyzer's y≈833–840 values most likely correspond to the **bottom edge of a body fill / the lower boundary region of the price pane**, not to a true wick tip. On the visible evidence the lowest wick is closer to **702**, not 700.7–700.9.\\n\\n**Summary:** Lowest visible wick ≈ a red candle's lower wick (with a matching teal wick beside it) ending near **702**; thin same‑color traces through fills are normal wick‑over‑body rendering, not hidden wicks; the derived and crop views confirm rather than alter this; and I do **not** accept the analyzer's 700.7–700.9 figure — the visible low is closer to **702**. I am reporting only what is visible and flagging the 700.7–700.9 value as inconsistent with the chart as shown.", "image_count": 6}	f	2026-09-16 23:52:56.415926-04
