110	chat-1d9e33f3-cab0-44f3-8f7b-3cf32241dcf1	step-03	vision_image	{"paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916.jpg"], "prompt": "This is a QQQ stock chart. I need you to identify ALL visible price axis labels on the right side (or left side) of the chart. For each visible numeric price label, report:\\n1. The exact price value shown (e.g., 710.00, 708.00, 706.00, 704.00, 702.00, 700.00)\\n2. Its approximate vertical position (y-coordinate in pixels from the top of the image)\\n3. Whether it appears to be a gridline label or a price tag/annotation\\n\\nAlso identify:\\n- The \\"Overnight\\" price line (should be around 709.18) and its y position\\n- The current price line (should be around 704.69) and its y position\\n- The top and bottom boundaries of the main price pane\\n- Any other visible horizontal reference lines\\n\\nBe precise about which labels are explicitly visible as text vs. which are just gridlines without labels."}	{"ok": true, "tool": "vision_image", "paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\QQQ_followup_hidden_wick_test_20260916.jpg"], "answer": "Here's a precise read of the right‑hand price axis and the reference lines in the main price pane. Pixel y‑coordinates are visual estimates from the top edge of the image (image is ~1240 × 1456 px); treat them as ±10 px.\\n\\n### Main price pane — axis labels (right side)\\nAll of these are **gridline labels** (plain text aligned to faint horizontal gridlines), not tags:\\n\\n| Label | Approx. y (px) | Type |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 712.00 | ~165 | gridline label |\\n| 710.00 | ~265 | gridline label |\\n| 708.00 | ~365 | gridline label |\\n| 706.00 | ~465 | gridline label |\\n| 704.00 | ~565 | gridline label |\\n| 702.00 | ~665 | gridline label |\\n| 700.00 | ~765 | gridline label |\\n\\nSpacing is even (~100 px per 2.00), confirming a linear scale.\\n\\n### Price tags / annotations (colored boxes on the right)\\nThese are **price tags**, not gridline labels:\\n\\n- **Overnight 709.18** — purple/magenta box, center ≈ **y 290–305 px** (sits between the 710.00 and 708.00 gridlines, closer to 710).\\n- **704.69** — teal/green box, center ≈ **y 500–515 px** (sits between the 706.00 and 704.00 gridlines, closer to 704). This is the *current price* tag.\\n\\n### Reference lines in the main pane\\n- **Overnight line (709.18):** dotted horizontal line at ≈ y 290–305 px, matching the purple tag.\\n- **Current price line (704.69):** dotted horizontal line at ≈ y 500–515 px, matching the teal tag.\\n- **Dashed black line** at ≈ y 565 px (the 704.00 level) — a separate manual/reference dashed line, distinct from the dotted current‑price line.\\n- Faint solid gridlines at each of the 700–712 levels listed above.\\n\\n### Main price pane boundaries\\n- **Top boundary:** ≈ y 110–130 px (just below the \\"Invesco QQQ Trust, Series 1 / 704.69 +0.18\\" header block).\\n- **Bottom boundary:** ≈ y 820–850 px (where the volume histogram ends and the next oscillator pane begins).\\n\\n### Other panes (for completeness, not part of the price axis)\\n- Oscillator pane labels: **100** (≈ y 880 px) and **0** (≈ y 1110 px).\\n- Next pane label: **0.0000** (≈ y 1190 px).\\n- Bottom pane label: **20.00** (≈ y 1410 px).\\n\\n### Notes / caveats\\n- The only *text* price labels in the main pane are the seven gridline values (700.00–712.00) plus the two colored tags (709.18 Overnight, 704.69 current). There are no additional unlabeled gridlines in the main pane beyond those seven.\\n- The \\"Overnight\\" and \\"704.69\\" values appear **twice**: once as a colored tag on the right axis and once as a dotted reference line across the chart — they are the same price, not separate levels.\\n- Pixel positions are estimates from visual inspection of the screenshot; if you need exact pixel values for automation, I can run a quick image analysis pass to measure them precisely.\\n\\nWant me to measure the exact pixel coordinates programmatically, or is this level of precision enough for what you're doing with the chart?", "image_count": 1}	f	2026-09-17 04:02:56.277682-04
111	chat-1d9e33f3-cab0-44f3-8f7b-3cf32241dcf1	step-04	read_file	{"path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\docs\\\\CHART_VISION_CHEATSHEET.md"}	{"ok": true, "path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\docs\\\\CHART_VISION_CHEATSHEET.md", "size": 3525, "tool": "read_file", "sha256": "f1a2c9f4aac86f859ecc8a412a6ad3d6937fc5f7fcfac253d589306d27970bf6", "content": "CHART VISION CHEAT SHEET ??? layered/occlusion-aware price reading\\n\\n1. PRICE AXIS: Never infer price from pane top/bottom. Anchor only to visible labeled prices/lines. For this QQQ image, sanity anchors are approximately Overnight 709.18 at y???297 and current price 704.69 at y???514. Refine those y positions from pixels if possible. The resulting linear mapping must also agree with the visible 710/708/706/704/702/700 labels; reject any mapping that does not.\\n\\n2. CONSTANT VS DATA: Grid/pane geometry is reference. Candles, wicks, volume bars, moving averages and indicators are data. Do not treat a volume bar as background/reference.\\n\\n3. OBJECT LAYERS: A chart is a composite of overlapping objects. Keep separate object hypotheses for candle body, wick, volume bar, MA/indicator line, gridline, annotation/UI. Inferred z-order is render order, not physical depth.\\n\\n4. OCCLUSION: Broad mostly-uniform rectangles are likely fills. Thin vertically-continuous same-color traces are likely wicks/lines. If a thin trace reaches a broad fill, trace the literal pixel/color continuity through the fill until it stops. Use local darkness, narrow width, vertical continuity, edge orientation, color-family consistency and overlap geometry together.\\n\\n5. NORMAL WICK-OVER-BODY VS HIDDEN WICK: A wick passing through its OWN candle body is normal and not the interesting case. The important case is a trace that continues beyond the candle body into/through an INDEPENDENT broad volume-bar/fill region. Do not dismiss the latter merely because normal wick-over-body rendering exists.\\n\\n6. LOW-CONFIDENCE REGIONS: Do not force a conclusion. But once a region is suspicious, rescan it aggressively: crop, 4x/8x nearest-neighbor zoom, contrast/gamma/saturation variants, multiplicative feature score, neighboring-column comparison, continuity tracing, and original-image recheck. Promotion requires cross-view convergence.\\n\\n7. MULTIPLICATIVE TRACE EVIDENCE: Prefer trace_strength ??? color_family ?? local_darkness ?? thinness ?? vertical_continuity ?? edge_verticality. Occlusion confidence additionally multiplies overlap_with_fill ?? same_pane ?? z-consistency. A weak channel should lower the score rather than be hidden by averaging.\\n\\n8. DISAGREEMENT RULE: A semantic vision model may disagree with pixel geometry. Do NOT average the two into a compromise price. Investigate the disputed region until it is CONFIRMED, REJECTED, or explicitly UNRESOLVED. Geometry is not automatically right; vision is not automatically right.\\n\\n9. CANDIDATE AUDIT: The deep red candidates around x???510???552 and y???833???840 in this QQQ image are AUDIT TARGETS, not facts. Re-examine them from the original pixels. Determine whether each is (a) actual thin trace/wick continuation, (b) broad-fill/body edge, (c) compression/aliasing artifact, or (d) unresolved.\\n\\n10. PRICE CONVERSION COMES LAST: First determine the true endpoint geometry. Only then convert y???price using independently verified labeled-axis anchors. Report the anchor coordinates, fitted mapping, residuals against other visible labels, endpoint y, price, and uncertainty.\\n\\n11. REDRAW TEST: The decomposition should be able to plausibly redraw/reconstruct the relevant local chart region. If the proposed object/layer model cannot reproduce the original pixels, treat the interpretation as suspect.\\n\\n12. NO HINDSIGHT TARGETING: Do not search for a specific low or force sub-700/sub-702. Follow the pixels. The goal is accurate perception, not agreement with a desired answer.\\n", "end_line": 25, "start_line": 1, "total_lines": 25}	f	2026-09-17 04:07:40.009119-04
