1549	chat-c467de3f-d486-460c-8ddc-774ee34440cb	step-01	read_file	{"path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\cors-dummy\\\\backend\\\\tests\\\\test_loader.py"}	{"ok": true, "path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\cors-dummy\\\\backend\\\\tests\\\\test_loader.py", "size": 5975, "tool": "read_file", "sha256": "b4b69b7b1eb865d7bffd7453cc30d7bcf704f57c7531f7e215f67f4f94e591c6", "content": "\\"\\"\\"Tests for the drop-in endpoint discovery loader (``app.endpoints.loader``).\\n\\nThese tests exercise the loader's contract in isolation, using temporary\\nendpoint modules created in pytest's ``tmp_path`` directory. The\\n``endpoint_module`` fixture (see ``backend/conftest.py``) makes those temp\\nmodules importable through the real ``app.endpoints`` package, which is how\\n``discover_endpoints`` resolves them by dotted name.\\n\\nNo database, network, or long-lived processes are involved.\\n\\"\\"\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\nfrom app.endpoints.loader import (\\n    DiscoveredEndpoint,\\n    EndpointDiscoveryError,\\n    discover_endpoints,\\n)\\n\\n\\n# --- (1) Discovery of two valid modules, sorted by name ---------------------\\ndef test_discovery_two_valid_sorted(endpoint_module):\\n    endpoint_module.make(\\n        \\"alpha\\",\\n        \\"from fastapi import APIRouter\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"router = APIRouter()\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"@router.get('/a')\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"def a():\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"    return {'m': 'alpha'}\\\\n\\",\\n    )\\n    endpoint_module.make(\\n        \\"beta\\",\\n        \\"from fastapi import APIRouter\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"router = APIRouter()\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"@router.post('/b')\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"def b():\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"    return {'m': 'beta'}\\\\n\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    result = discover_endpoints(endpoint_module.path)\\n\\n    assert [ep.module_name for ep in result] == [\\"alpha\\", \\"beta\\"]\\n    assert all(isinstance(ep, DiscoveredEndpoint) for ep in result)\\n    # Route extraction is correct for each module.\\n    by_name = {ep.module_name: ep.routes for ep in result}\\n    assert by_name[\\"alpha\\"] == [(\\"GET\\", \\"/a\\")]\\n    assert by_name[\\"beta\\"] == [(\\"POST\\", \\"/b\\")]\\n\\n\\n# --- (2) Module missing the router attribute --------------------------------\\ndef test_missing_router_raises(endpoint_module):\\n    endpoint_module.make(\\"norouter\\", \\"VALUE = 1\\\\n\\")  # no `router` attribute\\n\\n    with pytest.raises(EndpointDiscoveryError) as excinfo:\\n        discover_endpoints(endpoint_module.path)\\n\\n    assert \\"norouter\\" in str(excinfo.value)\\n    assert \\"router\\" in str(excinfo.value)\\n\\n\\n# --- (3) Module whose router is not an APIRouter ----------------------------\\ndef test_wrong_router_type_raises(endpoint_module):\\n    endpoint_module.make(\\"badtype\\", \\"router = 'not a router'\\\\n\\")\\n\\n    with pytest.raises(EndpointDiscoveryError) as excinfo:\\n        discover_endpoints(endpoint_module.path)\\n\\n    assert \\"badtype\\" in str(excinfo.value)\\n    assert \\"APIRouter\\" in str(excinfo.value)\\n\\n\\n# --- (4) Duplicate (method, path) across two modules ------------------------\\ndef test_duplicate_route_raises(endpoint_module):\\n    endpoint_module.make(\\n        \\"alpha\\",\\n        \\"from fastapi import APIRouter\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"router = APIRouter()\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"@router.get('/dup')\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"def a():\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"    return 'alpha'\\\\n\\",\\n    )\\n    endpoint_module.make(\\n        \\"beta\\",\\n        \\"from fastapi import APIRouter\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"router = APIRouter()\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"@router.get('/dup')\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"def b():\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"    return 'beta'\\\\n\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    with pytest.raises(EndpointDiscoveryError) as excinfo:\\n        discover_endpoints(endpoint_module.path)\\n\\n    msg = str(excinfo.value)\\n    assert \\"alpha\\" in msg\\n    assert \\"beta\\" in msg\\n    assert \\"/dup\\" in msg\\n\\n\\n# --- (5) Mount / WebSocket routes (methods=None) are skipped ----------------\\ndef test_mount_and_websocket_skipped(endpoint_module):\\n    endpoint_module.make(\\n        \\"mixed\\",\\n        \\"from fastapi import APIRouter\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"router = APIRouter()\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"@router.get('/ok')\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"def ok():\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"    return {'ok': True}\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"@router.websocket('/ws')\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"async def ws(websocket):\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"    pass\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"def _sub_app(scope, receive, send):\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"    pass\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"router.mount('/sub', _sub_app)\\\\n\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    result = discover_endpoints(endpoint_module.path)\\n\\n    assert [ep.module_name for ep in result] == [\\"mixed\\"]\\n    routes = result[0].routes\\n    # The normal HTTP route is present...\\n    assert (\\"GET\\", \\"/ok\\") in routes\\n    # ...but the WebSocket and Mount routes (methods is None) are excluded.\\n    assert all(path != \\"/ws\\" for _, path in routes)\\n    assert all(path != \\"/sub\\" for _, path in routes)\\n\\n\\n# --- (6) Missing directory raises -------------------------------------------\\ndef test_missing_directory_raises(tmp_path):\\n    missing = tmp_path / \\"does_not_exist\\"\\n    with pytest.raises(EndpointDiscoveryError) as excinfo:\\n        discover_endpoints(missing)\\n    assert str(missing) in str(excinfo.value)\\n\\n\\n# --- (7) Underscore-prefixed and __init__.py files are skipped --------------\\ndef test_underscore_and_init_skipped(endpoint_module):\\n    # A valid module that SHOULD be discovered.\\n    endpoint_module.make(\\n        \\"alpha\\",\\n        \\"from fastapi import APIRouter\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"router = APIRouter()\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"@router.get('/a')\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"def a():\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"    return 'alpha'\\\\n\\",\\n    )\\n    # A valid module that must be SKIPPED because its name starts with '_'.\\n    endpoint_module.make(\\n        \\"_private\\",\\n        \\"from fastapi import APIRouter\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"router = APIRouter()\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"@router.get('/p')\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"def p():\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"    return 'private'\\\\n\\",\\n    )\\n    # An __init__.py that must be SKIPPED.\\n    (endpoint_module.path / \\"__init__.py\\").write_text(\\n        \\"from fastapi import APIRouter\\\\n\\"\\n        \\"router = APIRouter()\\\\n\\",\\n        encoding=\\"utf-8\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    result = discover_endpoints(endpoint_module.path)\\n\\n    assert [ep.module_name for ep in result] == [\\"alpha\\"]\\n\\n\\n# --- (8) Import failure in a module raises loudly ---------------------------\\ndef test_import_failure_raises(endpoint_module):\\n    # Write the module to disk but do NOT register it in sys.modules, so the\\n    # import mechanism cannot find it and raises ModuleNotFoundError.\\n    endpoint_module.make(\\"broken\\", \\"raise RuntimeError('boom')\\\\n\\", register=False)\\n\\n    with pytest.raises(EndpointDiscoveryError) as excinfo:\\n        discover_endpoints(endpoint_module.path)\\n\\n    assert \\"broken\\" in str(excinfo.value)\\n", "end_line": 181, "start_line": 1, "total_lines": 181}	f	2026-09-19 16:17:37.132276-04
1674	chat-f70ef80b-5387-422a-83da-fe212221217a	step-05	write_file	{"path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\boost-python-sql\\\\README.md", "content": "# boost-python-sql\\n\\nA personal financial-data acquisition and storage system that crawls daily and 1-minute intraday stock/index OHLCV price data from the **Financial Modeling Prep (FMP) REST API**, stores it in **PostgreSQL** databases (using partitioned table structures), and migrates/partitions existing data between PostgreSQL instances.\\n\\nThe system is designed for a single developer's local/remote data infrastructure, connecting across a **Tailscale** network to multiple PostgreSQL instances and a MongoDB credential store.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Technology Stack\\n\\n| Category | Technology |\\n|----------|-----------|\\n| Language | Python 3.13 |\\n| DB driver (ODBC) | `turbodbc` |\\n| DB driver (native) | `psycopg` (v3), `psycopg2` |\\n| HTTP client | `httpx` (sync + async) |\\n| Data manipulation | `pandas`, `numpy` |\\n| MongoDB access | `pymongo` (via `kh_data.mong_access`) |\\n| Holiday calendar | `holidays` |\\n| Console output | `rich`, custom ANSI loggers |\\n| Async I/O | `asyncio`, `concurrent.futures` |\\n| Environment | Conda (`D:\\\\Pythons\\\\Conda`, env `base`) |\\n| Network | Tailscale (`.ts.net` hostnames) |\\n| API source | Financial Modeling Prep (FMP) REST API |\\n| Databases | PostgreSQL (multiple instances), MongoDB (credential store) |\\n\\n### External Local Packages (not in this repo)\\n\\nThese packages are imported but not versioned or present in this directory:\\n\\n- `kh_network.connect_help` — builds ODBC connection strings\\n- `kh_data.mong_access` — MongoDB credential store access\\n- `kh_data.strings_theory` — string utilities (e.g., `shorterns`)\\n- `kh_output.color_logs` — colored logging formatter\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Repository Structure\\n\\n```\\nboost-python-sql/\\n├── credentials.py              # Central credential/connection definitions (MongoDB-backed)\\n├── main.py                     # Primary entry point — DB copy/partition pipeline\\n├── move_and_partition_db.py    # 9-line stub re-exporting pipeline helpers\\n├── run_main.ps1                # PowerShell launcher (Conda activate → python main.py)\\n├── stat_functions.py           # SQL query generators for DB inspection\\n├── finmo_crawl/                # Daily OHLCV crawl from FMP API\\n│   ├── zz_main.py              #   Entry point (async driver)\\n│   ├── function_batch_get.py   #   Sync batch processor (active path)\\n│   ├── async_batch_get.py      #   Alternate async variant (experimental)\\n│   ├── init_variables.py       #   Config: iterations, batch size, DB connections\\n│   ├── custom_pool.py          #   Queue-based turbodbc connection pool\\n│   ├── batch_verify_helpers.py #   verify_table, batch_generator\\n│   ├── get_n_random_ticker_helper.py  # Random ticker selection\\n│   ├── to_copy_db.py           #   pg_dump/psql copy helper (standalone)\\n│   ├── vv_intraday_begin.py    #   1-min URL builder + connection test (WIP)\\n│   ├── _xx_index_get.py        #   Hardcoded index URLs (scratch)\\n│   ├── _xx_try_new_part.py     #   psycopg partition helper (experiment)\\n│   └── PART_queue_queue.py     #   Producer/consumer queue scaffold (experiment)\\n├── pipeline_update_tickers/    # 3-step intraday index (^IXIC) pipeline\\n│   ├── step_ff_main.py         #   Entry point for the 3-step flow\\n│   ├── step_01_fetch.py        #   Async httpx fetch with retry + 429 handling\\n│   ├── step_02_iterate_variables.py  # Date generation (holidays-aware), batch split\\n│   ├── step_03_insert_to_db.py #   Queue consumer → DB writer thread\\n│   ├── shared_queue.py         #   data_queue = queue.Queue()\\n│   ├── help_connect.py         #   turbodbc connections + partition helpers\\n│   ├── porting_3step.py        #   JSONB → column transform (standalone)\\n│   └── step01-init.py          #   5-line import stub\\n├── restart_update_tickers/     # Alternate/restart intraday pipeline (newer)\\n│   ├── main.py                 #   Entry point: per-ticker intraday crawl with resume\\n│   ├── step_03_insert_to_db.py #   DB insert (adds url column)\\n│   ├── gen_var.py              #   Globals: date range, iterations, URL templates\\n│   ├── geta_ticker.py          #   Random tickers from company_info\\n│   ├── dates_from_db.py        #   Fetch distinct dates (resume/skip logic)\\n│   ├── color_logs.py           #   Local ANSI color-logging formatter\\n│   ├── cleanup.py              #   Insert + delete-empty helper (standalone)\\n│   ├── ticker_trans.py         #   Column value-replacement helper (standalone)\\n│   └── async_try.py            #   Async fetch experiment\\n├── .idea/                      # JetBrains IDE configuration\\n└── __pycache__/                # Python 3.13 bytecode\\n```\\n\\n### How the Pieces Relate\\n\\n- **Root `main.py`** is a standalone migration utility: it copies existing 1-minute tables from a source PostgreSQL DB into year/month-partitioned replicas in a destination DB. It does not fetch from the FMP API.\\n- **`finmo_crawl/`** creates *new* daily data from the FMP API and writes `{ticker}_daily` tables.\\n- **`pipeline_update_tickers/`** fetches 1-minute intraday data for a specific index (^IXIC) and stores raw JSONB responses.\\n- **`restart_update_tickers/`** is a reworked intraday pipeline that fetches 1-minute data per-ticker with resume support (skips already-filled dates) and adaptive throttling. It appears to be the **newer iteration** of the intraday workflow.\\n- **`credentials.py`** (root) is imported by `finmo_crawl/get_n_random_ticker_helper.py` and `finmo_crawl/vv_intraday_begin.py`. It pulls all secrets from MongoDB at import time and creates two live `turbodbc` connections as module-level globals.\\n- **`move_and_partition_db.py`** star-imports from `pipeline_update_tickers.help_connect` — appears to be an early or superseded entry point.\\n- **`stat_functions.py`** provides two SQL query-builder helpers for inspecting partitioned tables and recently created objects. It is not imported by any other file in the repo.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Entry Points\\n\\n| Entry Point | How to Run | Purpose |\\n|-------------|-----------|---------|\\n| `main.py` (root) | `run_main.ps1` or `python main.py` | Copy/partition random 1-minute tables from source → destination DB (1000 iterations, 10 threads) |\\n| `finmo_crawl/zz_main.py` | `python zz_main.py` (from `finmo_crawl/`) | Daily OHLCV crawl for 1250 random tickers in batches of 8 |\\n| `pipeline_update_tickers/step_ff_main.py` | `python step_ff_main.py` (from that dir) | 3-step intraday index (^IXIC) fetch → queue → DB write, 6-month date intervals |\\n| `restart_update_tickers/main.py` | `python main.py` (from that dir) | Per-ticker intraday crawl with resume, adaptive throttling, 255 random tickers |\\n\\nNo CLI framework (argparse, click, typer) is used. All entry points are plain `python script.py` invocations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Current Progress / State\\n\\n### Implemented / Working-Looking\\n\\nComponents with complete logic, real DB connections, and no placeholder configs:\\n\\n- **Root `main.py`** — Full partition-copy pipeline: connect → check table → create year/month partitions → fetch → insert.\\n- **`finmo_crawl/zz_main.py` + `function_batch_get.py`** — Complete async driver + sync batch processor with real FMP endpoint, DB writes, connection pool, and table-existence check.\\n- **`finmo_crawl/init_variables.py`** — Real config pulling API key + DB connection from MongoDB at import.\\n- **`pipeline_update_tickers/step_ff_main.py` + 3 steps** — Complete flow: async fetch with retry/429 handling → date generation (holidays-aware) → queue → DB writer thread.\\n- **`restart_update_tickers/main.py`** — Most complete intraday pipeline: resume logic (skip filled dates), per-ticker tables, adaptive wait, NYSE holiday awareness.\\n\\n### Experimental / Alternate Versions\\n\\nFiles with placeholder configs, simulated logic, or alternate I/O models:\\n\\n- `finmo_crawl/async_batch_get.py` — Alternate async variant of `function_batch_get.py` (not imported by `zz_main.py`).\\n- `finmo_crawl/PART_queue_queue.py` — Producer/consumer queue scaffold with placeholder API URL and simulated DB functions.\\n- `finmo_crawl/_xx_index_get.py` — Hardcoded FMP URLs for 4 indices (scratch file).\\n- `finmo_crawl/_xx_try_new_part.py` — `psycopg` partition-creation helper with placeholder config.\\n- `finmo_crawl/vv_intraday_begin.py` — 1-min URL builder + `SELECT 42` connection test.\\n- `finmo_crawl/to_copy_db.py` — `pg_dump`/`psql` copy helper with placeholder configs.\\n- `pipeline_update_tickers/porting_3step.py` — 3-step data reshaping with placeholder config.\\n- `pipeline_update_tickers/step01-init.py` — 5-line import stub.\\n- `restart_update_tickers/cleanup.py` — Insert + delete-empty helper with placeholder config.\\n- `restart_update_tickers/ticker_trans.py` — Column value-replacement helper with placeholder config.\\n- `restart_update_tickers/async_try.py` — Async fetch experiment with placeholder API URL.\\n\\n### Incomplete / Missing\\n\\n- **No dependency management** — No `requirements.txt`, `setup.py`, `pyproject.toml`, or `environment.yml`.\\n- **No tests** — Zero test files in any directory.\\n- **No `__init__.py`** — Subdirectories are flat script packages (top-level imports, not package-qualified).\\n- **Not a Git repository** — No `.git` directory, no `.gitignore`.\\n- **External local packages undocumented** — `kh_network`, `kh_data`, `kh_output` are imported but not present in this repo.\\n- **Hardcoded secrets in multiple files** — `credentials.py` (MongoDB-backed), `pipeline_update_tickers/help_connect.py` (inline DB password), `finmo_crawl/_xx_index_get.py` (inline API key). No `.env` or secret manager.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Ambiguities / Unclear Areas\\n\\n1. **Which intraday pipeline is \\"current\\"?** `pipeline_update_tickers` and `restart_update_tickers` implement the same workflow (fetch 1-min data → store in PostgreSQL). `restart_update_tickers` has resume logic, per-ticker tables, and adaptive throttling — suggesting it is the newer iteration. However, no file explicitly deprecates the other.\\n\\n2. **Root `main.py` vs. subdirectory pipelines:** The root `main.py` copies *existing* 1-minute tables between databases (a migration utility), while the subdirectories *create* new data from the FMP API. The relationship (which runs first, which is the \\"production\\" flow) is not documented.\\n\\n3. **`stat_functions.py`:** No file imports it. It may be a manual ops utility run ad-hoc, or it may be dead code.\\n\\n4. **Project name \\"boost-python-sql\\":** Does not clearly indicate the financial-data purpose. The name may refer to an earlier iteration or a different scope.\\n\\n5. **MongoDB as credential store:** The system depends on a MongoDB instance for all credentials and API keys. If that instance is unavailable, no script can run. This is a single point of failure not documented anywhere.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Running the Project\\n\\n1. Ensure the Conda environment is available at `D:\\\\Pythons\\\\Conda` (env `base`).\\n2. Ensure the external local packages (`kh_network`, `kh_data`, `kh_output`) are importable (installed or on `PYTHONPATH`).\\n3. Ensure the MongoDB credential store is reachable.\\n4. Ensure the target PostgreSQL instances are reachable over Tailscale.\\n5. Run the desired entry point:\\n   ```powershell\\n   # Root partition-copy pipeline\\n   .\\\\run_main.ps1\\n\\n   # Daily crawl\\n   cd finmo_crawl\\n   python zz_main.py\\n\\n   # Intraday index pipeline\\n   cd pipeline_update_tickers\\n   python step_ff_main.py\\n\\n   # Intraday per-ticker pipeline (newer)\\n   cd restart_update_tickers\\n   python main.py\\n   ```\\n\\n> **Note:** No `requirements.txt` exists. Install dependencies manually or reconstruct from the imports listed above.\\n\\n---\\n\\n*This README was generated from inspection of the repository contents on 2026-09-20. It reflects the state of the code at that time.*\\n"}	{"ok": true, "path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\boost-python-sql\\\\README.md", "tool": "write_file", "bytes": 11904, "sha256": "2e8090ab73b711de0eb0b949413bcd816bf567bf5b7e2b491b7f439a0631cb90", "created": true}	f	2026-09-19 20:49:19.711215-04
