1420	chat-44b0e0ba-0234-4891-9ba8-59e33431b4c2	step-02	read_file	{"path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\cors-dummy\\\\backend\\\\conftest.py"}	{"ok": true, "path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\cors-dummy\\\\backend\\\\conftest.py", "size": 3783, "tool": "read_file", "sha256": "4f1598cf1841e668a43ef1ed16710454ea6dd86a9deb31af41ab8e3688effb65", "content": "\\"\\"\\"Pytest configuration for the backend test suite.\\n\\nTwo responsibilities:\\n\\n1. Put the ``backend/`` directory on ``sys.path`` so the ``app`` package (and\\n   therefore ``app.endpoints.loader``) is importable regardless of the\\n   directory pytest is invoked from.\\n2. Provide the :func:`endpoint_module` fixture, which creates temporary\\n   endpoint modules that are importable through the real ``app.endpoints``\\n   package.\\n\\nWhy the fixture is needed\\n-------------------------\\n``discover_endpoints`` imports candidate modules by their dotted name\\n``app.endpoints.<stem>`` (see ``loader.py``). A plain ``tmp_path`` file is not\\nreachable by that dotted name through the normal import mechanism, so the\\nfixture pre-registers each temp module in ``sys.modules`` using\\n``importlib.util.spec_from_file_location``. When the loader later calls\\n``importlib.import_module(\\"app.endpoints.<stem>\\")``, Python finds the module\\nalready in ``sys.modules`` and returns it directly.\\n\\nFor the import-failure test, the module is written to disk but **not**\\nregistered in ``sys.modules``, so the import mechanism cannot find it and\\nraises ``ModuleNotFoundError``, which the loader converts to\\n``EndpointDiscoveryError``.\\n\\nThe fixture yields a small namespace object with two members:\\n\\n* ``path``  -- the ``tmp_path`` directory (pass it to ``discover_endpoints``).\\n* ``make``  -- ``make(name, source, register=True)`` writes ``<name>.py``\\n  into that directory and optionally registers it in ``sys.modules``.\\n\\"\\"\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport importlib.util\\nimport sys\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom types import SimpleNamespace\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\n# --- 1. Make the backend package importable ---------------------------------\\n# ``backend/`` is the parent of the ``app`` package. Insert it at the front of\\n# ``sys.path`` so ``import app`` resolves to this project's backend.\\n_BACKEND_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\\nif str(_BACKEND_ROOT) not in sys.path:\\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(_BACKEND_ROOT))\\n\\n\\n# --- 2. Temp endpoint-module fixture ----------------------------------------\\n@pytest.fixture\\ndef endpoint_module(tmp_path):\\n    \\"\\"\\"Create temporary endpoint modules importable as ``app.endpoints.<name>``.\\n\\n    Usage::\\n\\n        def test_something(endpoint_module):\\n            endpoint_module.make(\\"alpha\\", \\"router = APIRouter()\\")\\n            result = discover_endpoints(endpoint_module.path)\\n            ...\\n\\n    For the import-failure test, pass ``register=False`` so the module is\\n    written to disk but not registered in ``sys.modules``::\\n\\n        def test_import_failure(endpoint_module):\\n            endpoint_module.make(\\"broken\\", \\"raise RuntimeError('boom')\\", register=False)\\n            with pytest.raises(EndpointDiscoveryError):\\n                discover_endpoints(endpoint_module.path)\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    # Ensure the parent package is imported so the dotted name resolves.\\n    import app.endpoints  # noqa: F401\\n\\n    created: list[str] = []\\n    registered: list[str] = []\\n\\n    def _make(name: str, source: str, register: bool = True) -> None:\\n        module_file = tmp_path / f\\"{name}.py\\"\\n        module_file.write_text(source, encoding=\\"utf-8\\")\\n        created.append(name)\\n\\n        if register:\\n            dotted = f\\"app.endpoints.{name}\\"\\n            spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(dotted, str(module_file))\\n            module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\\n            sys.modules[dotted] = module\\n            spec.loader.exec_module(module)\\n            registered.append(dotted)\\n\\n    yield SimpleNamespace(path=tmp_path, make=_make)\\n\\n    # --- teardown: clear registered modules and remove temp files ---\\n    for dotted in registered:\\n        sys.modules.pop(dotted, None)\\n    for name in created:\\n        (tmp_path / f\\"{name}.py\\").unlink(missing_ok=True)\\n", "end_line": 96, "start_line": 1, "total_lines": 96}	f	2026-09-19 12:28:59.505027-04
