1592	chat-c467de3f-d486-460c-8ddc-774ee34440cb	step-04	write_file	{"path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\cors-dummy\\\\README.md", "content": "# cors-dummy\\n\\nA compact, production-ready **FastAPI endpoint host** with a small **Vue 3 + Vite\\ndeveloper console**. Its defining feature is **drop-in endpoint modules**: adding a\\nnew API endpoint means adding **one file** under `backend/app/endpoints/` — you never\\nedit `main.py` or maintain a central router/import list.\\n\\nIn production the FastAPI process serves both the JSON API **and** the built Vue\\nconsole, so normal deployment is **one process and same-origin**. There is no\\nPostgreSQL, SQLAlchemy, Alembic, or Flask in the live implementation, and the app\\nboots with no database and no network I/O.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Project layout\\n\\n```\\ncors-dummy/\\n├── .env.example                  # safe, restrictive config template (no secrets)\\n├── README.md\\n├── cors-dummy-original-20260919.zip   # preserved original backup (do not modify)\\n├── backend/\\n│   ├── requirements.txt          # fastapi, uvicorn[standard], httpx, pytest\\n│   ├── conftest.py               # sys.path setup + endpoint_module test fixture\\n│   ├── app/\\n│   │   ├── main.py               # app factory (create_app) + static/SPA serving\\n│   │   ├── cors_policy.py        # origin policy (no wildcard default)\\n│   │   ├── meta.py               # core metadata route (OUTSIDE endpoints/)\\n│   │   └── endpoints/\\n│   │       ├── __init__.py       # exposes endpoints_dir()\\n│   │       ├── loader.py         # deterministic discovery + validation\\n│   │       ├── health.py         # example: GET /health\\n│   │       └── echo.py           # example: GET /info, POST /echo\\n│   └── tests/                    # backend test suite (pytest)\\n└── frontend/\\n    ├── package.json              # vue, vite, vitest, @vue/test-utils, jsdom\\n    ├── vite.config.js            # dev proxy /api -> FastAPI; vitest config\\n    ├── index.html\\n    └── src/\\n        ├── main.js\\n        ├── App.vue\\n        ├── lib/api.js            # fetch client for /api/*\\n        ├── components/           # HealthBadge, RouteList, RequestRunner\\n        ├── styles/main.css       # project-owned CSS variables\\n        └── __tests__/            # frontend test suite (vitest)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The drop-in endpoint signature\\n\\nEvery discoverable endpoint module lives in `backend/app/endpoints/` and exports\\n**exactly one** `router` attribute of type `fastapi.APIRouter`. That is the whole\\ncontract.\\n\\n### Add one endpoint file (copyable example)\\n\\nCreate a new file, e.g. `backend/app/endpoints/time.py`:\\n\\n```python\\n\\"\\"\\"Example endpoint module: time.\\n\\nDrop-in convention: add this one file and it is discovered automatically at\\nstartup. No changes to main.py or any central router list are required.\\n\\"\\"\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\n\\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter\\n\\nrouter = APIRouter()\\n\\n\\n@router.get(\\"/time\\")\\ndef time() -> dict:\\n    \\"\\"\\"Return the current UTC time.\\"\\"\\"\\n    return {\\"utc_now\\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()}\\n```\\n\\nThat's it. Restart the app (or reload in dev) and the new route is live at\\n`GET /api/time`, and it appears automatically in `GET /api/meta` and in the Vue\\nconsole. You did **not** touch `main.py`.\\n\\n### What the loader enforces\\n\\nThe loader (`backend/app/endpoints/loader.py`) discovers and validates modules\\ndeterministically at startup:\\n\\n- **Discovery** — scans `backend/app/endpoints/` for `*.py` files, **sorted\\n  alphabetically** for deterministic order.\\n- **Ignored** — `__init__.py` and any module whose name starts with an underscore\\n  (`_private.py`) are skipped, as is the loader itself.\\n- **Contract** — each discovered module must export a `router` attribute that is a\\n  `fastapi.APIRouter`. A missing or mistyped `router` raises\\n  `EndpointDiscoveryError` naming the offending module.\\n- **Loud failures** — an import failure in any endpoint module raises\\n  `EndpointDiscoveryError` naming the module. Nothing fails silently.\\n- **Collision detection** — two modules exposing the same `(method, path)` route\\n  raise `EndpointDiscoveryError` naming **both** modules. (Same path with\\n  different methods, e.g. `GET /x` and `POST /x`, is allowed.)\\n- **Safety** — no `eval`, `exec`, arbitrary filesystem imports, or remote code\\n  loading. Modules are imported by their package-local dotted name only.\\n\\nThe core **metadata route** (`GET /api/meta`) lives in `backend/app/meta.py`,\\n**outside** the auto-discovered package, and is mounted explicitly by the app\\nfactory. It reports the discovered modules and their effective routes so the Vue\\nconsole reflects endpoint additions automatically.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Configuration\\n\\nCopy `.env.example` to `.env` and adjust. All defaults are safe and restrictive.\\n\\n| Variable             | Default     | Meaning                                                        |\\n| -------------------- | ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | *(empty)* | Comma-separated explicit origins. Empty = no CORS middleware. |\\n| `HOST`               | `127.0.0.1` | Bind address for the production server.                       |\\n| `PORT`               | `18080`     | Port for the production server.                                |\\n\\n### CORS defaults (no wildcard)\\n\\n- The normal deployment is **same-origin** (FastAPI serves the built Vue app), so\\n  CORS is unnecessary by default.\\n- When `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` is **empty**, the app adds **no** CORS middleware at\\n  all — the most restrictive posture.\\n- When set, only the listed **explicit** origins are allowed.\\n- A wildcard `*` is **rejected at startup** with a `ValueError`. Wildcard CORS is\\n  never an acceptable default in this project.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Running\\n\\n### Prerequisites\\n\\n- Python 3.12 (`py -3.12`)\\n- Node.js + [pnpm](https://pnpm.io) for the frontend\\n\\n### Backend dependencies\\n\\n```bash\\npy -3.12 -m pip install -r backend/requirements.txt\\n```\\n\\n### Frontend dependencies\\n\\n```bash\\ncd frontend\\npnpm install\\n```\\n\\n### Development (two processes)\\n\\nRun the backend and the Vite dev server separately. Vite proxies `/api` to the\\nbackend, so the console works without CORS.\\n\\n```bash\\n# Terminal 1 — backend (default 127.0.0.1:18080)\\ncd backend\\npy -3.12 -m app.main\\n\\n# Terminal 2 — frontend dev server (default http://localhost:4665)\\ncd frontend\\npnpm dev\\n```\\n\\nOpen http://localhost:4665 for the developer console.\\n\\n### Production (one process, same-origin)\\n\\nBuild the frontend, then let FastAPI serve both the API and the built console:\\n\\n```bash\\n# 1. Build the Vue console into frontend/dist\\ncd frontend\\npnpm build\\n\\n# 2. Run the single-process production server\\ncd backend\\npy -3.12 -m app.main\\n```\\n\\nOpen http://127.0.0.1:18080 — the Vue console is served at `/`, static assets at\\n`/assets/*`, and the API at `/api/*`, all from the same origin.\\n\\n> The static/SPA serving is enabled automatically when `frontend/dist` exists. If\\n> the frontend has not been built, the app still starts (API-only), which is\\n> convenient for backend development.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n### Backend (pytest)\\n\\n```bash\\ncd backend\\npy -3.12 -m pytest tests/ -v\\n```\\n\\nCovers: auto-discovery without central registration, duplicate-route rejection,\\nmalformed-module and import-failure rejection, example endpoint responses,\\nmetadata output, default CORS safety (no wildcard), and the absence of any\\ndatabase/Flask/Alembic dependency.\\n\\n### Frontend (vitest)\\n\\n```bash\\ncd frontend\\npnpm test\\n```\\n\\nCovers: metadata/routes display, health state, and GET/POST JSON request-runner\\nbehavior (with mocked `fetch`/API client).\\n\\n### Frontend build\\n\\n```bash\\ncd frontend\\npnpm build\\n```\\n\\nProduces `frontend/dist/` (`index.html` + `assets/`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Preserved backup\\n\\nThe original project is preserved, untouched, at:\\n\\n```\\ncors-dummy-original-20260919.zip\\n```\\n\\nSHA-256: `94911AA0E7ECA739BBAC2A671F32251139387B20F6A49F220FA5AB2CC31B5340`\\n\\nThis ZIP is the safety backup of the pre-rebuild repository. It is **not** part of\\nthe live implementation and must not be modified. Verify it with:\\n\\n```bash\\n# Windows PowerShell\\nGet-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 \\"cors-dummy-original-20260919.zip\\"\\n```\\n"}	{"ok": true, "path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\cors-dummy\\\\README.md", "tool": "write_file", "bytes": 8189, "sha256": "a6ff9161365403cd02f71fa85557e6e202abebb0a5454ba18ebb86bf75be6db8", "created": true}	f	2026-09-19 16:45:11.418154-04
1593	chat-c467de3f-d486-460c-8ddc-774ee34440cb	step-04	read_file	{"path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\cors-dummy\\\\README.md"}	{"ok": true, "path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\cors-dummy\\\\README.md", "size": 8189, "tool": "read_file", "sha256": "a6ff9161365403cd02f71fa85557e6e202abebb0a5454ba18ebb86bf75be6db8", "content": "# cors-dummy\\n\\nA compact, production-ready **FastAPI endpoint host** with a small **Vue 3 + Vite\\ndeveloper console**. Its defining feature is **drop-in endpoint modules**: adding a\\nnew API endpoint means adding **one file** under `backend/app/endpoints/` — you never\\nedit `main.py` or maintain a central router/import list.\\n\\nIn production the FastAPI process serves both the JSON API **and** the built Vue\\nconsole, so normal deployment is **one process and same-origin**. There is no\\nPostgreSQL, SQLAlchemy, Alembic, or Flask in the live implementation, and the app\\nboots with no database and no network I/O.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Project layout\\n\\n```\\ncors-dummy/\\n├── .env.example                  # safe, restrictive config template (no secrets)\\n├── README.md\\n├── cors-dummy-original-20260919.zip   # preserved original backup (do not modify)\\n├── backend/\\n│   ├── requirements.txt          # fastapi, uvicorn[standard], httpx, pytest\\n│   ├── conftest.py               # sys.path setup + endpoint_module test fixture\\n│   ├── app/\\n│   │   ├── main.py               # app factory (create_app) + static/SPA serving\\n│   │   ├── cors_policy.py        # origin policy (no wildcard default)\\n│   │   ├── meta.py               # core metadata route (OUTSIDE endpoints/)\\n│   │   └── endpoints/\\n│   │       ├── __init__.py       # exposes endpoints_dir()\\n│   │       ├── loader.py         # deterministic discovery + validation\\n│   │       ├── health.py         # example: GET /health\\n│   │       └── echo.py           # example: GET /info, POST /echo\\n│   └── tests/                    # backend test suite (pytest)\\n└── frontend/\\n    ├── package.json              # vue, vite, vitest, @vue/test-utils, jsdom\\n    ├── vite.config.js            # dev proxy /api -> FastAPI; vitest config\\n    ├── index.html\\n    └── src/\\n        ├── main.js\\n        ├── App.vue\\n        ├── lib/api.js            # fetch client for /api/*\\n        ├── components/           # HealthBadge, RouteList, RequestRunner\\n        ├── styles/main.css       # project-owned CSS variables\\n        └── __tests__/            # frontend test suite (vitest)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The drop-in endpoint signature\\n\\nEvery discoverable endpoint module lives in `backend/app/endpoints/` and exports\\n**exactly one** `router` attribute of type `fastapi.APIRouter`. That is the whole\\ncontract.\\n\\n### Add one endpoint file (copyable example)\\n\\nCreate a new file, e.g. `backend/app/endpoints/time.py`:\\n\\n```python\\n\\"\\"\\"Example endpoint module: time.\\n\\nDrop-in convention: add this one file and it is discovered automatically at\\nstartup. No changes to main.py or any central router list are required.\\n\\"\\"\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\n\\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter\\n\\nrouter = APIRouter()\\n\\n\\n@router.get(\\"/time\\")\\ndef time() -> dict:\\n    \\"\\"\\"Return the current UTC time.\\"\\"\\"\\n    return {\\"utc_now\\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()}\\n```\\n\\nThat's it. Restart the app (or reload in dev) and the new route is live at\\n`GET /api/time`, and it appears automatically in `GET /api/meta` and in the Vue\\nconsole. You did **not** touch `main.py`.\\n\\n### What the loader enforces\\n\\nThe loader (`backend/app/endpoints/loader.py`) discovers and validates modules\\ndeterministically at startup:\\n\\n- **Discovery** — scans `backend/app/endpoints/` for `*.py` files, **sorted\\n  alphabetically** for deterministic order.\\n- **Ignored** — `__init__.py` and any module whose name starts with an underscore\\n  (`_private.py`) are skipped, as is the loader itself.\\n- **Contract** — each discovered module must export a `router` attribute that is a\\n  `fastapi.APIRouter`. A missing or mistyped `router` raises\\n  `EndpointDiscoveryError` naming the offending module.\\n- **Loud failures** — an import failure in any endpoint module raises\\n  `EndpointDiscoveryError` naming the module. Nothing fails silently.\\n- **Collision detection** — two modules exposing the same `(method, path)` route\\n  raise `EndpointDiscoveryError` naming **both** modules. (Same path with\\n  different methods, e.g. `GET /x` and `POST /x`, is allowed.)\\n- **Safety** — no `eval`, `exec`, arbitrary filesystem imports, or remote code\\n  loading. Modules are imported by their package-local dotted name only.\\n\\nThe core **metadata route** (`GET /api/meta`) lives in `backend/app/meta.py`,\\n**outside** the auto-discovered package, and is mounted explicitly by the app\\nfactory. It reports the discovered modules and their effective routes so the Vue\\nconsole reflects endpoint additions automatically.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Configuration\\n\\nCopy `.env.example` to `.env` and adjust. All defaults are safe and restrictive.\\n\\n| Variable             | Default     | Meaning                                                        |\\n| -------------------- | ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | *(empty)* | Comma-separated explicit origins. Empty = no CORS middleware. |\\n| `HOST`               | `127.0.0.1` | Bind address for the production server.                       |\\n| `PORT`               | `18080`     | Port for the production server.                                |\\n\\n### CORS defaults (no wildcard)\\n\\n- The normal deployment is **same-origin** (FastAPI serves the built Vue app), so\\n  CORS is unnecessary by default.\\n- When `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` is **empty**, the app adds **no** CORS middleware at\\n  all — the most restrictive posture.\\n- When set, only the listed **explicit** origins are allowed.\\n- A wildcard `*` is **rejected at startup** with a `ValueError`. Wildcard CORS is\\n  never an acceptable default in this project.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Running\\n\\n### Prerequisites\\n\\n- Python 3.12 (`py -3.12`)\\n- Node.js + [pnpm](https://pnpm.io) for the frontend\\n\\n### Backend dependencies\\n\\n```bash\\npy -3.12 -m pip install -r backend/requirements.txt\\n```\\n\\n### Frontend dependencies\\n\\n```bash\\ncd frontend\\npnpm install\\n```\\n\\n### Development (two processes)\\n\\nRun the backend and the Vite dev server separately. Vite proxies `/api` to the\\nbackend, so the console works without CORS.\\n\\n```bash\\n# Terminal 1 — backend (default 127.0.0.1:18080)\\ncd backend\\npy -3.12 -m app.main\\n\\n# Terminal 2 — frontend dev server (default http://localhost:4665)\\ncd frontend\\npnpm dev\\n```\\n\\nOpen http://localhost:4665 for the developer console.\\n\\n### Production (one process, same-origin)\\n\\nBuild the frontend, then let FastAPI serve both the API and the built console:\\n\\n```bash\\n# 1. Build the Vue console into frontend/dist\\ncd frontend\\npnpm build\\n\\n# 2. Run the single-process production server\\ncd backend\\npy -3.12 -m app.main\\n```\\n\\nOpen http://127.0.0.1:18080 — the Vue console is served at `/`, static assets at\\n`/assets/*`, and the API at `/api/*`, all from the same origin.\\n\\n> The static/SPA serving is enabled automatically when `frontend/dist` exists. If\\n> the frontend has not been built, the app still starts (API-only), which is\\n> convenient for backend development.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n### Backend (pytest)\\n\\n```bash\\ncd backend\\npy -3.12 -m pytest tests/ -v\\n```\\n\\nCovers: auto-discovery without central registration, duplicate-route rejection,\\nmalformed-module and import-failure rejection, example endpoint responses,\\nmetadata output, default CORS safety (no wildcard), and the absence of any\\ndatabase/Flask/Alembic dependency.\\n\\n### Frontend (vitest)\\n\\n```bash\\ncd frontend\\npnpm test\\n```\\n\\nCovers: metadata/routes display, health state, and GET/POST JSON request-runner\\nbehavior (with mocked `fetch`/API client).\\n\\n### Frontend build\\n\\n```bash\\ncd frontend\\npnpm build\\n```\\n\\nProduces `frontend/dist/` (`index.html` + `assets/`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Preserved backup\\n\\nThe original project is preserved, untouched, at:\\n\\n```\\ncors-dummy-original-20260919.zip\\n```\\n\\nSHA-256: `94911AA0E7ECA739BBAC2A671F32251139387B20F6A49F220FA5AB2CC31B5340`\\n\\nThis ZIP is the safety backup of the pre-rebuild repository. It is **not** part of\\nthe live implementation and must not be modified. Verify it with:\\n\\n```bash\\n# Windows PowerShell\\nGet-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 \\"cors-dummy-original-20260919.zip\\"\\n```\\n", "end_line": 245, "start_line": 1, "total_lines": 245}	f	2026-09-19 16:45:24.054152-04
