1590	chat-c467de3f-d486-460c-8ddc-774ee34440cb	step-04	write_file	{"path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\cors-dummy\\\\backend\\\\requirements.txt", "content": "# cors-dummy backend dependencies\\n#\\n# Runtime (needed to import and serve the app):\\n#   - fastapi: the endpoint host framework (app factory, routers, TestClient).\\n#   - uvicorn[standard]: ASGI server used by `python -m app.main` / production.\\n#\\n# Test-only (needed to run the backend test suite):\\n#   - httpx: transport for fastapi.testclient.TestClient.\\n#   - pytest: test runner.\\n#\\n# There is intentionally NO database driver (no psycopg/SQLAlchemy/Alembic)\\n# and NO Flask. The endpoint host boots with no database and no network I/O.\\n#\\n# Install:\\n#   py -3.12 -m pip install -r backend/requirements.txt\\n\\nfastapi>=0.115,<1.0\\nuvicorn[standard]>=0.30,<1.0\\n\\n# --- test-only ---\\nhttpx>=0.27,<1.0\\npytest>=8.0,<10.0\\n"}	{"ok": true, "path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\cors-dummy\\\\backend\\\\requirements.txt", "tool": "write_file", "bytes": 712, "sha256": "b94d29505532cddb041b1151436253aa53114da42c0858650d6ce0a6f4de8e29", "created": true}	f	2026-09-19 16:43:14.6471-04
1591	chat-c467de3f-d486-460c-8ddc-774ee34440cb	step-04	write_file	{"path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\cors-dummy\\\\.env.example", "content": "# cors-dummy environment configuration (example)\\n#\\n# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust as needed. No secrets are required.\\n# The app reads these from the process environment; a `.env` file is only\\n# convenient for local runs. Every value below is a safe, restrictive default.\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# CORS (cross-origin access)\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Comma-separated list of EXPLICIT allowed origins, e.g.:\\n#   CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://app.example.com,https://admin.example.com\\n#\\n# IMPORTANT:\\n#   * Leave EMPTY (the default) for the normal same-origin deployment. When\\n#     empty, the app adds NO CORS middleware at all, which is the most\\n#     restrictive posture. This is the intended production default.\\n#   * A wildcard `*` is REJECTED at startup (ValueError). Wildcard CORS is\\n#     never an acceptable default here.\\n#   * The normal deployment is same-origin (FastAPI serves the built Vue app),\\n#     so CORS is usually unnecessary.\\nCORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Server bind (used by `python -m app.main` / uvicorn)\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Bind to loopback by default. Change to 0.0.0.0 only if you intentionally\\n# expose the host on a network interface (and keep CORS restrictive).\\nHOST=127.0.0.1\\n\\n# Port for the single-process production server (API + built Vue console).\\nPORT=18080\\n"}	{"ok": true, "path": "D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\cors-dummy\\\\.env.example", "tool": "write_file", "bytes": 1540, "sha256": "754d993de7c6ed8b6f3367b84e7c7bd6fea7b6508c4dbaa9c231a003d066625d", "created": true}	f	2026-09-19 16:43: