(758.89 / 02:24) live in the y≈430–470 band, *inside* the price pane.\\n- So the true price pane is roughly **y ≈ 110 → 600**, not 154 → 440.\\n\\n**2) Volume pane**\\n- Yes. A thin histogram of vertical volume bars sits immediately below the candles, ≈ **y 560–620**, with no (or minimal) numeric axis of its own. It is visually attached to the price pane but is a separate sub‑pane.\\n\\n**3) UI elements a detector could mistake for chart data**\\n- Right‑hand price axis labels: 776.00, 772.00, 768.00, 764.00, 760.00, 756.00.\\n- Red last‑price tag \\"758.89 / 02:24\\" on the right edge.\\n- Dotted horizontal last‑price line crossing the pane.\\n- Top‑left \\"5\\" timeframe dropdown and the green/pink indicator‑toggle icons; \\"USD\\" currency dropdown.\\n- Per‑pane axis labels on the right: 100/0, 10.00/0.0000, 50.00/25.00, 0.0000/‑40.00, 2.00/0.0000.\\n- X‑axis time labels: Sep, 4, 10, 15.\\n- Bottom toolbar (SPY, 15m, draw/indicator icons) and the nav bar (Watchlist / Chart / Explore / Community / Menu), plus the phone status bar.\\n\\n**4) Thin / ambiguous / occluded elements**\\n- Long thin candle wicks that can be dropped by a coarse detector.\\n- Multiple overlapping moving‑average lines (blue, orange, green) that cross each other and the band edges.\\n- The thin black Bollinger‑band boundary lines vs. candle wicks (easy to confuse).\\n- The very thin volume bars.\\n- Oscillator panes packed with thin red/green/blue lines and red/green histogram bars, plus pink/green background shading.\\n- Faint dotted gridlines that can be misread as data traces.\\n\\n**5) Does the detection match?**\\n- **Top y=154:** close but slightly low — the real top of the price pane is ~110–130; 154 lands just inside the upper band region. Acceptable as \\"top of drawing area\\" but it would clip the topmost gridline/label.\\n- **Bottom y=440:** **incorrect / too high.** It cuts off roughly the lower third of the price pane (the recent down‑leg candles, the 760/756 gridlines, and the red last‑price tag all sit below 440). The true bottom is ~560–620.\\n\\n**6) Overall layout**\\nTop‑to‑bottom: status bar → ticker header → **main price pane (with attached volume strip)** → **five indicator/oscillator panes** (0–100 histogram; 0–10 line; 0–50 stochastic‑style with shaded background; 0 to ‑40 green line; 0–2 multi‑line) → x‑axis time labels → bottom toolbar → nav bar → system nav. So: **1 main price pane + 1 volume strip + 5 indicator panes** below it.\\n\\n**Bottom line:** the pipeline's top (154) is marginally low and its bottom (440) is clearly wrong — it truncates the lower portion of the price pane and would mis‑assign the volume strip and the last‑price tag as \\"outside\\" the pane. Recommend re‑anchoring the price pane to ≈ **110 → 600** and treating the 560–620 band as a separate volume sub‑pane.", "image_count": 2}	f	2026-09-19 18:55:20.626427-04
