1701	chat-5bbe44fe-9282-40f3-9281-19760f0d27e8	step-01	vision_image	{"paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\SPY_15m_20260920-1105.jpg", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260920-111222-349a2d7b-SPY_15m_20260920-1105-high\\\\reconstruction.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260920-111222-349a2d7b-SPY_15m_20260920-1105-high\\\\06_horizontal.png"], "prompt": "This is an SPY 15-minute candlestick chart screenshot (709x1536 px). The main price pane spans roughly y=154 to y=578; below that is a volume histogram pane.\\n\\nPlease extract and report, with high precision:\\n1. The exact price-axis (right-side) tick labels visible in the main price pane, from top to bottom (e.g., 768.00, 764.00, 760.00, 756.00, etc.). List every numeric label you can read.\\n2. The approximate price of the most recent (rightmost) candle's close, high, and low.\\n3. The overall visible price range (highest high and lowest low) across the whole chart.\\n4. The candle structure of the most recent 1-2 sessions: are candles mostly green or red? Are there long wicks? Any obvious support/resistance levels where price repeatedly bounced?\\n5. The volume pane: are recent volume bars increasing or decreasing? Any standout high-volume bars?\\n6. Any visible trend lines, moving averages, or annotations.\\n7. The date/time labels on the x-axis if visible.\\n\\nBe precise about numbers. If a label is partially obscured, give your best estimate and note uncertainty."}	{"ok": true, "tool": "vision_image", "paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\SPY_15m_20260920-1105.jpg", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260920-111222-349a2d7b-SPY_15m_20260920-1105-high\\\\reconstruction.png", "C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260920-111222-349a2d7b-SPY_15m_20260920-1105-high\\\\06_horizontal.png"], "answer": "Here's my read of the chart. I've flagged estimates where the image resolution or overlap makes a label ambiguous.\\n\\n**1. Right‑side price‑axis tick labels (top → bottom)**\\n- 776.00\\n- 772.00\\n- 768.00\\n- 764.00\\n- 760.00\\n- 756.00\\n- 752.00\\n- 748.00\\n\\nPlus the **live‑price tag (green box) = 761.64**, which sits between the 764.00 and 760.00 gridlines (it's the current quote, not a gridline tick). Header confirms: **761.64, −0.91 (−0.12%)**.\\n\\n**2. Most recent (rightmost) candle**\\n- Close: **≈ 761.6** (matches the 761.64 tag)\\n- High: **≈ 762.5** (small upper wick)\\n- Low: **≈ 759.5–760.0** (lower wick into the 760 gridline)\\n- Body is small; this is an estimate from pixel position, ±~0.5.\\n\\n**3. Overall visible price range**\\n- Highest high: **≈ 774–775** (the early peak where the blue MA tops out, just under the 776 gridline).\\n- Lowest low: **≈ 752–753** (the long red down‑wick in the right‑of‑center area, dipping just below the 752 gridline).\\n- So the chart spans roughly **752 → 775**.\\n\\n**4. Recent 1–2 session candle structure**\\n- **Mixed green and red**, no dominant color — choppy, range‑bound action with many small bodies and prominent wicks (two‑sided).\\n- **Long wicks** are common, especially downward (e.g., the deep red wick to ~752) and a few upward spikes.\\n- Repeated **support** bounces around **756–758** and **760**; repeated **resistance** around **764–766** and the upper band **~770–774**. Price has been oscillating inside that envelope.\\n\\n**5. Volume pane**\\n- Bars are **mixed green/red**, generally **moderate and roughly flat** across the window — no clear sustained increase or decrease.\\n- **Standout high‑volume bars:** a few tall green spikes (notably mid‑chart around the \\"10–12\\" x‑region and one near the right edge) that punch well above the surrounding bars; the rest are short.\\n\\n**6. Trend lines / MAs / annotations**\\n- **Two moving averages** overlaid on price: a **blue** line and an **orange/yellow** line (the \\"5\\" dropdown is the MA‑period selector).\\n- A **light‑purple shaded band** enveloping price (Bollinger‑band / regression‑channel style envelope).\\n- A circled **\\"D\\"** marker annotation in the lower‑right of the price pane.\\n- Lower indicator panes show oscillator‑style lines (red/green/blue) and a histogram, but no explicit trendlines.\\n\\n**7. X‑axis date/time labels**\\n- Visible numeric day labels: **4, 10, 15, 18** (day‑of‑month), with a **partially cut‑off label at the far left** (looks like the tail of a month/day word, e.g. \\"…ep\\" — likely \\"Sep\\" or a weekday; uncertain).\\n- Timeframe is **15m** (shown in the bottom bar: \\"SPY 15m\\").\\n\\n**Uncertainty notes:** exact high/low of the last candle and the precise peak/trough values are pixel‑estimated (±0.5–1.0). The far‑left x‑axis label is clipped and only partially legible. Everything else is read directly from visible labels.", "image_count": 3}	f	2026-09-20 11:13:46.205809-04
1702	chat-5bbe44fe-9282-40f3-9281-19760f0d27e8	step-01	vision_image	{"paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\SPY_15m_20260920-1105.jpg"], "prompt": "Focus ONLY on the right-side price axis of the main candlestick pane (the pane between roughly y=154 and y=578). \\n\\n1. Read every numeric price label on the right axis from top to bottom. Be exact — are they 776, 772, 768, 764, 760, 756, 752, 748? Or different numbers?\\n\\n2. Read the header bar at the very top of the image: what is the ticker, the current price, the change (absolute and %), and any other data shown (volume, etc.)?\\n\\n3. Look at the last 8-10 candles (rightmost portion of the price pane). For each, estimate: is it green or red? approximate body size (small/medium/large)? Does it have a long upper wick, long lower wick, or both? What approximate price level does its body sit at?\\n\\n4. Is there a visible gap (open above prior close, or open below prior close) at the start of the most recent session?\\n\\n5. What is the x-axis label for the rightmost time period? Is it a date like \\"Sep 19\\" or \\"Sep 20\\"?"}	{"ok": true, "tool": "vision_image", "paths": ["C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\SPY_15m_20260920-1105.jpg"], "answer": "Here is my exact read of the image, point by point.\\n\\n**1. Right‑side price axis (main candlestick pane), top → bottom:**\\n- 776.00\\n- 772.00\\n- 768.00\\n- 764.00\\n- **761.64** (this one is in a green highlighted box — it's the live/last price tag, not a gridline)\\n- 760.00\\n- 756.00\\n- 752.00\\n- 748.00\\n\\nSo your list is *almost* right but incomplete: the gridlines are 776 / 772 / 768 / 764 / 760 / 756 / 752 / 748 (in 4‑point steps), **plus** the floating 761.64 price tag sitting between 764 and 760. There is no 768→760 jump; 764 is present.\\n\\n**2. Header bar (top):**\\n- Ticker / name: **SPDR S&P 500 ETF TRUST** (symbol SPY, per the bottom bar)\\n- Current price: **761.64**\\n- Change: **−0.91** absolute, **−0.12%** (shown in red)\\n- Currency selector on the right: **USD**\\n- No volume figure is shown in the header itself (volume is the thin bar strip at the bottom of the price pane).\\n- Left of the chart there's an interval selector showing **5** (with a down‑chevron); the bottom status bar confirms the active chart is **SPY 15m**.\\n\\n**3. Rightmost ~8–10 candles (estimates):**\\nReading left‑to‑right toward the right edge, bodies are generally **small** and clustered in the **760–764** band:\\n- A few candles back there is one candle with a **very long lower wick** (a sharp spike down toward ~752–753, near the blue \\"D\\" marker) — small body, long lower wick.\\n- The next several are small‑bodied, alternating **green and red**, mostly no long wicks, bodies around **761–763**.\\n- The **last (rightmost) candle** appears **green**, small body, sitting around **761–762**, with a short upper wick and minimal lower wick.\\n- Overall the rightmost cluster is tight range‑bound (≈760–764) with one prominent down‑wick outlier just before it.\\n\\n**4. Visible session gap at the start of the most recent session:**\\nOn this 15m view I do **not** see a clean open‑above‑prior‑close or open‑below‑prior‑close gap in the rightmost cluster — the candles connect continuously. The most notable discontinuity is the **long lower wick / spike** (the down‑tick to ~752–753), not a true session gap. So: no clear visible gap; one sharp intrabar wick instead.\\n\\n**5. Rightmost x‑axis label:**\\nThe time axis reads (left→right): a partial **\\"…ep\\"** (i.e. *Sep*), then **4**, **10**, **15**, **18**. The rightmost label is **18** — a day‑of‑month number, **not** \\"Sep 19\\" or \\"Sep 20\\".\\n\\nCaveat: candle color/wick calls in point 3 are visual estimates from a compressed screenshot; the axis numbers, header values, and x‑axis labels in points 1, 2, and 5 are read directly and should be exact.", "image_count": 1}	f	2026-09-20 11:14:53.454205-04
