ent swing‑high cluster around **768–770** [EST], with the left‑side peak approaching the **772.00** line [EXACT label] as the major overhead supply.\\n\\n**7. INTERMEDIATE PIVOT / GAP‑FILL**\\n- **Gap:** No clear empty price band (session gap) is visible on this 15m view — candles are continuous across the pane. **No gap‑fill magnet identified.**\\n- **Intermediate pivot:** The **blue MA line / ~762–763 consolidation midpoint** [EST] sits between the last close (761.64) and the 764.00 resistance — a natural pivot / re‑entry reference.\\n\\n**8. VISIBLE PRICE RANGE (full span)**\\n- Highest high: **~771–772** (left‑side peak, near the 772.00 line) [EST]\\n- Lowest low: **~752–753** (the long lower wick of the sharp down candle, right‑of‑center) [EST]\\n\\n**9. THE 'D' MARKER**\\nSits at approximately **752–754** [EST] in the lower‑right of the price pane, aligned with the **low wick of the sharp down candle** — i.e., it is flagging that **wick low** (a divergence / demand‑zone signal at the swing low), not a body.\\n\\n---\\n**Summary of the 3–4 key levels to anchor Monday:**\\n- Resistance 2: **768–770** (upper band / swing highs)\\n- Resistance 1: **764.00** (upper band + orange MA)\\n- **Last close / pivot: 761.64** (blue MA ~762–763)\\n- Support 1: **760.00** (lower band + blue MA + last wick)\\n- Support 2 (deeper): **756.00**, hard floor **~752–753**\\n\\nCaveat: only the header values and the right‑axis tick labels are exact; every candle high/low, MA position, band edge, and the 'D' marker's price are pixel estimates against those gridlines and will carry a small error. If you want, I can re‑measure any single level against a specific gridline to tighten the estimate.", "image_count": 1}	f	2026-09-20 11:25:10.121759-04
