chat-44b0e0ba-0234-4891-9ba8-59e33431b4c2	step-02	[]	# Recovery Handoff — Step 2/9: Endpoint Loader & Validation\n\n**Parent task:** chat-44b0e0ba-0234-4891-9ba8-59e33431b4c2 / step-02\n**Project root:** `D:\\LOCAL_Share\\Code Projects\\cors-dummy`\n**Status:** Design complete. **Zero files written. Zero tests run.**\n\n## Immutable Scope (Step 2 ONLY)\nWrite `backend/app/endpoints/loader.py` + tests. Do NOT implement app factory, metadata route, example endpoints, Vue, or any step 3+ work. No PostgreSQL/SQLAlchemy/Alembic/Flask. No `eval`/`exec`. ZIP `cors-dummy-original-20260919.zip` in live root must remain byte-identical.\n\n## Settled Design (implement exactly this)\n\n**File:** `backend/app/endpoints/loader.py`\n\n- `DiscoveredEndpoint` dataclass: `module_name: str`, `router: APIRouter`, `routes: list[tuple[str, str]]` (method, path).\n- `EndpointDiscoveryError(Exception)` — all failure modes.\n- `discover_endpoints(endpoints_dir: Path | str) -> list[DiscoveredEndpoint]`:\n  1. Resolve dir; if missing → raise `EndpointDiscoveryError`.\n  2. Scan `*.py`; skip `__init__.py` and names starting with `_`.\n  3. Sort stems alphabetically (deterministic).\n  4. Import via `importlib.import_module(f"app.endpoints.{stem}")`. Catch any exception → raise `EndpointDiscoveryError(f"Import failed for '{stem}': {exc}")`.\n  5. Validate: `router = getattr(mod, "router", None)`; must be `isinstance(router, fastapi.APIRouter)`. Missing/wrong type → raise naming the module.\n  6. Extract routes: for each `r in router.routes`, if `r.methods` is not None, yield `(m, r.path)` for each `m in r.methods`. Skip Mount/WebSocket (methods=None).\n  7. Duplicate detection: dict `(method, path) → first_module`. Collision → raise naming both modules + conflicting route.\n  8. Return list sorted by `module_name`.\n\n**Convention:** module exports exactly one `router` attr of type `APIRouter`. Multiple routers not supported; only `router` checked.\n\n## Test Plan (write `backend/tests/test_endpoint_loader.py`)\n\n| Case | Expectation |\n|---|---|\n| Valid module discovered | In result list |\n| `_private.py` / `__init__.py` | Ignored |\n| Missing `router` export | `EndpointDiscoveryError` naming module |\n| Import failure (`import nonexistent_pkg`) | `EndpointDiscoveryError` with module name |\n| Two modules, same method+path | `EndpointDiscoveryError` naming both |\n| Same path, GET vs POST | Allowed, no error |\n| `zeta`, `alpha`, `mid` → order | alpha, mid, zeta |\n| Non-existent dir | `EndpointDiscoveryError` |\n| Empty dir | `[]` |\n| Source scan | No `eval(`, no `exec(` in loader source |\n\n**Fixture hygiene:** after each test, delete temp `.py` files from endpoints dir; purge `sys.modules` entries for `app.endpoints.*`. Ensure `sys.path` includes `backend/` before importing loader.\n\n## Exact Next Actions (in order)\n1. Confirm/install FastAPI: `pip install fastapi` (or verify present).\n2. Create `backend/app/__init__.py` (empty), `backend/app/endpoints/__init__.py` (empty).\n3. Write `backend/app/endpoints/loader.py` per design above.\n4. Write `backend/tests/test_endpoint_loader.py` per test plan above.\n5. Run `pytest backend/tests/test_endpoint_loader.py -v`; iterate until green.\n6. Grep loader source for `eval`/`exec` to confirm absence.\n7. Git checkpoint commit.\n\n## Authoritative Constraints\n- No `eval`, `exec`, or unsafe dynamic loading.\n- No DB dependencies of any kind.\n- No wildcard CORS (that's step 3+ anyway).\n- ZIP integrity: verify hash before and after any work; do not modify.\n- Loader must be importable standalone: `from app.endpoints.loader import discover_endpoints, EndpointDiscoveryError, DiscoveredEndpoint`.\n\n## Unresolved (minor, decide during implementation)\n- Loader filename: `loader.py` (preferred) vs `discovery.py`. Use `loader.py`.\n- Whether to accept a pre-built module-name list for test injection. Current: directory scan only; tests create real temp files.\n\n## What Must Happen Next (for this step)\nImplement the loader + tests, run them green, verify no eval/exec, commit. Then hand off to step 3 (app factory, metadata route, example endpoints). Do not absorb step 3 work.	2026-09-19 11:26:19.293532-04	2026-09-19 11:26:19.293532-04
child-4a894c02-7146-42dc-a1e6-24d9d34569dd	work	[]	All verification checks pass with discriminating evidence. The work step is complete and verified.\n\n## Final Candidate — Oversize Recovery Unit 1: Provision Environment & Package Scaffolding\n\n**Status: COMPLETE — all verification criteria satisfied with discriminating evidence.**\n\n### Verification Evidence (observed, not assumed)\n\n| Check | Command / Method | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| fastapi + pytest importable | `py -3.12 -c "import fastapi, pytest"` | **exit 0** — fastapi 0.141.1, pytest 9.1.1 |\n| `backend/app/__init__.py` exists + readable | readback via `os.path.getsize` + SHA-256 | 0 bytes, `e3b0c442…b855` (empty-file hash) |\n| `backend/app/endpoints/__init__.py` exists + readable | readback via `os.path.getsize` + SHA-256 | 0 bytes, `e3b0c442…b855` |\n| Backup ZIP unchanged | SHA-256 of `cors-dummy-original-20260919.zip` | `94911aa0e7eca739bbac2a671f32251139387b20f6a49f220fa5ab2cc31b5340` — **matches expected** |\n| Negative: no loader.py / test file written | full `os.walk` of `backend/` | tree contains **only** the two `__init__.py` files |\n\n### What was done (this unit, bounded scope)\n1. Chose `py -3.12` as the single interpreter; installed **fastapi** and **pytest** into it; both import successfully.\n2. Created empty `backend/app/__init__.py` and `backend/app/endpoints/__init__.py` so `app.endpoints.*` is importable.\n3. **Did not** write `loader.py` or any test file — confirmed by full tree walk (only the two `__init__.py` files exist under `backend/`).\n4. Backup ZIP verified byte-identical (SHA-256 unchanged).\n\n### Scope discipline\n- No step-3+ work leaked in (no app factory, no metadata route, no example endpoints, no Vue).\n- No DB dependencies, no eval/exec, no wildcard CORS introduced.\n- The durable checkpoint is file readback + green import (project is not a git repository, so no commit is applicable).\n\n### Handoff to next unit\nThe environment is provisioned and the package skeleton is importable. The next unit ("Implement the endpoint loader") can now write `backend/app/endpoints/loader.py` per the settled design in the compact handoff note (`step-02.md`) and import it standalone with `backend/` on `sys.path`.\n\n**No long-lived server left running. No files outside the editable root touched. Backup ZIP preserved.**	2026-09-19 11:38:17.505181-04	2026-09-19 11:38:17.505181-04
chat-3a1c2103-f75a-4477-a4b1-01d0a0d60ad2	step-02	[]	**RECOVERY HANDOFF — Step 2/6: docker-compose.yml + Traefik config**\nParent: `chat-3a1c2103-f75a-4477-a4b1-01d0a0d60ad2` / `step-02`\n\n**PROJECT ROOT**: `D:\\LOCAL_Share\\Code Projects\\ca8d-tailnet-host`\n**DEPLOY TARGET**: ca8d QNAP NAS (Tailscale-only). Do NOT deploy or bind on KHzz.\n\n**IMMUTABLE SCOPE**: Write `docker-compose.yml`, `config/traefik.yml` (static), `config/dynamic.yml` (or generation script), `scripts/setup-tls.sh`, append `TAILNET_BIND_ADDR` to `.env.example`. Verify per checklist. Do NOT write devbox Dockerfile (step-04), test-service Dockerfile (step-03), README, or `.gitignore`.\n\n**COMPLETED**: Nothing on disk. All design locked in thinking notes. No files written yet.\n\n**LOCKED DESIGN DECISIONS**:\n- Networks: `proxy` (traefik, pihole, test-http) + `backend` (pihole, devbox). Pihole on both.\n- Bind: single `TAILNET_BIND_ADDR` env (default `127.0.0.1`). Never `0.0.0.0`. All host port mappings use it.\n- No full Docker socket mount. Traefik discovery via **file provider** (`dynamic.yml`).\n- TLS: `scripts/setup-tls.sh` (POSIX). Modes: `tailscale` | `internal-ca` | `none`. Ensures `TLS_CERTS_DIR/tls.crt`+`tls.key` exist before Traefik starts.\n- Healthchecks: traefik→`wget -qO- http://127.0.0.1:80/ping`; pihole→`wget -qO- http://127.0.0.1:80/`; test-http→`wget -qO- http://127.0.0.1:8080/`; devbox→`pgrep -x sshd` (step-04 must add `procps`; fallback `bash -c 'exec 3<>/dev/tcp/127.0.0.1/22'`).\n- test-http: `build: ./test-service` (step-03). devbox: `build: ./devbox` (step-04).\n- Pihole admin: via Traefik only (no direct host port). DNS 53/tcp+udp: direct host port.\n- Compose: no `version:` field. `name: ${COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME:-ca8d-tailnet-host}`.\n- Traefik image: `traefik:v3.1`. Dashboard on 8081 (tailnet-only).\n- Ports: 8080 (web), 8443 (websecure), 8081 (dashboard), 53/tcp+udp (DNS), 2222 (SSH).\n\n**#1 BLOCKER — FQDN in dynamic.yml**:\n`dynamic.yml` is a plain file; `${TAILSCALE