 config-summary; use bounded upstream reads; validate configured URLs/paths; no wildcard production CORS.\\n\\nVerification evidence must actually prove the requirement and would fail if the work were wrong. Do not use echo/no-op success markers. Short-lived bounded local servers are acceptable for real tests and must be stopped. Do not leave the app running after verification.\\n\\nNORM-GENERATED EXECUTION STEP:\\nImplement a backend settings module (pydantic-settings or equivalent) that loads CORS allowed origins, dev/test mode flag, service registry config, timeouts, and bounded response size from environment variables with restrictive production defaults. Implement an Origin Contract module that owns all origin-policy decisions and returns a structured allow/deny decision with a reason code. Production default must be restrictive (no wildcard). Wildcard allowed only when an explicit dev/test mode flag is set.\\n\\nVERIFICATION REQUIREMENT:\\nOrigin Contract module exists and returns structured allow/deny with reason; production default rejects wildcard; dev mode flag enables wildcard; settings load from environment without hard-coded secrets.\\n\\nDo only this step. Do not silently absorb later steps. Return a concise durable result for subsequent steps. Do not present this intermediate result as the final answer."}, {"id": "step-03", "name": "Service Registry and safe upstream client", "verify": "Service Registry validates names and paths; upstream client enforces timeout and bounded size; requests to unregistered services or disallowed paths are rejected; no cookies/authorization forwarded by default.", "depends_on": ["step-02"], "description": "PROMPT ORIGIN: norm_generated_step\\nTASK STEP: 3/10\\nSTEP NAME: Service Registry and safe upstream client\\n\\nAUTHORITATIVE ORIGINAL USER REQUEST:\\nFinish D:\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\Code Projects\\\\cors-dummy as a production-ready CORS troubleshooting/reference app. Actually implement it. Preserve the repo's experimenta