chat-80cb7910-1e35-4743-b2be-e1b9ac28bc26	step-03	Inspect custom CSS and LESS files	completed	I now have all the custom CSS/LESS files read. Let me compile the complete catalog.\n\n---\n\n## Step 3 Result: Custom CSS & LESS Catalog\n\n### Which Files Are Actually Loaded\n\nFrom `index.html` `<head>` (Step 2), only **one** custom stylesheet is linked:\n\n| Line | Link | Status |\n|------|------|--------|\n| 10 | `<link rel="stylesheet/less" href="/css/personal-touch-cleaned.less">` | **ACTIVE** — compiled in-browser by less.js |\n| 11 | less.js 4.1.3 CDN | **ACTIVE** — runtime LESS compiler |\n\n**Dead / unlinked files (5):**\n\n| File | Size | Why dead |\n|------|------|----------|\n| `personal-touch.css` | 7.3 KB | Compiled version of the LESS, but the `.less` source is linked instead. Also **out of sync** with the LESS (see below). |\n| `barebones.css` | 83 B | Single `.test-big-square-box` rule. No element in HTML uses this class. |\n| `dropdown-converted.css` | 2.7 KB | Green-themed dropdown nav (Futura font, `#58d39f` palette). No matching markup in `index.html`. |\n| `dropdown-example.sass` | 3.2 KB | SASS source for the above. Different preprocessor, different design. |\n| All 37 Bootstrap/theme files | ~2.5 MB | Bootstrap is loaded from CDN (line 8). Local copies are never linked. |\n\n**Inline `<style>` in `resume.html`** (loaded via `$.load()`):\n```css\n.resume { background-color:#f0f0f0; border-width:4px; border-style:dashed; padding-left:40px; text-align:left; }\nh5 { font-family:'Raleway',sans-serif; font-size:2rem; }\n```\n- `'Raleway'` font is **never loaded** (no Google Fonts link for it). Falls back to `sans-serif`.\n- `h5` rule is **global** (no scoping) — will affect every `<h5>` on the page once injected.\n\n---\n\n### `personal-touch-cleaned.less` — Full Rule Catalog (607 lines)\n\n#### LESS Variables (lines 1–8)\n| Variable | Value | Used? |\n|----------|-------|-------|\n| `@layer-top` | `200` | **Never referenced** in any rule |\n| `@layer-middle-1` | `100` | **Never referenced** |\n| `@layer-middle-2` | `99` | **Never referenced** |\n| `@layer-middle-3` | `98` | **Never referenced** |\n| `@layer-middle-4` | `97` | **Never referenced** |\n| `@layer-bottom` | `-100` | **Never referenced** |\n| `@ccolor-blue` | `#0e4d8d` | Used once: `#div-developer ol { background-color: #0e4d8d }` |\n| `@ccolor-yellow` | `#ffee9f` | **Never referenced** |\n\n> **6 of 8 variables are dead.** The z-index layer system was planned but never applied.\n\n#### CSS Custom Properties in `:root` (lines 9–13)\n| Property | Value | Used? |\n|----------|-------|-------|\n| `--full-menu-height` | `0px` | **Never referenced** in any rule |\n| `--ccolor-neat-green` | `#28d898` | Used once: `#highlight-box` inline style in HTML |\n| `--ccolor-nice-blue` | `#103b66` | **Never referenced** |\n| `--ccolor-solid-yellow` | `rgb(255,225,70)` | **Never referenced** |\n\n#### `:root` Block — Nested Rules (lines 14–35) ⚠️\nThe `:root` block **contains nested element/class selectors**:\n```less\n:root {\n  * { z-index: 0; }\n  .red-box { ... }\n  .blue-box { ... }\n  .border-box { ... }\n  .dotted-box { ... }\n}\n```\n- **LESS compiles this to** `:root *`, `:root .red-box`, etc. — technically valid CSS (descendants of `<html>`), functionally equivalent to top-level, but a **structural anti-pattern**.\n- `* { z-index: 0 }` — **global z-index reset on every element**. This is extremely aggressive and likely causes stacking-context bugs throughout the site.\n- `.red-box`, `.blue-box`, `.border-box`, `.dotted-box` — **no elements in `index.html` use any of these classes**. Dead code.\n\n#### `body` (lines 37–46)\n```less\nbody {\n  background-color: azure;\n  color: #666;\n  font-family: roboto, helvetica, arial, san-serif, serif;\n  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;\n  height: inherit;\n  min-width: 800px;\n  margin: 0;\n  -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;\n}\n```\n- **`min-width: 800px`** — forces horizontal scroll on any viewport < 800px. **Kills mobile.**\n- **`height: inherit`** — `<body>` inherits from `<html>` which has no explicit height. Effectively `auto`. Pointless.\n- **`san-serif`** — typo (should be `sans-serif`). Falls through to `serif`.\n- **Bootstrap override:** replaces Bootstrap's `body` font-family, color, and margin.\n- The compiled `personal-touch.css` version **adds** `display: inline-flex; justify-content: space-evenly; align-items: center;` which are **commented out** in the LESS. The two files are out of sync.\n\n#### `#main-content` (lines 48–53)\n```less\n#main-content {\n  position: relative;\n  &.small-version { top: 400px; }\n}\n```\n- **`top: 400px`** — magic number, no responsive adjustment.\n- `.small-version` is added by JS when viewport ≤ 1500px.\n\n#### `.hide` (lines 55–62)\nStandard visually-hidden pattern (clip rect). Used on the nav checkbox `#s2`. **Functional, correct.**\n\n#### Accordion System (lines 64–118)\n| Selector | Purpose |\n|----------|---------|\n| `.accordion-header:hover` | Hover state for nav label |\n| `.accordion-item` / `:last-child` | List item borders |\n| `.accordion-label` | Padding, font-size 18px |\n| `.accordion-child` | **Hidden by default** (`height:0; opacity:0; transform:scale(1,0)`) |\n| `.accordion-child + .small-version` | `max-width: 70vh` |\n| `.accordion-child:hover:not(.dir-arrow)` | `translate: 10% 0px` |\n| `.accordion-child:focus:not(.dir-arrow)` | Green background `#51bc53` |\n\nThis is a **custom accordion** that is **not** Bootstrap's collapse. The HTML uses Bootstrap's `data-bs-toggle="collapse"` for the developer section, but the nav uses this custom checkbox-driven accordion. Two different accordion systems coexist.\n\n#### Checkbox-Driven Nav (lines 120–145)\n```less\nlabel.accordion-header.btn {\n  border: none;  /* Bootstrap btn override */\n  input[type=checkbox]:checked {\n    ~ .accordion-child { ... }\n    ~ .accordion-child.dir-arrow { ... }\n  }\n}\n```\n- **Bootstrap override:** `border: none` on `.btn`.\n- The `~` general sibling combinator drives the nav open/close.\n- `.dir-arrow` — the up/down arrow buttons get special treatment (20% width, black bg, 50% opacity).\n\n#### `.dir-arrow` Shimmer Effect (lines 119–135)\n```less\n.dir-arrow::before {\n  background: linear-gradient(120deg, transparent, #fff, transparent);\n  left: -100%;\n  transition: all .5s ease-in-out;\n}\n.dir-arrow:hover::before {\n  transform: translateX(200%);\n}\n```\n- Decorative shimmer on hover. **Brittle:** depends on `position: absolute` parent, `height: 100%` on a pseudo-element with no explicit height context.\n\n#### `.hazy-black` Overlay (lines 147–165)\n```less\n.hazy-black::before {\n  background-color: #992424;\n  transform: skewX(-20deg) translateY(-5%) translateX(10%);\n  z-index: -110;\n}\n.hazy-black > #nav-back {\n  background-color: fade(#000000, 30%);\n  width: 120%;\n  translate: -5% calc(5% - 5px);\n}\n```\n- **`z-index: -110`** — negative z-index, relies on the global `* { z-index: 0 }` to work.\n- **`width: 120%`** on `#nav-back` — overflows parent.\n- **`translate: -5% calc(5% - 5px)`** — magic offset to compensate for the 120% width.\n- The `::before` creates a **skewed red panel** behind the nav. Purely decorative.\n\n#### `#navbar` (lines 196–210)\n```less\n#navbar {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  left: 10px;\n  min-width: 400px;\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 10%;\n  z-index: -100;\n  & + .small-version { z-index: 100; }\n  #nav-area {\n    align-items: start;\n    justify-content: start;\n    z-index: -200;\n  }\n}\n```\n- **`z-index: -100`** on `#navbar` — **conflicts** with the compiled CSS which has `z-index: 100`. Out of sync.\n- **`min-width: 400px`** — forces nav to be at least 400px wide. On a 375px phone, this overflows.\n- **`top: 10%`** — percentage-based vertical position, not viewport-relative.\n- **`#nav-area { z-index: -200 }`** — even more negative. The compiled CSS has `z-index: 200`. **Direct contradiction between the two files.**\n\n#### `#ham-icon` Hamburger (lines 212–290)\n- 6 `<span>` elements, each 9px tall, 50% wide, positioned at `top: 0/18/36px`.\n- `.open` state rotates spans into an X.\n- **Vendor prefixes:** `-webkit-`, `-moz-`, `-o-` prefixes on every transform/transition. **Unnecessary** for any modern browser. Adds ~40 lines of redundancy.\n- **`width: 60px; height: 45px`** — fixed pixel size, no responsive scaling.\n- **Touch target:** 60×45px is below the 44×44px WCAG minimum on the height axis (barely).\n\n#### `#s-head` (lines 292–330)\n```less\n#s-head {\n  background: linear-gradient(#B79001, yellow, #B79001, #DBB701, black);\n  border: 10px groove rgba(255, 245, 238, .6);\n  color: #580202;\n  margin: 30px auto 10%;\n  min-width: 680px;\n  opacity: .1;\n  padding: 2%;\n}\n```\n- **`opacity: .1`** — header is **90% transparent by default**. Only becomes visible when JS adds `.on-load`. **If JS fails, the header is nearly invisible.**\n- **`min-width: 680px`** — another mobile killer.\n- **`border: 10px groove`** — `groove` border style is non-standard-looking, not used in Bootstrap.\n- **`margin-bottom: 10%`** — percentage margin, viewport-dependent.\n\n#### `#s-head h1` (lines 318–323)\n```less\nh1 {\n  font-weight: 700;\n  padding-left: 150px;\n  padding-top: 10px;\n  font-size: 3.6rem;\n  font-family: 'Titillium Web', sans-serif;\n}\n```\n- **`'Titillium Web'` is never loaded** (no Google Fonts link). Falls back to `sans-serif`.\n- **`padding-left: 150px`** — magic number, no responsive adjustment.\n\n#### `#s-head > h4::before` (lines 325–330)\n```less\ncontent: '\\f0a4';\nfont-family: 'Font Awesome\\ 5 Free', sans-serif;\nfont-size: 3rem;\n```\n- **Font Awesome 5 Free** is referenced, but the site loads **Font Awesome 6.2.1** (line 7 of HTML). The glyph `\\f0a4` (user icon) may render differently or not at all in FA6. **Version mismatch.**\n\n#### `#byline-tag` (lines 332–339)\n```less\nbackground-color: #8e8e8e;\nborder: 4px solid fade(#e5ffff, 50%);\nbox-shadow: rgba(0,0,0,.5) 0px 5px 12px 0px;\ncolor: black;\n```\n- **Contrast:** black text on `#8e8e8e` (medium gray) = **~3.5:1 ratio**. Below WCAG AA (4.5:1) for normal text.\n\n#### `#profile-pic img` (lines 341–347)\n```less\nmax-width: 20vw;\nmax-height: 300px;\nposition: relative;\nz-index: -40;\ntop: 20%;\nright: 100px;\n```\n- **`right: 100px`** — fixed pixel offset.\n- **`z-index: -40`** — negative, relies on global z-index reset.\n- **`top: 20%`** — percentage offset, context-dependent.\n\n#### `#div-developer` (lines 349–430)\n- **`background-color: #0c0c4d`** — dark navy.\n- **`padding: 10px 10%`** — percentage horizontal padding.\n- **`::before { content: 'Software Development' }`** — section title injected via CSS pseudo-element. **Not accessible to screen readers** (pseudo-element content is not reliably read).\n- **`button` styles** — overrides Bootstrap `.btn`:\n  - `font-size: 1.5rem; padding-top/bottom: 5%; margin: 30px; border-width: .7rem`\n  - `:hover` — `translate: 5px 5px`, blue glow\n  - `:focus` — green glow, **`font-size: 1.2rem`** (shrinks on focus — **inverted focus indicator**)\n- **`.work-in-progress`** — `@keyframes fadein` nested inside (LESS compiles to top-level). `font-size: 5rem`, `color: wheat`, `font-variant: all-petite-caps`.\n- **`ol`** — `counter-reset: li`, `list-style: none`, `*list-style: decimal` (**IE6/7 hack, dead**), `font: 15px 'trebuchet MS'` (font not loaded).\n- **`.rectangle-list a`** — complex counter-based numbered list with `::before`/`::after` arrows. **No element in HTML uses `.rectangle-list`.** Dead code.\n\n#### `#div-finance` (lines 432–460)\n- **`::before { content: 'Finance' }`** — same pseudo-element title pattern.\n- **`#highlight-box`** — `position: absolute; width: 15%`. Moved by JS on hover.\n- **`#finance-button-box`** — `position: relative; display: flex`.\n- **`ul li {}`** — **empty rule block.** Dead code.\n\n#### `#div-resume` (lines 462–466)\n```less\nmargin: 20px 10px;\nbackground-color: #ffffff;\npadding: 10px 10%;\n```\n- White background on a site with `azure` body. No `::before` title (unlike other sections).\n\n#### `#div-customer-service` (lines 468–500)\n- **`::before { content: 'Customer Service' }`** — pseudo-element title.\n- **`.carousel { padding: 80px }`** — **Bootstrap carousel override.** 80px padding is very large on mobile.\n- **`.carousel-indicators button { height: 100px; width: 100px }`** — **Bootstrap override.** 100×100px indicators are very large (Bootstrap default is ~20px).\n- **`.carousel-inner .item img { height: 600px }`** — **Fixed 600px height.** No `max-height`, no `width: 100%`, no responsive. On mobile, this overflows.\n- **`ul { justify-content: space-evenly; justify-items: baseline; align-items: baseline; display: inline-flex }`** — `justify-items` is not a flexbox property (it's for grid). **Invalid in this context.**\n\n#### `#div-accomplishments` (lines 502–506)\n```less\nmargin: 20px 10px;\nbackground-color: #0c0c4d;\npadding: 10px 10%;\n```\n- No `::before` title. No specific content styles.\n\n#### `#s-foot` (lines 508–512)\n```less\nmargin: 20px 10px;\nbackground-color: #0c0c4d;\npadding: 10px 10%;\n```\n- Same pattern. No `::before` title.\n\n---\n\n### `personal-touch.css` (Compiled, 377 lines) — Divergence from LESS\n\n| Property | LESS (loaded) | Compiled CSS (dead) |\n|----------|---------------|---------------------|\n| `body` display | *(commented out)* | `inline-flex; justify-content: space-evenly; align-items: center` |\n| `#navbar z-index` | `-100` | `100` |\n| `#nav-area z-index` | `-200` | `200` |\n| `#s-head background` | `linear-gradient(#B79001, yellow, ...)` | `#2d2c41` (solid) |\n| `#s-head color` | `#580202` | `aquamarine` |\n| `#s-head width` | *(not set)* | `80%` |\n| `#s-head margin` | `30px auto 10%` | `2%` + `margin-top: 30px` |\n| `#s-head h1 font-family` | `'Titillium Web'` | *(not set)* |\n| `#s-head h1 font-size` | `3.6rem` | *(not set)* |\n| `#s-head h1 padding-left` | `150px` | *(not set)* |\n\n> The two files have **diverged significantly**. Since only the LESS is loaded, the compiled CSS is dead, but its existence creates confusion about which is authoritative.\n\n---\n\n### `barebones.css` (3 lines)\n```css\n.test-big-square-box { border: 5px solid black; height: 800px; width: 1500px; }\n```\n- **No element uses `.test-big-square-box`.** Entirely dead.\n\n---\n\n### `dropdown-converted.css` (140 lines) & `dropdown-example.sass` (126 lines)\n- A **completely different design system**: green palette (`#58d39f`, `#2eb079`), Futura font, table-based nav layout, 3D perspective dropdown animation.\n- **No markup in `index.html` matches any of these selectors** (`nav li`, `.dropdown`, `.has-dropdown`, `.dropdown-item`).\n- The SASS uses `scale-color()`, `darken()`, `lighten()` — SASS-specific functions.\n- **Both files are entirely dead.** They appear to be a design experiment that was never integrated.\n\n---\n\n### Responsive Breakpoints\n\n**There are zero `@media` queries in any custom CSS/LESS file.**\n\nThe only responsive behavior in the entire site is:\n1. **JS in `index.html`** (line 149): `if (window.innerWidth > 1500)` — opens nav / adds `.small-version`\n2. **`body { min-width: 800px }`** — forces horizontal scroll below 800px\n3. **`#navbar { min-width: 400px }`** — forces nav width\n4. **`#s-head { min-width: 680px }`** — forces header width\n5. **`#div-customer-service .carousel-inner .item img { height: 600px }`** — fixed height\n6. **`#profile-pic img { max-width: 20vw }`** — viewport-relative (only truly responsive rule)\n7. **Bootstrap's own breakpoints** (from CDN) — apply to `.row`, `.col`, `.d-*` utilities\n\n> The site has **no custom responsive design**. It relies on `min-width` constraints and one JS viewport check.\n\n---\n\n### Bootstrap Overrides Summary\n\n| Selector | What's overridden | File |\n|----------|-------------------|------|\n| `body` | font-family, color, background, margin, min-width | LESS |\n| `label.accordion-header.btn` | `border: none` (removes Bootstrap btn border) | LESS |\n| `#div-developer button` | font-size, padding, margin, border-width, hover/focus states | LESS |\n| `#div-customer-service .carousel` | padding (80px) | LESS |\n| `.carousel-indicators button` | height/width (100×100px) | LESS |\n| `.carousel-inner .item img` | height (600px) | LESS |\n| `nav` (in dropdown-converted.css) | display, width, background | **dead file** |\n\n---\n\n### Brittle / Redundant / Dead Code Summary\n\n| Issue | Location | Severity |\n|-------|----------|----------|\n| `* { z-index: 0 }` global reset | LESS `:root` block | **High** — causes stacking bugs |\n| `body { min-width: 800px }` | LESS | **High** — kills mobile |\n| `#s-head { opacity: .1 }` default | LESS | **High** — invisible without JS |\n| `#s-head h1 { font-family: 'Titillium Web' }` | LESS | **Medium** — font never loaded |\n| `#s-head h4::before { font-family: 'Font Awesome\\ 5 Free' }` | LESS | **Medium** — FA6 loaded, FA5 referenced |\n| `#div-customer-service .carousel-inner .item img { height: 600px }` | LESS | **High** — fixed height, no responsive |\n| `#navbar { min-width: 400px }` | LESS | **Medium** — overflows small screens |\n| `#div-developer ol { *list-style: decimal }` | LESS | **Low** — IE6/7 hack |\n| `.rectangle-list` (entire block) | LESS | **Low** — no HTML uses it |\n| `#div-finance ul li {}` empty rule | LESS | **Low** — dead |\n| `#nav-area::after {}` empty rule | Compiled CSS | **Low** — dead |\n| `.hazy-black {}` empty rule | Compiled CSS | **Low** — dead |\n| 6 unused `@layer-*` variables | LESS | **Low** — dead |\n| `@ccolor-yellow` unused | LESS | **Low** — dead |\n| `--ccolor-nice-blue`, `--ccolor-solid-yellow`, `--full-menu-height` unused | LESS `:root` | **Low** — dead |\n| `.red-box`, `.blue-box`, `.border-box`, `.dotted-box` | LESS `:root` | **Low** — no HTML uses them |\n| `barebones.css` (entire file) | separate file | **Low** — dead |\n| `dropdown-converted.css` (entire file) | separate file | **Low** — dead |\n| `dropdown-example.sass` (entire file) | separate file | **Low** — dead |\n| `personal-touch.css` (entire file) | separate file | **Medium** — dead + out of sync |\n| `-webkit-`, `-moz-`, `-o-` prefixes on `#ham-icon` | LESS | **Low** — unnecessary |\n| `justify-items: baseline` in flexbox context | LESS | **Low** — invalid property |\n| `resume.html` `h5 { font-family: 'Raleway' }` | inline style | **Medium** — font not loaded, global scope |\n| `#div-developer button:focus { font-size: 1.2rem }` | LESS | **Medium** — shrinks on focus (inverted) |\n| `#byline-tag` black on `#8e8e8e` | LESS | **Medium** — ~3.5:1 contrast, below AA |\n| `::before { content: '...' }` for section titles | LESS (3×) | **Medium** — not screen-reader accessible |\n| `#main-content.small-version { top: 400px }` | LESS | **Medium** — magic number |\n| `#s-head h1 { padding-left: 150px }` | LESS | **Low** — magic number |\n| `#profile-pic img { right: 100px }` | LESS | **Low** — fixed offset |\n| `#ham-icon` 60×45px | LESS | **Low** — below 44px touch target |\n\n---\n\n### Key Structural Findings for Later Steps\n\n1. **Only `personal-touch-cleaned.less` is active.** All other custom CSS files are dead. The compiled `personal-touch.css` is out of sync and should be deleted or regenerated.\n2. **Zero media queries.** The site has no custom responsive design. Mobile is handled by `min-width` constraints (which break it) and one JS viewport check.\n3. **The `:root` block contains nested rules** — a LESS anti-pattern that compiles to `:root *` etc.\n4. **Global `* { z-index: 0 }`** combined with negative z-indexes (`-100`, `-110`, `-200`, `-40`) creates a fragile stacking system.\n5. **Three section titles are CSS pseudo-elements** (`::before { content: '...' }`) — invisible to screen readers.\n6. **Two fonts are referenced but never loaded** (`Titillium Web`, `Raleway`).\n7. **Font Awesome version mismatch** (FA5 glyph in CSS, FA6 loaded).\n8. **The hamburger icon has ~40 lines of vendor prefixes** that are unnecessary.\n9. **The carousel has a fixed 600px image height** and 100×100px indicators — both will overflow on mobile.\n10. **The `dropdown-*` files are a separate, unused design experiment** (green theme, Futura, 3D dropdown) that can be deleted.\n\nNo files were modified. Ready for Step 4 (inspect JavaScript).	[]	All custom CSS/LESS rules are cataloged with specific selectors, breakpoints, and overrides noted, distinguishing Bootstrap overrides from custom styles.	\N	2026-09-14 10:58:43.281083-04	2026-09-14 11:03:06.349962-04
