n| `js/bootstrap.*.js` (all variants + .map files) | Bootstrap loaded from CDN |\n| `js/myApp.js` | AngularJS stub, not referenced |\n| `js/myCtrl.js` | AngularJS stub, not referenced |\n| `files/` (13 images + duplicate resume.html) | Static assets |\n| `resources/profile.png` | Duplicate image |\n| `README.md` | Documentation |\n| `.git/` | Version control |\n\n### Key Observations for Subsequent Steps\n\n1. **Viewport meta blocks zoom**: `user-scalable=no, maximum-scale=1.0, minimum-scale=1.0` — must be fixed.\n2. **`body { min-width: 800px }`** in the LESS file — forces horizontal scroll on phones.\n3. **`#navbar { min-width: 400px }`** — forces overflow on 360px screens.\n4. **`#s-head { min-width: 680px }`** — forces overflow on small screens.\n5. **`#main-content { width: 90%; margin-left: 15% }`** (inline) — fixed layout assumption.\n6. **JS viewport check** (`$(window).width() > 1500`) — should be replaced with CSS media queries.\n7. **`/js/resumeSection.js`** referenced in `resume.html` does not exist — broken reference (no action needed unless it causes an error).\n8. **No existing media queries** in the LESS file — all responsive work will be additive.\n9. **Carousel images** have `height: 600px` fixed — will overflow on small screens.\n10. **`#profile-pic img { max-width: 20vw; right: 100px }`** — absolute positioning may break on narrow screens.\n\n---\n\n*This is an intermediate step result. Proceeding to Step 2 (detailed HTML analysis) when ready.*	[]	A complete file map is produced listing the main HTML file, all active CSS/LESS files, and all active JS files, with inactive/vendor files explicitly noted as out of scope.	\N	2026-09-14 14:09:58.587079-04	2026-09-14 14:11:17.957507-04
chat-17c66d3d-2cc2-42fb-a46b-71928dda06b1	step-02	Read and analyze the main HTML file	completed	I now have the full content of both HTML files. Let me produce the structured inventory.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2 Result: Responsive-HTML Inventory\n\n### A. Viewport Meta Tag\n\n| Line | Code | Mobile Problem |\n|------|------|----------------|\n| **4** | `user-scalable=no, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=1.0, minimum-scale=1.0` | **Blocks pinch-zoom entirely.** Accessibility violation (WCAG 1.4.4). Users cannot zoom text to readable size. |\n\n### B. Inline Styles on Structural Elements\n\n| Line | Element | Inline Style | Mobile Problem |\n|------|---------|-------------|----------------|\n| **14** | `<body>` | `display: flex; align-items: stretch;` | Flex on body is fine, but combined with nested containers (below) creates a rigid layout that doesn't reflow. |\n| **20** | `<label.accordion-header>` | `margin-left: 20px` | Fixed left offset; minor but adds to cumulative horizontal space. |\n| **22** | `#ham-surround` | `margin: 10%` | Percentage-based, scales OK. No issue. |\n| **24** | `<h3>` "Menu" | `position: absolute; left: 45%; bottom: 00%` | Absolute positioning without a positioned ancestor — placement is unpredictable on narrow screens; may overlap hamburger icon. |\n| **25** | `#menu-up` button | `padding: 4px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto` | Minor; auto margins center within flex. OK. |\n| **32** | `#menu-down` button | `padding: 4px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto` | Same as above. OK. |\n| **34** | `#main-content` | `min-height: 100vh; width: 90%; margin-left: 15%` | **Critical.** Fixed 90%/15% split assumes the nav occupies the left 10%. On a 360px screen the nav's `min-width: 400px` (in LESS) already exceeds the viewport, so the 15% left margin + 90% width pushes content off-screen. |\n| **38** | `#profile-pic` | `position: absolute` | **Critical.** No explicit width/height. Combined with LESS `right: 100px` and `max-width: 20vw`, the image is absolutely positioned and can overlap or escape the content column on narrow screens. |\n| **83** | `#highlight-box` | `height: 5%; min-width: 10px; bottom: -10%; z-index: 10` | `min-width: 10px` is negligible. `bottom: -10%` is relative. Low risk. |\n| **125** | `<h3>` "Certifications" | `color: darksalmon` + class `offset-2` | `offset-2` = `margin-left: 16.67%`. Pushes heading right on mobile. |\n| **129** | `<h3>` "Footnotes" | class `offset-2` | Same as above. |\n\n### C. Bootstrap Offset Classes (Fixed Left Margins)\n\n| Line | Element | Class | Effect | Mobile Problem |\n|------|---------|-------|--------|----------------|\n| **36** | `<h2>` "Welcome" | `offset-4` | `margin-left: 33.33%` | On 360px, pushes heading 120px right — wastes a third of the screen. |\n| **39** | `<h4>` "My name is" | `offset-5` | `margin-left: 41.67%` | On 360px, pushes text 150px right — nearly half the screen is empty. |\n| **125** | `<h3>` "Certifications" | `offset-2` | `margin-left: 16.67%` | Minor push; acceptable but unnecessary on mobile. |\n| **129** | `<h3>` "Footnotes" | `offset-2` | `margin-left: 16.67%` | Same. |\n\n### D. Nested Container / Structural Issues\n\n| Line | Element | Issue | Mobile Problem |\n|------|---------|-------|----------------|\n| **15** | `#body-whole` | `class="container d-flex"` | Bootstrap `container` adds `padding-left/right: 12px` (mobile) or `15px` (≥576px). |\n| **16** | inner div | `class="d-flex container"` | **Second nested `container`** — double padding (24–30px total horizontal). Wastes space on 360px. |\n| **18** | `#nav-area` | `class="col container"` | **Third nested `container`** — triple padding. Also `col` without a number means `flex: 0 0 auto; max-width: 100%`. |\n\n### E. Fixed-Width / Min-Width Constraints (from LESS, applied to these elements)\n\nThese are defined in the LESS file but attach to HTML elements listed here:\n\n| HTML Element (line) | LESS Rule (approx.) | Mobile Problem |\n|---------------------|---------------------|----------------|\n| `#navbar` (line 17) | `min-width: 400px` | **Forces 400px minimum on a 360px screen → horizontal scroll.** |\n| `#s-head` (line 35) | `min-width: 680px` | **Forces 680px minimum → massive horizontal scroll on phones and small tablets.** |\n| `#main-content` (line 34) | (inline) `width: 90%` | Combined with nav's min-width, total exceeds viewport. |\n| `body` (line 14) | `min-width: 800px` | **Forces 800px minimum → horizontal scroll on all phones and most tablets.** |\n| Carousel `img` (lines 102–111) | `height: 600px` | **Fixed 600px height overflows small screens; no `max-height` or responsive height.** |\n| `#profile-pic img` (line 38) | `max-width: 20vw; right: 100px` | `right: 100px` is a fixed pixel offset; on 360px the image is pushed 100px from the right edge, overlapping content. |\n\n### F. Finance Button Row (Lines 82–90)\n\n| Line | Element | Issue | Mobile Problem |\n|------|---------|-------|----------------|\n| **82** | `#finance-button-box` | `d-flex align-items-stretch` with 6 `<li>` children | Six buttons in a single flex row. On 360px each button gets ~60px — text wraps or overflows. No `flex-wrap` class. |\n\n### G. Developer Accordion Buttons (Lines 44–47)\n\n| Line | Element | Issue | Mobile Problem |\n|------|---------|-------|----------------|\n| **44** | `#div-developer` | `row justify-content-between` with three `col` buttons | Three equal-width buttons in a row. On 360px each is ~120px — "HTML/JavaScript" and "SQL/MongoDB" will wrap or overflow. |\n\n### H. Viewport-Size JavaScript (Lines 136–172)\n\n| Line | Code | Mobile Problem |\n|------|------|----------------|\n| **141** | `if ($(window).width() > 1500)` | **Viewport-size check.** Toggles `.small-version` classes on `#s2`, `.menu-item`, `#main-content`, `#navbar`. This is a JS-driven layout switch that should be a CSS media query. Runs once on load; does not respond to resize. |\n| **147–149** | `document.onscroll` → `$('#navbar').css('top', offset)` | Scroll handler sets navbar position. Functional but uses jQuery `.css()` on every scroll event — minor perf concern, not a layout bug. |\n| **151–154** | `indicator(e)` → `marker.css('left', e.offsetLeft); marker.css('width', e.offsetWidth)` | Positions the highlight box under finance buttons. Uses `mouseover` (line 157) — **no touch equivalent**, so the highlight never appears on mobile. Not a layout bug but a dead feature. |\n| **170–172** | `$('#div-resume').load(...)` → sets `#main-content` min-height | Adjusts height after async load. Functional; no responsive issue per se, but the height calc may be wrong if the resume content overflows. |\n\n### I. `resume.html` Fragment (injected into `#div-resume`)\n\n| Line | Element | Issue | Mobile Problem |\n|------|---------|-------|----------------|\n| **5** | `.resume` | `padding-left: 40px` | Fixed 40px left padding. On 360px this is 11% of the screen. |\n| **34** | `#div-education` | `width: 125%; translate: -10% 0; padding-left: 18px; padding-right: 18px` | **Critical.** `width: 125%` overflows the parent by 25%. The `translate: -10% 0` partially compensates but the right edge still extends ~12.5% beyond the parent → **horizontal scroll on all small screens.** |\n| **51** | `<script src="/js/resumeSection.js">` | File does not exist | 404 error in console. No functional impact but indicates a broken reference. |\n\n### J. Bootstrap Classes Already in Use (for reuse in fixes)\n\n| Class | Where Used | Relevance |\n|-------|-----------|-----------|\n| `container` | Lines 15, 16, 18 | Already provides responsive padding; over-nested. |\n| `d-flex` | Lines 15, 16, 82 | Flex utilities already in use. |\n| `row` | Lines 35, 44 | Bootstrap grid row. |\n| `col` | Lines 18, 45, 46, 47 | Grid column (auto-width). |\n| `offset-2/4/5` | Lines 36, 39, 125, 129 | Fixed left offsets — candidates for responsive removal. |\n| `btn btn-primary` | Lines 45–47 | Button styling. |\n| `btn btn-outline-light` | Lines 84–89 | Button styling. |\n| `nav-pills` | Lines 84–89 | Pill styling. |\n| `carousel slide` | Line 94 | Bootstrap carousel. |\n| `d-block w-100` | Lines 102, 105, 108, 111 | Carousel image sizing. |\n| `collapse` | Lines 48, 56, 73 | Bootstrap collapse/accordion. |\n| `text-center` | Lines 40, 74 | Text alignment. |\n| `text-justify` | Line 67 | Text alignment. |\n| `text-start` | Line 20 | Text alignment. |\n| `text-end` | resume.html lines 38–39 | Text alignment. |\n| `visually-hidden` | Lines 115, 119 | Accessibility. |\n| `justify-content-between` | Line 44 | Flex alignment. |\n| `align-items-stretch` | Line 82 | Flex alignment. |\n\n### K. Custom Classes Requiring Responsive Treatment\n\n| Class / ID | Defined In | Needs |\n|------------|-----------|-------|\n| `#navbar` | LESS | Remove `min-width: 400px`; add responsive stacking. |\n| `#s-head` | LESS | Remove `min-width: 680px`; allow natural width. |\n| `#main-content` | Inline + LESS | Replace fixed `width: 90%; margin-left: 15%` with responsive layout. |\n| `#profile-pic` | LESS | Remove `right: 100px`; use responsive positioning. |\n| `.small-version` | LESS + JS | Replace JS toggle with CSS media query. |\n| `.accordion-header` / `.accordion-child` | LESS | Ensure touch targets ≥ 44px. |\n| `.finance-button-item` | LESS | Add `flex-wrap` or responsive sizing. |\n| `.rectangle-list` | LESS | Check for fixed widths. |\n| `.hazy-black` | LESS | Check for fixed dimensions. |\n| `.give-space` | LESS | Check for fixed margins. |\n| `.blue-back` | LESS | Check for fixed dimensions. |\n| `.open` (on `#ham-icon`) | LESS | Check for fixed dimensions. |\n| `.on-load` (on `#s-head`) | LESS | Check for fixed dimensions. |\n| `.dir-arrow` | LESS | Check for fixed dimensions. |\n| `.button-menu` | LESS | Check for fixed dimensions. |\n| `.work-in-progress` | LESS | Check for fixed dimensions. |\n\n### L. Summary of Critical Mobile Blockers (Priority Order)\n\n1. **`body { min-width: 800px }`** (LESS) — forces horizontal scroll on every pho