d role | Current observed state |\n|---|---|---|\n| `inputs/` | Script reads input images from here. | Empty. |\n| `originals/` | Script moves processed input files here. | Contains 14 `.webp` files, including names such as `blue_frog`, `detailed_frog`, `firey_cat`, and `simple_frog`. |\n| `outputs/` | Script writes cropped PNG outputs here. | Contains at least 200 visible `.png` files matching `{base}_logo_{N}.png`; includes many 69-byte files and larger files up to about 1.8 MB. |\n| `outputs - backup/` | Not referenced in `sliceImages.py`. | Contains at least 200 visible `.png` files with the same naming pattern; inferred to be a manual backup or earlier output snapshot. |\n| `.idea/` | JetBrains IDE metadata. | Not part of the script's logic. |\n\n## Inputs and outputs\n\n**Observed:**\n- Input: image files placed in `inputs/` with supported extensions `.png`, `.jpg`, `.jpeg`, and `.webp`.\n- Output: cropped PNG files written to `outputs/` with names such as `{base}_logo_{N}.png`.\n- Side effect: the original input file is moved to `originals/` after processing.\n\n**Inference:**\n- The likely workflow is to place new source images in `inputs/`, run `sliceImages.py`, then review the generated crops in `outputs/` while the source images are retained in `originals/`.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n**Observed imports in `sliceImages.py`:**\n- `cv2` (OpenCV)\n- `numpy`\n- `os`\n- `shutil`\n\n**Inference:**\n- The script requires a Python environment where OpenCV and NumPy are available.\n- No dependency manifest, such as `requirements.txt`, was observed, so exact version requirements are not documented in the project.\n\n## Apparent usage\n\n**Observed:**\n- There is no README, CLI interface, test suite, or dependency manifest at the project root.\n- The script uses fixed relative folders: `inputs/`, `outputs/`, and `originals/`.\n\n**Inference:**\n- The project appears to be used as a simple local batch tool: add images to `inputs/`, execute the Python script, and collect cropped results in `outputs/`.\n- `outputs - backup/` appears to be a manually maintained copy of earlier or alternative outputs.\n\n## Uncertainties\n\n- The exact visual intent of the generated images was not verified by inspecting image contents.\n- The purpose of `outputs - backup/` is inferred from its name and contents; it is not referenced by the script.\n- Many 69-byte PNG files were observed in `outputs/`, but their visual content was not inspected; they may be very small or near-empty crops.\n- No setup instructions, version pins, or usage documentation were present, so usage details are inferred from the script and folder structure.\n```\n\n**Verification for this step:** the draft covers purpose, main script, folders, inputs/outputs, dependencies, apparent usage, and uncertainties; it labels observed facts versus inferences; and it avoids unsupported setup commands or invented behavior.	[]	Draft content is complete, distinguishes facts from inferences, and contains no fabricated setup steps or behavior.	\N	2026-09-14 17:08:49.587097-04	2026-09-14 17:11:32.412728-04
