chat-49ce4d7f-cb2d-4416-9f30-cd08d73d3fd2	step-05	Select the recommended discard	completed	## Step 5 Result: Recommended Discard\n\n**Recommended discard: South wind (南 / S)**\n\n**Justification:** Among the four structurally identical top-tier discards (East, South, North, 4-man — all preserving 4-shanten with 71 ukeire), South is the safest to discard (an honor tile that is neither the round wind nor our seat wind, carrying only 1,000-pt yakuhai value) and the least valuable to retain, making it the optimal choice with zero offensive cost.\n\n---\n\n### Decision Summary\n\n| Factor | South (chosen) | East | North | 4-man |\n|--------|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|\n| Shanten | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 |\n| Ukeire | 71 | 71 | 71 | 71 |\n| Safety | **Safest** | Moderate | Safe | Riskiest |\n| Value to retain | **Lowest** (1,000-pt) | 2,000-pt (round wind) | 2,000-pt (seat wind) | Flexible number tile |\n| Posture fit | Offense ✓ | Offense ✓ | Offense ✓ | Offense ✓ |\n\n**Why South over the others:**\n- **vs. East:** East is the round wind — all four players may be targeting it for a 2,000-pt yakuhai. Discarding it is marginally more dangerous.\n- **vs. North:** North is our seat wind (2,000-pt if paired). Slightly more useful to keep than South.\n- **vs. 4-man:** A middle number tile that could fill a ryanmen or kanchan wait for any opponent. Highest deal-in risk of the four.\n\n**Why not a second/third-tier discard (7m, 9s, 7s, 3p, 7p, 6m, 3s, 4s, 4p, 6p):**\nEach of these sacrifices 4–8 ukeire tiles (dropping from 71 to 67 or 63) for no safety benefit, since they are number tiles (more dangerous to discard) and break or weaken an existing taatsu.\n\n**Durable fact for Step 6:** The recommended discard is **South wind (南)**. The reasoning chain is: all discards are 4-shanten → top tier (E/S/N/4m) maximizes ukeire at 71 → South is safest and least valuable among those four → offense posture confirmed by East 3 mid-round context with no visible danger.\n\n*This is an intermediate step result