e remaining backend core in D:\\\\\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\\\\\Code Projects\\\\\\\\cors-dummy\\\\\\\\backend\\\\\\\\app\\\\\\\\. (1) Create upstream_client.py: a safe relay client that takes a ServiceEntryConfig + request path, validates the path against allowed_path_prefixes, makes an HTTP request with explicit timeout, enforces max response bytes, forwards only safe headers (never cookies/authorization by default), and returns a structured result. (2) Create probe_trace.py: a ProbeTrace dataclass/factory that assigns a trace id (uuid4), records mode (direct|relay), target service name, origin decision (if applicable), HTTP status, failure class, and duration_ms; provides a to_response_headers() method for a harmless X-Probe-Trace header and a to_dict() for JSON metadata. (3) Create app_factory.py: a create_app(settings) function that constructs the FastAPI instance, wires CORSMiddleware using OriginContract.allowed_origins_for_cors_middleware() and allow_credentials(), and registers all routes. No import-time network or DB side effects. (4) Implement routes: GET /health (liveness), GET /config-summary (non-secret config: mode, origin count, service names, timeout, max bytes — never secrets), GET /probe/direct-info (returns info about direct-probe support: which services are browser-probeable), POST /relay/{service_name}/{path:path} (validates service exists, path is allowed, performs relay via upstream_client, wraps result in ProbeTrace). (5) Replace the old main.py entry point with a thin module that calls create_app(get_settings()) and runs uvicorn. Do NOT modify origin_contract.py or settings.py (they are complete). Do NOT touch legacy files (flask_main.py, dynamic-scripts.py, alembic/, database.py, models.py, crud.py, schemas.py) in this unit — that is the next unit's job.\\",\\"verify\\":\\"Run: python -c 'from app.app_factory import create_app; from app.settings import get_settings; app=create_app(get_settings()); print([r.path for r in app.routes])' — must show /health, /config-summary, /probe/direct-info, /relay/{service_name}/{path:path}. Run: python -c 'from app.upstream_client import relay_request; from app.probe_trace import ProbeTrace; print(ProbeTrace.__dataclass_fields__.keys())' — must show trace_id, mode, service, status, failure_class, duration_ms. Confirm no import-time DB connection by running the app factory with no PostgreSQL available.\\",\\"scope_items\\":[]},{\\"name\\":\\"Backend cleanup, legacy isolation, and discriminating test suite\\",\\"instruction\\":\\"In D:\\\\\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\\\\\Code Projects\\\\\\\\cors-dummy\\\\\\\\backend\\\\\\\\: (1) Move legacy files (flask_main.py, dynamic-scripts.py, database.py, models.py, crud.py, schemas.py, alembic/, alembic.ini, app/alembic/, app/tests/sql.py) into a backend/legacy/ subdirectory. Add a backend/legacy/README.md explaining what each file was and why it is preserved. (2) Rewrite requirements.txt to contain only: fastapi, uvicorn, httpx (or requests), pydantic, pydantic-settings. Remove psycopg2, sqlalchemy, alembic. (3) Create backend/.env.example with all supported env vars documented (CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS, CORS_DEV_MODE, SERVICE_REGISTRY, UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS, UPSTREAM_MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES, APP_HOST, APP_PORT) with safe defaults and comments. (4) Write a comprehensive pytest test suite in backend/tests/ (new __init__.py, conftest.py, test_origin_contract.py, test_settings.py, test_upstream_client.py, test_app_factory.py, test_relay_routes.py): prove allowed-origin returns 200 with correct headers; disallowed-origin returns 403 with reason code; dev-mode wildcard allows any origin; empty allowlist in production denies all; service registry validation (unknown service → 404, disallowed path prefix → 403); relay timeout produces a structured failure (mock httpx); bounded response size is enforced; /health returns 200 without DB; /config-summary does not leak secrets; no arbitrary URL relay is possible (test that a service with base_url pointing to an internal address still only allows configured prefixes). Every test must be discriminating: it must fail if the corresponding requirement is not met. Use httpx.MockTransport or respx for upstream mocking. Do NOT start a long-lived server.\\",\\"verify\\":\\"Run: cd backend && python -m pytest tests/ -v --tb=short — all tests must pass. Confirm: grep -r 'psycopg2\\\\\\\\|sqlalchemy\\\\\\\\|alembic' requirements.txt returns nothing. Confirm: ls legacy/ shows the moved files. Confirm: cat .env.example shows all documented vars. Confirm: no test uses echo/no-op as evidence — each test asserts specific HTTP status codes, header values, or JSON fields.\\",\\"scope_items\\":[]},{\\"name\\":\\"Frontend rebuild: diagnostic UI, port fix, and tests\\",\\"instruction\\":\\"In D:\\\\\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\\\\\Code Projects\\\\\\\\cors-dummy\\\\\\\\frontend\\\\\\\\: (1) Fix the Vite/Playwright port mismatch: update playwright.config.js baseURL to http://localhost:4665 and webServer.port to 4665 (matching vite.config.js server.port). (2) Rebuild the Vue 3 UI around the CORS diagnostic model: create src/stores/probeLedger.js (Pinia store holding an array of ProbeRecord objects: {id, mode:'direct'|'relay', service, path, origin, status, failureClass, durationMs, timestamp, traceId}); create src/components/ServicePanel.vue (lists configured services from /config-summary, shows name, base URL, allowed prefixes, probeable flag); create src/components/ProbeForm.vue (select service, enter path, choose direct or relay mode, submit); create src/components/ProbeLedger.vue (table of ProbeRecord entries with color-coded status, mode badge, latency, failure reason); create src/components/OriginStatus.vue (shows current origin decision from backend); rewrite src/views/HomeView.vue to compose these components; remove HelloWorld.vue, TheWelcome.vue, WelcomeItem.vue, and the counter store. (3) Use project-owned CSS custom properties (define in src/assets/main.css or a dedicated theme.css): --probe-success, --probe-failure, --probe-pending, --surface, --text-primary, --text-muted, --border, --radius, --font-mono for trace IDs. Distinctive but restrained: semantic color coding, monospace trace IDs, clear mode badges. No UI kit dependency. (4) Write Vitest unit tests: src/stores/__tests__/probeLedger.spec.js (add record, clear, filter by mode/status); src/components/__tests__/ProbeLedger.spec.js (renders records, shows correct status colors). (5) Write a bounded Playwright e2e smoke test in e2e/smoke.spec.js: navigate to the app, verify the service panel renders, submit a relay probe against a mock (or verify the form is present and interactive). The e2e test must not require external kh22 services. (6) Ensure pnpm build succeeds (vite build). Do NOT add new npm dependencies beyond what is already in package.json.\\",\\"verify\\":\\"Run: cd frontend && pnpm build — must succeed with no errors. Run: cd frontend && pnpm test:unit — all unit tests pass. Run: cd frontend && npx playwright test --project=chromium e2e/smoke.spec.js — smoke test passes (or is skipped with a clear reason if browser unavailable). Confirm: grep '5173' playwright.config.js returns nothing. Confirm: ls src/components/ shows ServicePanel.vue, ProbeForm.vue, ProbeLedger.vue, OriginStatus.vue and does NOT show HelloWorld.vue. Confirm: src/stores/probeLedger.js exists and counter.js is removed.\\",\\"scope_items\\":[]},{\\"name\\":\\"Documentation, final build, and discriminating verification\\",\\"instruction\\":\\"In D:\\\\\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\\\\\Code Projects\\\\\\\\cors-dummy\\\\\\\\: (1) Rewrite the root README.md to describe: the finished current architecture (Vue 3 frontend + FastAPI backend with Origin Contract, Service Registry, Probe Trace, safe relay), the two probe modes (direct and relay), the security model (no wildcard production CORS, no open proxy, bounded upstream reads, no secret forwarding), exact setup instructions (backend: pip install -r requirements.txt, set env vars from 