tically, imports via importlib.import_module(f\\\\\\"app.endpoints.{stem}\\\\\\") catching any exception into EndpointDiscoveryError naming the module, validates a single `router` attr of type fastapi.APIRouter (missing/wrong type -> raise naming the module), extracts routes skipping methods=None (Mount/WebSocket), detects duplicate (method,path) collisions naming both modules and the conflicting route, and returns a list sorted by module_name. No eval/exec, no DB, no step-3+ code.\\",\\"verify\\":\\"File exists and imports standalone (`from app.endpoints.loader import discover_endpoints, EndpointDiscoveryError, DiscoveredEndpoint` with backend/ on sys.path); source contains no `eval(` or `exec(`; a quick import smoke-check succeeds.\\",\\"scope_items\\":[]},{\\"name\\":\\"Write and run the loader test suite\\",\\"instruction\\":\\"Write backend/tests/test_endpoint_loader.py covering all 10 settled cases (valid module discovered; _private.py and __init__.py ignored; missing router export raises naming module; import failure raises naming module; two modules same method+path raises naming both; same path GET vs POST allowed; zeta/alpha/mid order -> alpha,mid,zeta; non-existent dir raises; empty dir -> []; source scan has no eval/exec). Apply fixture hygiene: delete temp .py files after each test, purge sys.modules entries for app.endpoints.*, and ensure sys.path includes backend/ before importing the loader. Run pytest until green.\\",\\"verify\\":\\"`pytest backend/tests/test_endpoint_loader.py -v` reports all tests passing (discriminating: a deliberately malformed/duplicate fixture must fail); ZIP SHA-256 remains 94911aa0e7eca739bbac2a671f32251139387b20f6a49f220fa5ab2cc31b5340; no long-lived server left running.\\",\\"scope_items\\":[]}],\\"merge_requirements\\":[\\"The owning parent must confirm all three step-2 units are green before advancing to step 3 (app factory, core metadata route, example endpoints); step-3+ work must not leak into step-2.\\",\\"The owning