ate detection, sorted output.\\",\\n    \\"Smoke check script (_smoke_check.py) written to exercise discovery with a temp module and verify missing-dir error.\\",\\n    \\"Backup ZIP verified intact (9162 entries, testzip passes, 33.5 MB).\\",\\n    \\"Self-scan blocker identified and root-caused via live execution (EndpointDiscoveryError: 'loader' does not export a 'router' attribute).\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\"remaining_units\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"name\\": \\"Fix self-scan conflict in loader.py\\",\\n      \\"instruction\\": \\"Edit backend/app/endpoints/loader.py to add a self-skip guard in _candidate_stems (or in the discover_endpoints loop) so that the loader's own module stem is excluded from discovery. The guard should compare the candidate stem against the current module's own stem (e.g., Path(__file__).stem or a module-level constant). Add a brief comment explaining why. Do not change any other behavior. Verify by running: py -3.12 -c \\\\\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, r'D:\\\\\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\\\\\Code Projects\\\\\\\\cors-dummy\\\\\\\\backend'); from pathlib import Path; from app.endpoints.loader import discover_endpoints; res = discover_endpoints(Path(r'D:\\\\\\\\LOCAL_Share\\\\\\\\Code Projects\\\\\\\\cors-dummy\\\\\\\\backend\\\\\\\\app\\\\\\\\endpoints')); print([e.module_name for e in res])\\\\\\" — this should print an empty list (no other endpoint modules exist yet) without raising.\\",\\n      \\"verify\\": \\"discover_endpoints called on the real endpoints/ directory returns an empty list (no error) because loader.py is now self-excluded. The file still lives at backend/app/endpoints/loader.py. No other behavioral changes.\\",\\n      \\"scope_items\\": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"name\\": \\"Write and run loader tests\\",\\n      \\"instruction\\": \\"Create backend/tests/__init__.py (zero-byte) and backend/tests/test_loader.py. Tests must cover: (1) discovery of two valid endpoint modules in a temp directory returns both sorted by name; (2) a 