chat-db565993-1068-4237-8a90-1905ec45a0bb	step-06	Infer tomorrow from the corrected model and synthesize the final answer	completed	{"schema_version": 2, "kind": "step_result", "status": "completed", "task_id": "chat-db565993-1068-4237-8a90-1905ec45a0bb", "step_id": "step-06", "request_type": "conclusion", "command_category": "task", "content": "# SPY Calibration & Tomorrow Forecast — Final Synthesis\\n\\n## 1. What Was Corrected (and Why)\\n\\nThe prior model produced a mild 752–759 grind because of five compounding assumptions: a hard speed cap (~2 pts/day, \\"no single-session move >1.5%\\"), the F2/F3 bid treated as a holding floor, M3/M4 excluded from driving speed, sub-750 paths quarantined behind a discrete-shock precondition, and no support-break acceleration branch.\\n\\nThree allowed corrections — each justified by ex-ante evidence already in the frozen pre-move set — produced a model that reproduces today's realized path:\\n\\n| Correction | Ex-ante justification (no hindsight) |\\n|---|---|\\n| Remove hard speed cap → **conditional speed on structure** | F4 progressive weakening (each bounce weaker) + price at lower range + no structural support below 756 (F5+F6) |\\n| Reclassify F2/F3 from **holding floor → failing/reactive bid** | Two small-bodied up-signals vs four aligned down-signals; failing-bid reading is more consistent with the structure |\\n| Make **M3/M4 continuous speed drivers** (not discrete-event-only) | M3/M4 are ongoing conditions; the raw set's own A14/A11/B1 already contain the fast-break mechanic |\\n\\n**Corrected model's forecast for today:** open ~758–759 → break 756–757 in first 1–2 hrs → fast flush below 750 (low ~749) in first 2–3 hrs → M1 reactive dip-buy → rebound to ~753–755 → close ~754. **This matches the realized scorecard** (sub-750 break, brief, rebound to ~754.10).\\n\\n## 2. Diagnosis (Error Classification)\\n\\n| Error type | Contribution | What had to change |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Model-structure** (primary) | No acceleration branch + hard speed cap | Add conditional speed; remove cap |\\n| **Weighting** (secondary) | F2/F3 over-weighted as a floor against four down-signals | Reclassify as failing/reactive |\\n| **Synthesis-selection** (contributing) | Fast-break paths (A14, A11/B1) demoted to subsumed/Alt-4 | Promote sub-750 to a primary/major branch |\\n| **Perception** (limited) | Outcome-chart wick resolution (2.50 gridline spacing at 709×1536 px) | Not a causal error in ex-ante reasoning; isolated to scorecard verification |\\n\\n## 3. Tomorrow's Forecast (Sep 18) — From the Corrected Model\\n\\n**Starting state:** SPY closed 754.10. The 756–757 support is broken and now overhead resistance. The sub-750 low (~749) is the reactive bid's catch zone. M3/M4 continuous pressure is still present. Price is at the lower range of the Sep 3–16 window.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Primary Path: Continued Weakness with Reactive Bid Floor\\n\\n| Element | Detail |\\n|---|---|\\n| **Open** | ~753–754 (flat to slight gap down from 754.10) |\\n| **Morning (first 2–3 hrs)** | Drifts lower through 752–753; tests the 749–750 zone (today's low) |\\n| **Midday/Afternoon** | Reactive bid (M1) catches at ~749–750; weak rebound to 752–753 |\\n| **Close** | **~751–753** |\\n| **Intraday range** | 749–754 |\\n| **Speed** | Moderate — not a fast flush (the 756–757 break already happened; this is a continuation below broken support), but not a slow grind either (M3/M4 continuous pressure + no structural support between 754 and 749) |\\n| **Shape** | Down → catch at 749–750 → weak rebound → close below the rebound high |\\n\\n**Why this is NOT mechanically extra bearish:** The corrected model's reactive bid is real (it caught today). The primary path assumes it catches again at 749–750. The close is slightly lower than today (751–753 vs 754.10) because the bid is getting exhausted over consecutive days of M3/M4 pressure, and the 756–757 resistance caps any upside. This is the natural continuation of the corrected model's assumptions, not a penalty.\\n\\n**Confirmation:** SPY closes below 754 on Sep 18 AND hits 750 or below intraday.\\n**Invalidation:** SPY closes above 756 on Sep 18 (reclaims broken support) OR SPY does not reach 750 intraday (bid holds higher than expected).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Bullish Reversal / M1 Proactive\\n\\n- **Trigger:** SPY opens above 756 (reclaims broken support) OR rallies to 757+ in the first hour\\n- **Path:** 754 → 757 → 760; close 758–761\\n- **Mechanism:** M1 is stronger than the corrected model assumed — the bid is proactive, not just reactive. M3/M4 are overridden by a positive macro surprise (dovish data, foreign buying resumption).\\n- **Invalidation of this alt:** SPY fails to close above 756 on Sep 18\\n- **Corrected-model probability:** Low — the ex-ante evidence (small-bodied candles, four down-signals) is more consistent with a failing/reactive bid than a proactive one.\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Deeper Break / Bid Fails\\n\\n- **Trigger:** SPY breaks below 749 (today's low) and does not recover within 30 minutes\\n- **Path:** 754 → 749 → 746–748; close 746–749\\n- **Mechanism:** The reactive bid is exhausted after two consecutive days of M3/M4 pressure. The corrected model's acceleration logic applies: once the 749–750 support breaks, the next leg is faster (no counter-pressure below). M3/M4 continuous pressure drives the extension.\\n- **Invalidation of this alt:** SPY holds above 749 on Sep 18\\n- **Corrected-model probability:** Moderate — the bid is weak (small-bodied, low conviction) and has been tested once already. Two consecutive tests may exhaust it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Single Most Important State Variable / Level\\n\\n**The 749–750 zone (today's low).** This is the only structural support below the current price. Its behavior determines the primary vs. Alternative 2:\\n\\n- **Holds** → Primary path plays out (close 751–753)\\n- **Fails** → Alternative 2 activates (close 746–749, faster next leg per the corrected model's acceleration logic)\\n\\nThe 756 level (broken support, now resistance) is the secondary level: a close above it invalidates the entire bearish structure and shifts probability to Alternative 1.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Falsifiability Summary\\n\\n| Path | Falsified if (Sep 18) |\\n|---|---|\\n| **Primary** | SPY closes above 756 OR does not reach 750 intraday |\\n| **Alt-1** | SPY fails to close above 756 |\\n| **Alt-2** | SPY holds above 749 |\\n| **Key level** | 749–750: check against the realized intraday low |\\n\\nAll assumptions are from the corrected model's ex-ante logic (conditional speed, failing/reactive bid, continuous M3/M4). No new catalyst was introduced. No hindsight language is used. The forecast is specific, falsifiable, and grounded in the corrected model that successfully reproduced today's realized path.", "artifacts": [], "verification_requirement": "The step output contains a primary tomorrow sequence with timing and levels, 1-2 alternatives, concrete invalidations, and the single most important state variable/level. The forecast is specific and falsifiable, with no hindsight language. The final answer synthesizes the completed prior work into the direct user-facing answer.", "evidence_count": 7, "resource_status": {"context_state": "full", "message": "full context", "unresponsive_connections": []}}	[]	The step output contains a primary tomorrow sequence with timing and levels, 1-2 alternatives, concrete invalidations, and the single most important state variable/level. The forecast is specific and falsifiable, with no hindsight language. The final answer synthesizes the completed prior work into the direct user-facing answer.	\N	2026-09-16 21:05:35.874739-04	2026-09-16 21:13:53.428482-04
