chat-a75c8e0b-516d-4e77-932e-0ee779c79575	step-03	Read source and config files	completed	{"schema_version": 2, "kind": "step_result", "status": "completed", "task_id": "chat-a75c8e0b-516d-4e77-932e-0ee779c79575", "step_id": "step-03", "request_type": "step", "command_category": "task", "content": "All source and config files have been read. Here is the durable step-03 result:\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Step 03 complete — All source and config files read and analyzed.**\\n\\n## Project Purpose\\n\\nA minimal Go HTTP backend API providing read-only access to a PostgreSQL database. It exposes:\\n- A health-check endpoint\\n- A customer lookup by ID (from a `customers` table)\\n- A list of database schemas (from `information_schema.schemata`)\\n- A list of tables with optional schema/name/limit filters (from `information_schema.tables`)\\n\\nBuilt entirely on the standard `net/http` package — no web framework.\\n\\n## Directory Structure (confirmed from files read)\\n\\n```\\ngoBackend/\\n├── main.go                        ← GoLand IDE template (prints \\"Hello gopher\\"), NOT the server\\n├── cmd/\\n│   └── server/\\n│       └── main.go                ← Actual server entry point (CORS, routing, startup)\\n├── internal/\\n│   ├── config/\\n│   │   └── config.go              ← Env-var config loader (DATABASE_URL, PORT)\\n│   ├── db/\\n│   │   └── db.go                  ← pgxpool creation + ping\\n│   └── handlers/\\n│       ├── health.go              ← App struct, New(), /health handler\\n│       ├── customers.go           ← /api/customers?id=N handler\\n│       ├── schemas.go             ← /api/schemas handler\\n│       └── tables.go              ← /api/tables?schema=&name=&limit= handler\\n├── .env                           ← DATABASE_URL (masked), PORT=12245\\n├── go.mod / go.sum\\n└── .idea/                         ← GoLand IDE config (not runtime-relevant)\\n```\\n\\n## Environment Variables (names only, values masked)\\n\\n| Variable | Required | Default | Purpose |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `DATABASE_URL` | **Yes** (fatal if missing) | — | PostgreSQL connection string (host, port, user, password, dbname, sslmode) |\\n| `PORT` | No | `8080` | HTTP listen port (`.env` sets it to `12245`) |\\n\\n## HTTP Routes\\n\\n| Method | Path | Query Params | Description |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| GET | `/health` | — | Returns `{\\"status\\":\\"ok\\"}` |\\n| GET | `/api/customers` | `id` (int, required) | Returns `{id, name, email}` from `customers` table |\\n| GET | `/api/schemas` | — | Returns `{schemas: [...]}` from `information_schema.schemata` |\\n| GET | `/api/tables` | `schema`, `name` (ILIKE), `limit` (int, random order) | Returns `[{schema, name}]` from `information_schema.tables` |\\n\\n## CORS Allowed Origins (hardcoded in `cmd/server/main.go`)\\n\\n- `http://kh24.boga-dace.ts.net:3000` / `:5173`\\n- `http://khzz.boga-dace.ts.net:3000` / `:5173`\\n- `http://localhost:3000` / `:5173`\\n\\n## Run Instructions (derived from code)\\n\\n```bash\\n# 1. Ensure .env exists with DATABASE_URL and PORT\\n# 2. Run the server:\\ngo run ./cmd/server\\n\\n# Or build first:\\ngo build -o goBackend ./cmd/server\\n./goBackend\\n```\\n\\n## Notable Observations\\n\\n- The root `main.go` is a **GoLand IDE template** (prints \\"Hello gopher\\"), not part of the server. The real entry point is `cmd/server/main.go`.\\n- All dependencies in `go.mod` are marked `// indirect` — suggests `go mod tidy` has not been run since the imports were added.\\n- No Dockerfile, docker-compose, Makefile, or `.env.example` present.\\n- No test files (`*_test.go`) present.\\n- The `.env` file contains a live `DATABASE_URL` with credentials — **value masked in this report**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n*This is an intermediate result for step 04 (draft README) and step 05 (write README). All five required sections (purpose, structure, dependencies, config/env vars, run instructions) are now identified from actual file contents.*", "artifacts": [], "verification_requirement": "All relevant files are read; project purpose, structure, env vars (names only, no values), and run commands are identified.", "evidence_count": 19, "resource_status": {"context_state": "full", "message": "full context", "unresponsive_connections": []}}	[]	All relevant files are read; project purpose, structure, env vars (names only, no values), and run commands are identified.	\N	2026-09-16 19:32:34.922336-04	2026-09-16 19:34:04.905037-04
chat-a75c8e0b-516d-4e77-932e-0ee779c79575	step-04	Draft README.md content	completed	{"schema_version": 2, "kind": "step_result", "status": "completed", "task_id": "chat-a75c8e0b-516d-4e77-932e-0ee779c79575", "step_id": "step-04", "request_type": "step", "command_category": "task", "content": "{\\n  \\"schema_version\\": 2,\\n  \\"kind\\": \\"step_result\\",\\n  \\"status\\": \\"completed\\",\\n  \\"task_id\\": \\"chat-a75c8e0b-516d-4e77-932e-0ee779c79575\\",\\n  \\"step_id\\": \\"step-04\\",\\n  \\"request_type\\": \\"step\\",\\n  \\"command_category\\": \\"task\\",\\n  \\"content\\": \\"**Step 04 complete — README.md draft composed.**\\\\n\\\\nDraft for `D:/LOCAL_Share/Code Projects/goBackend/README.md`:\\\\n\\\\n# goBackend\\\\n\\\\n## Purpose\\\\n\\\\ngoBackend is a small Go HTTP API that provides read-only access to a PostgreSQL database. It uses the standard `net/http` package and a `pgx` connection pool.\\\\n\\\\nEndpoints:\\\\n- `GET /health`\\\\n- `GET /api/customers?id=<int>`\\\\n- `GET /api/schemas`\\\\n- `GET /api/tables?schema=<schema>&name=<substring>&limit=<int>`\\\\n\\\\nThe server also includes CORS middleware with a hardcoded allowlist for local and private frontend origins.\\\\n\\\\n## Directory structure\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\ngoBackend/\\\\n├── main.go                  # GoLand IDE template; not the server entry point\\\\n├── cmd/\\\\n│   └── server/\\\\n│       └── main.go          # Server entry point: loads .env, config, DB pool, routes, CORS\\\\n├── internal/\\\\n│   ├── config/\\\\n│   │   └── config.go        # Reads DATABASE_URL and PORT\\\\n│   ├── db/\\\\n│   │   └── db.go            # Creates and pings pgxpool\\\\n│   └── handlers/\\\\n│       ├── health.go        # App struct and /health handler\\\\n│       ├── customers.go     # /api/customers handler\\\\n│       ├── schemas.go       # /api/schemas handler\\\\n│       └── tables.go        # /api/tables handler\\\\n├── .env                     # Local environment configuration\\\\n├── go.mod\\\\n├── go.sum\\\\n└── .idea/                   # GoLand IDE settings\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Dependencies\\\\n\\\\nModule: `goBackend`\\\\nGo version: `1.26`\\\\n\\\\nRuntime libraries imported by source:\\\\n- `github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 v5.9.1` — PostgreSQL driver and `pgxpool`\\\\n- `github.com/joho/godotenv v1.5.1` — `.env` loading\\\\n\\\\nSupporting modules present in `go.mod` / `go.sum`:\\\\n- `github.com/jackc/pgpassfile v1.0.0`\\\\n- `github.com/jackc/pgservicefile v0.0.0-20240606120523-5a60cdf6a761`\\\\n- `github.com/jackc/puddle/v2 v2.2.2`\\\\n- `golang.org/x/sync v0.17.0`\\\\n- `golang.org/x/text v0.29.0`\\\\n\\\\nNote: `go.mod` currently lists all modules as indirect; running `go mod tidy` may reclassify directly imported modules.\\\\n\\\\n## Configuration / environment variables\\\\n\\\\n| Variable | Required | Default | Description |\\\\n|---|---:|---:|---|\\\\n| `DATABASE_URL` | Yes | None | PostgreSQL connection string. The server exits if this is missing. |\\\\n| `PORT` | No | `8080` | HTTP listen port. |\\\\n\\\\nThe repository includes a local `.env` file. Keep real credentials out of version control.\\\\n\\\\n## Build, run, and test\\\\n\\\\nPrerequisites: Go `1.26` or newer and a reachable PostgreSQL database.\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\n# Run directly\\\\ngo run ./cmd/server\\\\n\\\\n# Build a binary\\\\ngo build -o goBackend ./cmd/server\\\\n./goBackend\\\\n\\\\n# Run tests (no *_test.go files are currently present)\\\\ngo test ./...\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nExample health check:\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\ncurl http://localhost:8080/health\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nIf `PORT` is set, replace `8080` with that port.\\\\n\\\\nVerification: The draft contains the five required sections — purpose, directory structure, dependencies, configuration/environment variables, and build/run/test — and contains no secret values.\\\\n\\\\nThis is an intermediate result for step 05 (write README.md).\\",\\n  \\"artifacts\\": [],\\n  \\"verification_requirement\\": \\"Draft covers all five required sections and contains no secret values.\\",\\n  \\"evidence_count\\": 0,\\n  \\"resource_status\\": {\\n    \\"context_state\\": \\"full\\",\\n    \\"message\\": \\"full context\\",\\n    \\"unresponsive_connections\\": []\\n  }\\n}", "artifacts": [], "verification_requirement": "Draft covers all five required sections and contains no secret values.", "evidence_count": 19, "resource_status": {"context_state": "full", "message": "full context", "unresponsive_connections": []}}	[]	Draft covers all five required sections and contains no secret values.	\N	2026-09-16 19:34:05.012931-04	2026-09-16 19:37:20.943602-04
