s drawn from C2 (4 paths), C3 (4 paths), C5-B3 (1 path), C4 (3 paths), C6 (2 paths). Remaining paths (B7, B9, B13, B4, B15, B2, B6, B8, B10, B11, B14, B5, B12, A7, A12, A8, A14) are subsumed into the 5 alternatives or the primary as near-duplicates with preserved attribution.\\n- **No path dropped without accounting.** Near-duplicates merged with mechanism attribution preserved.\\n- **5 distinct alternatives retained** (each has a unique distinguishing trigger that cannot be satisfied by the primary or by another alternative).\\n\\n*Intermediate result only — not the final answer. Ready for step-04 (draft synthesis markdown).*", "artifacts": [], "verification_requirement": "Primary path has explicit SPY/QQQ levels, timing, confirmation, and invalidation; alternatives are distinct and each has a distinguishing evidence trigger.", "evidence_count": 2, "resource_status": {"context_state": "full", "message": "full context", "unresponsive_connections": []}}	[]	Primary path has explicit SPY/QQQ levels, timing, confirmation, and invalidation; alternatives are distinct and each has a distinguishing evidence trigger.	\N	2026-09-16 19:51:40.228238-04	2026-09-16 19:54:16.723364-04
