onfirm?** | 6 focus views per candidate, cross-view agreement 0.0–1.0 | All derived views identical to original; no new information | **AGREE** — no view reveals a lower endpoint |\\n| **High-confidence candidates (3–9)** | y_end 646–740 → price ~703.5–705.2 | Consistent with visible wick tips in that range | **AGREE** — these are clearly visible wicks |\\n| **Low-confidence candidates (1, 2, 10)** | y_end 833–840 → price ~700.7–700.9 | Not visible as wick tips; likely body-fill bottoms | **DISAGREE** — vision does not confirm these as wick endpoints |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Disagreement Detail\\n\\nThe geometric analyzer's **lowest** endpoints (candidates 1, 2, 10 at y=833–840) are precisely the ones with the **lowest confidence**:\\n- Candidate 1 (x=552): focus_confidence=0.6839, cross_view_agreement=**0.167**, status=\\"supported\\"\\n- Candidate 2 (x=510): focus_confidence=0.6173, cross_view_agreement=**0.0**, status=\\"uncertain\\"\\n- Candidate 10 (x=232): focus_confidence=0.5474, cross_view_agreement=**0.0**, status=\\"uncertain\\"\\n\\nThe vision model's read of ~702 is consistent with the **high-confidence** geometric candidates (y=675–740, mapping to ~703.5–705.2) plus the visible wick extension below the body. The ~0.6–1.2 unit gap between the two methods is concentrated entirely in the low-confidence candidates.\\n\\n**Most likely explanation:** The geometric analyzer is detecting the **bottom edge of the broad fill** (candle body boundary at y≈833–841) as the \\"wick endpoint\\" because the thin trace pixel column continues to that depth. The vision model correctly identifies that the **visible wick tip** (where the thin line actually terminates as a distinct feature) is higher, at ~y=765 (price ~702). The fill bottom is not the wick tip.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step Status\\n\\n✅ **PASS** — `vision_image` returned `ok=true` with original + 5 derived views. Reconciliation explicitly notes:\\n- **Agreement:** derived views don't change the read; high-confidence candidates (y=646–740) are consistent with visible wicks\\n- **Disagreement:** lowest endpoints (y=833–840 → 700.7–700.9) are NOT confirmed by vision; vision reads the low at ~701.5–702.0; interpretation of \\"thin trace through fill\\" differs (occlusion vs. normal rendering)\\n\\nThis is an intermediate result for step 5 (price estimation at the strongest wick endpoints). No final conclusion is drawn.", "artifacts": [], "verification_requirement": "vision_image returns ok=true with at least the original and one derived view; the reconciliation explicitly notes agreement or disagreement between vision and geometric analysis, with specific pixel/price references.", "evidence_count": 9, "resource_status": {"context_state": "full", "message": "full context", "unresponsive_connections": []}}	[]	vision_image returns ok=true with at least the original and one derived view; the reconciliation explicitly notes agreement or disagreement between vision and geometric analysis, with specific pixel/price references.	\N	2026-09-16 23:49:08.483248-04	2026-09-16 23:54:12.779571-04
