o:\\n\\n```text\\ny ≈ 765 – 795\\n```\\n\\nThe vision model explicitly did **not** confirm the geometric `y = 833–840` endpoints as visible wick tips. It interpreted those lower pixels more likely as broad fill/body-bottom regions rather than true wick endpoints.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Reconciled Step-5 Estimate\\n\\nBecause the geometric and vision evidence disagree, the estimate is reported as a range rather than forcing agreement:\\n\\n```text\\nReconciled lowest-wick estimate: ~701.4\\nUncertainty range: 700.8 – 702.0\\nApproximate uncertainty: ±0.6 price units\\n```\\n\\nBreakdown:\\n\\n| Evidence source | Estimated low | Interpretation |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| Geometric thin-trace endpoints | **700.77 – 700.88** | Lowest pixel-level trace/fill-bottom candidates |\\n| Vision-supported visible wick tip | **701.5 – 702.0** | Lowest visually confirmed wick tip |\\n| Reconciled estimate | **~701.4** | Midpoint of the two evidence bands |\\n| Combined uncertainty range | **700.8 – 702.0** | Reflects geometric-vision disagreement |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Uncertainty Drivers\\n\\n1. **Geometric vs. vision disagreement**\\n   - Geometric low: `700.77–700.88`\\n   - Vision low: `701.5–702.0`\\n   - Gap: approximately `0.6–1.1` price units\\n\\n2. **Low cross-view agreement for the lowest geometric candidates**\\n   - Candidate 1: `0.167`\\n   - Candidate 2: `0.0`\\n   - Candidate 10: `0.0`\\n   - These are the candidates that produce the `700.77–700.88` estimate, so their price contribution is less certain.\\n\\n3. **Gridline interpolation**\\n   - The low lies between the `700.00` and `702.00` gridlines.\\n   - One pixel is only `~0.0164` price units, so pure pixel localization error is small.\\n   - The dominant uncertainty is semantic: whether the lowest detected pixels are true wick tips or fill/body boundaries.\\n\\n4. **JPEG artifact probability**\\n   - Overall artifact fraction: `0.000846`\\n   - This is negligible and does not materially widen the price uncertainty.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step-5 Durable Result\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"step_id\\": \\"step-05\\",\\n  \\"status\\": \\"completed\\",\\n  \\"pixel_to_price_mapping\\": \\"price = 700.00 + (887 - y) / 61.083\\",\\n  \\"gridline_spacing\\": {\\n    \\"px_per_2_units\\": 122.17,\\n    \\"px_per_1_unit\\": 61.083,\\n    \\"price_units_per_px\\": 0.0164\\n  },\\n  \\"strongest_geometric_low_endpoints\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"candidate\\": 1,\\n      \\"x\\": 552,\\n      \\"y_end\\": 836,\\n      \\"refined_y_end\\": 836,\\n      \\"estimated_price\\": 700.84,\\n      \\"focus_scan_status\\": \\"supported\\",\\n      \\"cross_view_agreement\\": 0.167\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"candidate\\": 2,\\n      \\"x\\": 510,\\n      \\"y_end\\": 833,\\n      \\"refined_y_end\\": 833,\\n      \\"estimated_price\\": 700.88,\\n      \\"focus_scan_status\\": \\"uncertain\\",\\n      \\"cross_view_agreement\\": 0.0\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"candidate\\": 10,\\n      \\"x\\": 232,\\n      \\"y_end\\": 840,\\n      \\"refined_y_end\\": 840,\\n      \\"estimated_price\\": 700.77,\\n      \\"focus_scan_status\\": \\"uncertain\\",\\n      \\"cross_view_agreement\\": 0.0\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\"vision_supported_visible_low\\": {\\n    \\"range\\": [701.5, 702.0],\\n    \\"approx_y_range\\": [765, 795]\\n  },\\n  \\"reconciled_estimate\\": {\\n    \\"best_estimate\\": 701.4,\\n    \\"range\\": [700.8, 702.0],\\n    \\"uncertainty\\": \\"±0.6 price units\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"uncertainty_sources\\": [\\n    \\"geometric vs vision disagreement\\",\\n    \\"low cross-view agreement for the lowest geometric candidates\\",\\n    \\"ambiguity between wick tip and broad fill/body bottom\\",\\n    \\"sub-gridline interpolation between 700.00 and 702.00\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\"directional_forecast\\": false\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThis is an intermediate step result for step 6, not the final user-facing synthesis.", "artifacts": [], "verification_requirement": "The estimated price and uncertainty range for the lowest wick endpoint are stated, derived solely from the visible axis/grid and the current image's pixel data, with no reference to prior task conclusions.", "evidence_count": 9, "resource_status": {"context_state": "full", "message": "full context", "unresponsive_connections": []}}	[]	The estimated price and uncertainty range for the lowest wick endpoint are stated, derived solely from the visible axis/grid and the current image's pixel data, with no reference to prior task conclusions.	\N	2026-09-16 23:54:12.882719-04	2026-09-16 23:58:23.901166-04
chat-ed0880fd-fdcf-46b9-b6ac-1b9ca7affbf6	step-06	Synthesize the blind perception validation conclusion and structured JSON	completed	{"schema_version": 2, "kind": "step_result", "status": "completed", "task_id": "chat-ed0880fd-fdcf-46b9-b6ac-1b9ca7affbf6", "step_id": "step-06", "request_type": "conclusion", "command_category": "task", "content": "## Blind Perception Validation — Final Conclusion\\n\\n### (a) Does any thin trace genuinely continue through a broad same-color fill?\\n\\n**Yes — the visual pattern is confirmed by both methods, but the interpretation differs.**\\n\\nThe geometric analyzer detected 10 candidates where a thin vertical trace of the same color family continues through a broad same-color fill. Six of these have high confidence (≥0.93) and full cross-view agreement (1.0 across all six preprocessing variants). The vision model independently confirmed: \\"thin vertical red lines that are the same red hue as the broad candle bodies… they run from the candle's high down through the body region and out the bottom.\\"\\n\\n**However, the two methods disagree on what this means semantically:**\\n- **Geometric analyzer:** labels this \\"thin_trace_continues_through_broad_same_color_fill\\" — an occlusion relationship where the trace is inferred to be behind the fill (z=0 vs z=1).\\n- **Vision model:** interprets this as **normal wick-over-body rendering** — the standard chart drawing convention where a wick line is drawn on top of its own candle body. It explicitly states: \\"This is not evidence of a separate, hidden wick continuing deeper behind the fill.\\"\\n\\nThe visual fact (thin same-color line passes through the broad fill) is not in dispute. The dispute is whether this represents a genuinely occluded wick or simply the normal rendering of a visible wick.\\n\\n### (b) Does this change the observed intraday low versus a naive whole-image read?\\n\\n**Yes, but by a modest amount, and the exact magnitude is uncertain.**\\n\\n- **Naive body-only read** (ignoring thin traces within fills): lowest broad-fill bottom ≈ 702.5–703.0 (vision estimate of fill bottoms).\\n- **Occlusion-aware read** (including thin traces): lowest wick tip ≈ 701.5–702.0 (vision) or 700.7–700.9 (geometric, low-confidence candidates).\\n- **Net shift:** approximately **0.1–0.5 price units lower** than the naive read.\\n\\nThe shift is real but not dramatic. It is not a \\"hidden wick\\" extending far below the visible bodies. It is the modest extension of wick tips below the body boundary that would be missed by a body-only edge-detection approach. The geometric analyzer's lowest endpoints (y=833–840) are precisely the ones with the **lowest confidence** (cross-view agreement 0.0–0.167), and the vision model does not confirm those as visible wick tips. The most likely explanation is that the geometric analyzer is detecting the **bottom edge of the broad fill** (candle body boundary) as the trace endpoint, while the true visible wick tip is slightly higher.\\n\\n### (c) Estimated key low with uncertainty\\n\\n| Evidence source | Estimated low | Basis |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| Geometric (pixel-level, low-confidence candidates) | 700.77–700.88 | y=833–840, cross-view agreement 0.0–0.167 |\\n| Vision (3 independent calls) | 701.5–702.0 | At/just below the 702.00 gridline |\\n| **Reconciled estimate** | **~701.4** | Midpoint of the two evidence bands |\\n| **Uncertainty range** | **700.8 – 702.0** | ±0.6 price units |\\n\\nThe dominant uncertainty is **semantic** (whether the lowest detected pixels are true wick tips or fill/body boundaries), not pixel-localization error (1 px ≈ 0.016 price units). JPEG artifact probability is negligible (0.000846).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Structured JSON\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"perception_status\\": \\"completed_with_uncertainty\\",\\n  \\"estimated_key_low\\": {\\n    \\"best_estimate\\": 701.4,\\n    \\"range\\": [700.8, 702.0],\\n    \\"uncertainty\\": \\"±0.6 price units\\",\\n    \\"geometric_estimate\\": \\"700.77-700.88 (candidates 1,2,10 at y=833-840, low cross-view agreement)\\",\\n    \\"vision_estimate\\": \\"701.5-702.0 (3 independent calls, at/just below 702.00 gridline)\\",\\n    \\"reconciliation\\": \\"Geometric and vision disagree by ~0.6-1.0 units; the gap is concentrated in the 3 lowest-confidence geometric candidates which vision does not confirm as visible wick tips\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"candidates\\": [\\n    {\\"id\\": 1, \\"color\\": \\"red\\", \\"x\\": 552, \\"y_start\\": 649, \\"y_end\\": 836, \\"refined_y_end\\": 836, \\"focus_scan_status\\": \\"supported\\", \\"focus_confidence\\": 0.6839, \\"cross_view_agreement\\": 0.167, \\"whole_pane_percentile\\": 94.564},\\n    {\\"id\\": 2, \\"color\\": \\"red\\", \\"x\\": 510, \\"y_start\\": 651, \\"y_end\\": 833, \\"refined_y_end\\": 833, \\"focus_scan_status\\": \\"uncertain\\", \\"focus_confidence\\": 0.6173, \\"cross_view_agreement\\": 0.0, \\"whole_pane_percentile\\": 92.743},\\n    {\\"id\\": 3, \\"color\\": \\"red\\", \\"x\\": 530, \\"y_start\\": 484, \\"y_end\\": 675, \\"refined_y_end\\": 675, \\"focus_scan_status\\": \\"high_confidence\\", \\"focus_confidence\\": 0.9996, \\"cross_view_agreement\\": 1.0, \\"whole_pane_percentile\\": 99.919},\\n    {\\"id\\": 4, \\"color\\": \\"red\\", \\"x\\": 529, \\"y_start\\": 484, \\"y_end\\": 655, \\"refined_y_end\\": 675, \\"focus_scan_status\\": \\"high_confidence\\", \\"focus_confidence\\": 0.999, \\"cross_view_agreement\\": 1.0, \\"whole_pane_percentile\\": 99.781},\\n    {\\"id\\": 5, \\"color\\": \\"green\\", \\"x\\": 577, \\"y_start\\": 615, \\"y_end\\": 740, \\"refined_y_end\\": 740, \\"focus_scan_status\\": \\"high_confidence\\", \\"focus_confidence\\": 1.0, \\"cross_view_agreement\\": 1.0, \\"whole_pane_percentile\\": 100.0},\\n    {\\"id\\": 6, \\"color\\": \\"red\\", \\"x\\": 551, \\"y_start\\": 648, \\"y_end\\": 735, \\"refined_y_end\\": 735, \\"focus_scan_status\\": \\"supported\\", \\"focus_confidence\\": 0.6839, \\"cross_view_agreement\\": 0.167, \\