d | 4 ambiguous/occluded data geometry |\\n\\n**Critical difference from prior run:** The high-profile analyzer places the primary pane bottom at **y=841**, not y=887. The y=887 line appears in horizontal consensus (max_length=690) but is NOT classified as reference geometry.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Reference vs Data Objects\\n\\n**Reference (constant coordinate) objects:**\\n| Object | Y | Role |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Overnight line (709.18) | y=298 | Labeled price anchor |\\n| Current price line (704.69) | y=514.5 | Labeled price anchor |\\n| Gridline 712.00 | y≈165 | Price grid |\\n| Gridline 702.00 | y≈644.5 | Price grid |\\n| Pane bottom boundary | y=841 | Pane separator (NOT a price anchor) |\\n\\n**Data objects (10 occlusion candidates):**\\n| ID | Color | X | Y_start | Y_end | Cross-view | Focus conf | Classification |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | red | 552 | 649 | 836 | 0.167 | 0.684 | **REJECTED** (volume bar) |\\n| 2 | red | 510 | 651 | 833 | 0.0 | 0.617 | **REJECTED** (volume bar) |\\n| 3 | red | 530 | 484 | 675 | 1.0 | 0.9996 | **CONFIRMED** (wick) |\\n| 4 | red | 529 | 484 | 675 | 1.0 | 0.999 | **CONFIRMED** (wick) |\\n| 5 | green | 577 | 615 | 740 | 1.0 | 1.0 | **CONFIRMED** (wick) |\\n| 6 | red | 551 | 648 | 735 | 0.167 | 0.684 | **REJECTED** (volume bar) |\\n| 7 | red | 530 | 559 | 675 | 1.0 | 0.980 | **CONFIRMED** (wick) |\\n| 8 | green | 622 | 566 | 661 | 1.0 | 0.987 | **CONFIRMED** (wick) |\\n| 9 | blue | 575 | 613 | 646 | 1.0 | 0.928 | **CONFIRMED** (wick) |\\n| 10 | red | 232 | 808 | 840 | 0.0 | 0.547 | **REJECTED** (volume bar) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Vision Image Results (6 views: original + 5 zoomed/focus crops)\\n\\nThe vision model examined the original image and 4x/8x zoomed crops of the disputed region and reported:\\n\\n> **1. Thin trace below the broad red fill? NO.** The only thin vertical red trace is at the **top** of the broad red fill, running **upward** into the price-pane background. The bottom edge of the broad red fill is the lowest red pixel — it terminates flat on the volume pane's 0 baseline. There is **no** separate thin red line continuing below the fill.\\n\\n> **2. Candle body or volume bar? VOLUME BAR.** The broad red region sits in the volume pane (0/100 axis), is a wide rectangle resting on the 0 baseline, and y≈833–840 maps below the 700 gridline — outside the price pane.\\n\\n> **3. Thin red wick below the fill in the original? NO.** The red simply ends at the bottom of the broad fill. No thin red line bridges from the bottom of the fill downward.\\n\\n> **4. Comparison with green at x≈577.** Same structure: thin green line at top (wick) stacked above broad green fill (volume bar). Normal wick-over-bar alignment.\\n\\n> **5. Edge vs interior line? NEITHER.** The thin vertical red line is the **candle wick from the price pane above**, a separate element that appears stacked on the volume bar because both share the same x-column.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Geometric vs Vision Reconciliation\\n\\n| Aspect | Geometric Analyzer | Vision Model | Resolution |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Disputed region (x≈510-552, y≈833-840) | \\"thin_trace_continues_through_broad_same_color_fill\\" | Volume bar in volume pane; thin trace is wick ABOVE | **Vision correct.** The geometric analyzer conflated two separate objects (wick + volume bar) in the same x-column and color family into a single occlusion relationship. |\\n| Cross-view agreement for disputed candidates | 0.0–0.167 (very low) | Not confirmed as wick tips | **Consistent.** Low cross-view agreement signals the geometric detection is unreliable. |\\n| High-confidence candidates (y=675, 740) | 1.0 agreement, conf ≥0.98 | Confirmed as normal wick-over-body | **Agreement.** Both methods confirm these are genuine wick endpoints. |\\n| Pane bottom | y=841 (high-profile) | y≈820-850 | **Consistent.** The disputed region (y=833-840) is at or below the pane boundary. |\\n\\n**Explicit disagreement:** The geometric analyzer's \\"occlusion\\" label for candidates 1, 2, 6, 10 is a **false positive**. The thin trace and broad fill are NOT in an occlusion relationship — they are separate objects (wick in price pane, volume bar in volume pane) that happen to share color and x-column. The vision model correctly identifies this.\\n\\n**Per cheat sheet rule 8:** I do NOT average the two. The disputed candidates are classified **REJECTED** based on:\\n- Vision's pixel-level identification of the region as a volume bar\\n- The geometric analyzer's own low cross-view agreement (0.0–0.167)\\n- The high-profile analyzer placing pane bottom at y=841 (the disputed pixels are at/below this boundary)\\n- The redraw test (below) confirming the volume-bar interpretation reproduces the pixels\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Price Conversion (Using Fresh Axis Transform from Step-03)\\n\\n**Mapping:** `price(y) = 709.18 − (y − 298) × 0.020715`\\n\\n**Confirmed wick endpoints (price pane only):**\\n\\n| Candidate | X | Y_end | Price | Confidence |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 5 (green) | 577 | 740 | **700.02** | 1.0 |\\n| 3 (red) | 530 | 675 | 701.37 | 0.9996 |\\n| 4 (red) | 529 | 675 | 701.37 | 0.999 |\\n| 7 (red) | 530 | 675 | 701.37 | 0.980 |\\n| 8 (green) | 622 | 661 | 701.66 | 0.987 |\\n| 9 (blue) | 575 | 646 | 701.97 | 0.928 |\\n\\n**Rejected (volume bars, NOT price data):**\\n| Candidate | X | Y_end | Would-be price | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 (red) | 552 | 836 | 698.04 | REJECTED — volume bar |\\n| 2 (red) | 510 | 833 | 698.10 | REJECTED — volume bar |\\n| 6 (red) | 551 | 735 | 700.13 | REJECTED — volume bar |\\n| 10 (red) | 232 | 840 | 697.95 | REJECTED — volume bar |\\n\\n**Estimated key low: ≈700.0** (from green candle wick endpoint at y=740, x=577)\\n\\n**Uncertainty:** ±0.3 price units (y=735–745 range → 699.8–700.2). The dominant uncertainty is whether the green wick tip is exactly at y=740 or ±5px.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Redraw/Reconstruction Sanity Check\\n\\n**Proposed decomposition for the disputed region (x≈510-552):**\\n1. **Price pane (y≈154-740):** Red candle body (y≈484-649) + red wick (y≈484-675, thin 1-2px line)\\n2. **Volume pane (y≈740-841):** Red volume bar (broad rectangle, y≈649-840, ~229px wide)\\n3. **Background:** Lavender/white pane background\\n\\n**Can this reproduce the original pixels?**\\n- ✅ The thin red wick line in the price pane: reproduced by object 1\\n- ✅ The broad red rectangle in the volume pane: reproduced by object 2\\n- ✅ The shared x-column and color: both objects are red, same x-range\\n- ✅ The flat bottom edge at y≈840: volume bar resting on 0 baseline\\n- ✅ No thin red line below y≈840: nothing in the decomposition extends below the volume bar\\n- ✅ The green candle at x=577 shows the same structure: wick (y=615-740) + volume bar (broad fill)\\n\\n**Verdict:** The decomposition **reproduces the original pixels** without requiring a \\"hidden wick\\" or occlusion relationship. The prior run's interpretation (thin trace continuing through broad fill as a hidden wick) is **not needed** to explain the pixels.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Prior Run Failure Diagnosis\\n\\n| Error | Detail |\\n|---|---|\\n| **Axis calibration** | Anchored pane bottom y=887 to price 700.00 (forbidden by gate rule 1). Correct: 700.00 is at y≈741. |\\n| **Object misidentification** | Treated volume bars (y≈833-840) as price wick endpoints. They are volume data, not price data. |\\n| **Occlusion false positive** | Accepted the geometric analyzer's \\"thin_trace_continues_through_broad_same_color_fill\\" label without verifying whether the trace and fill are actually in an occlusion relationship or just co-located in the same x-column. |\\n| **Result** | Concluded ~701.4 (range 700.8-702.0) based on invalid axis + misidentified objects. Correct estimate: **≈700.0** (range 699.8-700.2). |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Structured JSON (Step-04 Output)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"axis_anchors\\": {\\n    \\"overnight_709_18\\": {\\"y\\": 298.0, \\"source\\": \\"labeled_tag+geometric\\"},\\n    \\"current_704