w test confirms this decomposition reproduces the original pixels without requiring an occlusion relationship.\\n\\n### Geometric vs. Vision Disagreement\\n\\n| Aspect | Geometric Analyzer | Vision Model | Resolution |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Disputed region x≈510–552, y≈833–840 | \\"thin_trace_continues_through_broad_same_color_fill\\" (occlusion) | Volume bar in volume pane; thin trace is wick above | **Vision correct.** Geometric false positive. Candidates 1, 2, 6, 10 REJECTED. |\\n| High-confidence wicks (y=646–740) | Cross-view 1.0, conf ≥0.93 | Confirmed as normal wick-over-body | **Agreement.** Both methods concur. |\\n\\nPer cheat sheet rule 8, the two were NOT averaged. The disputed candidates are classified REJECTED based on vision's pixel-level identification, the geometric analyzer's own low cross-view agreement (0.0–0.167), and the redraw test.\\n\\n### Prior Run Failure Diagnosis\\n\\n1. **Axis calibration error:** Anchored pane bottom y=887 to price 700.00 (forbidden by gate rule 1). Correct: 700.00 is at y≈741.\\n2. **Object misidentification:** Treated volume bars (y≈833–840) as price wick endpoints. They are volume data in a separate pane.\\n3. **Occlusion false positive accepted:** The geometric analyzer's \\"thin trace through fill\\" label was accepted without verifying whether the trace and fill are actually in an occlusion relationship or merely co-located in the same x-column.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Structured JSON\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"axis_anchors\\": {\\n    \\"overnight_709_18\\": {\\"y\\": 298.0, \\"source\\": \\"labeled_tag + geometric_consensus_1.0\\"},\\n    \\"current_704_69\\": {\\"y\\": 514.75, \\"source\\": \\"labeled_tag + geometric_consensus_1.0\\"},\\n    \\"gridline_712\\": {\\"y\\": 165.0, \\"residual_px\\": 3.1},\\n    \\"gridline_702\\": {\\"y\\": 644.5, \\"residual_px\\": -0.1}\\n  },\\n  \\"axis_mapping\\": \\"price(y) = 709.18 - (y - 298) * 0.020715\\",\\n  \\"axis_residuals\\": {\\n    \\"712.00\\": {\\"predicted_y\\": 161