pt/residuals.\\n- **Gate rule violated:** Rule 5 (anchors must be `{visible_price, y_coordinate, association_evidence}`) and Rule 7 (NO PARTIAL PASS).\\n- **Corrected conclusion:** The wick endpoint was physically **below** the 750.00 gridline. The application readout (749.60) confirms this. The \\"above 750\\" interpretation is a calibration error, not a market-thesis error.\\n- **Standing lesson (from `SPY_20260916_GROUND_TRUTH_CORRECTION.md`):** When a crosshair/selection supplies an explicit candle OHLC readout, use that as authoritative. Geometry is a consistency/debugging problem, not a competing estimate.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. Counterfactual Audit Summary (prior task steps 2–3)\\n\\nThe prior 32-path experiment (persisted in `SPY_20260916_32_hypotheticals.md` and `SPY_QQQ_20260916_32_hypotheses_synthesized.md`) was built on:\\n- Starting reference: ~757–759 close, pre-market ~759–760\\n- Support zone: 748–750 (treated as a floor that held)\\n- Resistance: 765–770\\n- Horizon: through Sep 18 close\\n- Macro hypotheses M1–M4 as test inputs\\n\\n**What the actual outcome revealed:**\\n- Sep 16 low was 749.60 (below the assumed 750 floor) — the floor was **broken intraday** then reclaimed (close 751.24).\\n- Sep 17 rallied to ~762.44 by 12:10 ET — a ~12.8-point move from the low, far exceeding the \\"steady grind\\" paths.\\n- The prior paths that assumed 750 as a hard floor (A2, A3, etc.) were structurally too narrow; the paths that assumed a V-reversal (A3) were directionally correct but underestimated the speed/magnitude.\\n\\n**Method failures (not stochastic variance):**\\n1. **Axis calibration error:** Misread the low as above 750, eliminating the sub-750 dip-buy scenario from the constraint set.\\n2. **Floor rigidity:** Treated 750 as a hard structural floor rather than a testable level that could break and reclaim.\\n3. **Speed underestimation:** No path captured a >10-point single-day rally from a sub-750 low.\\n4. **Missing interaction:** The dip-buying mechanism (M1) was underweighted relative to the bearish-continuation paths (M2/M3/M4).\\n\\n**Useful old assumptions (preserved):**\\n- The 765–770 resistance zone remains relevant for upside targets.\\n- The multi-day horizon (Sep 17–18) is the correct practical window.\\n- The 7-field path structure (sequence, levels, timing, confirmation, invalidation, mechanism, constraint variation) is sound.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 4. Corrected Constraint/Method Set (carried forward to steps 2–8)\\n\\n| ID | Constraint | Rationale |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **C1** | Sep 16 15:15 low = **749.60** (application readout). Any path referencing the Sep 16 low must use 749.60, not a geometric estimate. | Ground truth outranks geometry. |\\n| **C2** | Sep 16 close = 751.24; the low was **reclaimed** intraday (close > low by 1.64 pts). The 750 level is a **tested-and-reclaimed** zone, not a hard floor. | Corrects the \\"floor held\\" assumption. |\\n| **C3** | Sep 17 actual: SPY reached ~762.44 by 12:10 ET. The forward state for new paths is **~762**, not ~757–759. | Corrects the starting reference. |\\n| **C4** | Axis gate: numeric `{price, y}` anchors required; semantic positions are insufficient. No partial passes. | Prevents recurrence of the calibration error. |\\n| **C5** | 750.00 is a **psychological/tested level**, not a structural wall. Paths must include scenarios where it breaks again and scenarios where it holds as support. | Corrects floor rigidity. |\\n| **C6** | Speed allowance: a >10-point single-session move from a sub-750 low is **plausible** given the observed Sep 17 rally. Paths must not cap daily range at 2–3 points. | Corrects speed underestimation. |\\n| **C7** | Horizon: Sep 17 (remainder) through Sep 18 close, matching the prior 32-path experiment structure. | Preserves comparability. |\\n| **C8** | Starting reference for forward paths: **~762.44** (Sep 17 12:10 ET level). Resistance: 765–770. Support: 758–760 (prior resistance turned support), then 755, then 750. | Corrects the starting state. |\\n| **C9** | Macro hypotheses M1–M4 remain test inputs; M1 (buying pressure) is now **confirmed** by the Sep 17 rally and should be weighted higher in path generation. | Updates weighting based on outcome. |\\n| **C10** | No hindsight targeting: paths are generated from the corrected current state (~762) forward; the Sep 17 rally is **input context**, not a target to be re-forecast. | Prevents circular reasoning. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 5. Evidence Artifacts (persisted, not re-run)\\n\\n| Artifact | Path | Role |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Prior source chart | `C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\SPY_recast_20260917_0730.jpg` | Sep 16 chart (morphology reference only; 749.60 is ground truth) |\\n| Outcome chart | `C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\norm images\\\\SPY_followup_actual_20260917-1139.jpg` | Sep 17 actual development (~762.44 by 12:10 ET) |\\n| Ground truth correction | `C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\docs\\\\SPY_20260916_GROUND_TRUTH_CORRECTION.md` | Authoritative OHLC + failure audit |\\n| Axis gate | `C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\docs\\\\CHART_AXIS_GATE.md` | Corrected perception contract |\\n| Vision cheatsheet | `C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\docs\\\\CHART_VISION_CHEATSHEET.md` | Reusable perception rules |\\n| Prior 32-path set | `C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\docs\\\\SPY_20260916_32_hypotheticals.md` | Structure/horizon reference |\\n| Prior synthesis | `C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\docs\\\\SPY_QQQ_20260916_32_hypotheses_synthesized.md` | Constraint/level reference |\\n\\n**No image analysis was re-run in this step.** All conclusions above are drawn from the persisted durable artifacts of `chat-0bceef52-c02c-461b-8214-1a91bff83fe2` steps 1–4 and the ground-truth correction document.\\n\\n---\\n\\n*This is an intermediate durable result for steps 02–08. It is not the final user-facing answer.*", "artifacts": [],