chat-b9144782-08a2-4db5-be1f-8a2b797163ee	step-04	Vision cross-check all four images against machine output	completed	{"schema_version": 2, "kind": "step_result", "status": "completed", "task_id": "chat-b9144782-08a2-4db5-be1f-8a2b797163ee", "step_id": "step-04", "request_type": "step", "command_category": "task", "content": "Now I have the vision observations for all four images. Let me compile the cross-check comparison against the machine outputs from steps 2-3.\\n\\n## Step-04 Durable Result: Vision Cross-Check of All Four Images\\n\\n### Vision Observations vs. Machine Output\\n\\n| Image | Machine Pane Bottom | Vision-Identified Bottom Boundary | Consistent? |\\n|-------|--------------------|---------------------------------|-------------|\\n| SPY 30m HA | y=547 (5/5 support, 1.0 consensus, len=560) | \\"Thin, full-width horizontal divider separating the price pane from the first oscillator\\" | ✅ Yes |\\n| QQQ 30m HA | y=547 (5/5 support, 1.0 consensus, len=560) | \\"Thin full-width divider separating the price pane from the first oscillator\\" | ✅ Yes |\\n| SPY 15m | y=440 (4/5 support, 0.8 consensus, len=410) | \\"Thin full-width divider separating the price pane from the first sub-pane (dense green/red bar strip, 100→0 scale)\\" — **below all gridlines** | ⚠️ **Discrepancy** |\\n| SPY 1h | y=486 (5/5 support, 1.0 consensus, len=412) | \\"Thin full-width divider separating the price pane from the first sub-pane (green/red bar histogram, 10→0 scale)\\" | ✅ Yes |\\n\\n### Detailed Discrepancy Analysis: SPY 15m\\n\\n**Vision identifies:**\\n- Price gridlines (partial-width) at levels: 776, 772, 768, 764, 760, 756\\n- Dotted current-price line at 758.89\\n- The pane separator is a **full-width structural divider BELOW all gridlines**\\n- The first sub-pane below contains \\"dense green/red vertical bars, 100→0 scale\\" (a separate oscillator/volume pane)\\n\\n**Machine selected:**\\n- y=440, max_length=410 (58% of 708px width), 4/5 variant support\\n- Step-03 analysis identified this as the **760.00 price gridline** (coincident with the last-price tag)\\n\\n**The discrepancy:** The vision model clearly places the pane separator **below** the 756.00 gridline (the lowest visible gridline). The machine selected y=440, which corresponds to the 760.00 gridline — an in-pane price level line, not the structural divider. The true separator should be at a y position below all gridlines, consistent with the y=578 (len=327) or y=670 (len=549) candidates in the consensus table.\\n\\n**Mechanism confirmed by vision:** The y=440 line is partial-width (410px out of 708px), matching the vision description of gridlines as \\"partial-width (stop at the axis gutter).\\" The true separator is described as \\"full-width\\" — consistent with the y=670 candidate (549px, the longest in the separator region) being the structural divider, partially occluded by the oscillator content below.\\n\\n### Wick/Trace Ambiguity (All Four Images)\\n\\nVision observations:\\n- **All four images:** Wicks in the bottom third of the price pane approach horizontal gridlines and vertical time-gridlines, creating visual wick-vs-gridline ambiguity.\\n- **SPY 30m HA:** Wicks near 751.00 gridline; thin MA lines trace close to wicks.\\n- **QQQ 30m HA:** Wicks near 703.00/698.00 gridlines; thin blue MA line and wicks nearly coincide.\\n- **SPY 15m:** Wicks extend toward 756.00 gridline; thin orange/blue MA lines and wicks overlap.\\n- **SPY 1h:** Wicks drop toward 752.00/760.00 gridlines; thin red MA line and wicks nearly coincide.\\n\\n**Machine status:** All four images report `occlusion_candidates: []` and `ambiguous_or_occluded_data_geometry count=0`. The machine did not flag any of these wick ambiguities.\\n\\n**Assessment:** The vision-identified wick ambiguities are real but minor — they involve thin vertical wicks visually merging with faint vertical time-gridlines, not true occlusion of data. The machine's \\"no occlusion\\" finding is defensible: these are not cases where data is hidden, but where two thin features (wick + time-gridline) are visually close. This is a known limitation of line-based detection, not a perception failure per se.\\n\\n### Volume Strip Location\\n\\n| Image | Vision Observation | Machine Treatment |\\n|-------|-------------------|-------------------|\\n| SPY 30m HA | In-pane overlay at bottom of candles (same pane) | Included in pane (bottom=547) ✅ |\\n| QQQ 30m HA | In-pane overlay at bottom of candles (same pane) | Included in pane (bottom=547) ✅ |\\n| SPY 15m | **Separate sub-pane** below the price divider (100→0 scale bars) | Excluded from pane (bottom=440, above separator) — **but the separator itself was misidentified** |\\n| SPY 1h | Ambiguous: faint in-pane overlay + separate sub-pane (10→0 scale) | Excluded from pane (bottom=486) ✅ |\\n\\n### Discrepancy Summary\\n\\n| # | Image | Field | Machine Value | Vision-Identified Correct Value | Nature |\\n|---|-------|-------|--------------|-------------------------------|--------|\\n| 1 | SPY 15m | `primary_pane_bottom` | 440 (760.00 gridline, partial-width, 4/5 support) | ~578–670 (full-width structural divider, below all gridlines) | **In-pane gridline selected as pane boundary** |\\n\\nNo other discrepancies found. The other three images have machine outputs fully consistent with vision-identified structure.\\n\\n### Verification Requirement Met\\n\\n- ✅ Vision observations recorded for all four images\\n- ✅ Discrepancy between machine output and visible structure identified (SPY 15m pane bottom) and documented with mechanism\\n- ✅ Wick/trace ambiguity assessed for all four (minor, not a perception failure)\\n- ✅ Volume strip location cross-checked\\n- ✅ No code modified\\n\\nThis is an intermediate step result for step-05 (final synthesis).", "artifacts": [], "verification_requirement": "Vision observations recorded for all four images; discrepancies between machine output and visible structure identified and documented. No code modifie