the candidate lines in the separator region are:\\n- y=578: length 327, 3/5 support, 0.6 consensus\\n- y=670: length 549, 3/5 support, 0.6 consensus\\n\\nThe vision model explicitly identifies the pane bottom as \\"a thin full-width divider separating the price pane from the first sub-pane (dense green/red bar strip, 100→0 scale)\\" — a structural element below all gridlines, not the 760.00 gridline at y=440.\\n\\n**Mechanism:** The reference-geometry selector scored the y=440 line (an in-pane price gridline at the 760.00 level, coincident with the last-price tag) above the true pane separator because it had the highest variant support (4/5) and consensus (0.8) among lower-region candidates. The selector weights variant support and consensus but lacks a feature that distinguishes a line coincident with a price-axis label (in-pane gridline) from a structural pane boundary. Notably, the max_length values do not cleanly separate the two: the selected gridline (y=440) has max_length=410 while the true separator (y=578) has max_length=327, so length alone is not a reliable discriminator in this case. The pipeline's own uncertainty reporting (`count=0`) failed to flag this as ambiguous.\\n\\n**Contrast with the other three images:** On SPY 30m HA, QQQ 30m HA, and SPY 1h, the pane separator line had the highest support (5/5, consensus 1.0) and was correctly selected. The SPY 15m layout is the one case where an in-pane gridline outscored the true boundary.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Wick/Trace Ambiguity (All Four Images)\\n\\nVision identified minor wick-vs-gridline visual proximity in the bottom third of the price pane on all four images (wicks approaching horizontal gridlines and vertical time-gridlines). The machine reported `occlusion_candidates: []` and `ambiguous_or_occluded_data_geometry count=0` on all four. This is defensible: these are cases of two thin features being visually close, not true data occlusion. No perception failure here.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Code-Change Justification\\n\\n**A concrete, reproducible perception failure was reproduced on 1 of 4 images (SPY 15m).** The failure is specific, has a clear mechanism, and the pipeline's own uncertainty reporting failed to flag it.\\n\\n**A targeted code change is justified.** The evidence supports a focused fix to the pane-boundary selection logic: the selector needs an additional distinguishing feature beyond variant support and consensus — for example, checking whether a candidate line coincides with a price-axis tick label (indicating an in-pane gridline) versus sitting in a gap between panes (indicating a structural boundary), or checking for the presence of a new content region (oscillator bars, different scale) immediately below the candidate line. The fix scope is narrow (selector scoring/feature weighting for pane-boundary candidates). No broader rewrite is indicated — the other three images, including two with similar multi-pane layouts, were detected correctly.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Constraint Confirmation\\n\\n- **No code was modified** in this task. The pipeline ran exactly as deployed.\\n- All evidence is from the actual `analysis.json` outputs (steps 02–03) and vision cross-checks (step 04).\\n\\n### Analysis Output Directories (This Rerun)\\n\\n1. `C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260919-210317-91ac3473-SPY_20260916-102400-high`\\n2. `C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260919-210322-21dc196f-QQQ_20260916-102500-high`\\n3. `C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260919-210816-b5df96fd-SPY_15m_20260916-102700-high`\\n4. `C:\\\\Users\\\\KHzz\\\\Documents\\\\Norm\\\\images\\\\analysis\\\\20260919-210820-4fe46e4d-SPY_1h_20260916-102700-high`", "artifacts": [], "verification_requirement": "Final report covers all four images with per-image evidence, identifies any reproduced failure with exact location and mechanism, states code-change justification (or lack thereof), confirms no c