rly-session peak, not retested since)\\n\\n### Uncertainty Notes\\n\\n- Volume color calls (green vs. red on specific bars) are visual estimates from a compressed phone screenshot. The *relative* volume trend (contracting into the right side) is consistent across both vision passes and is the more reliable signal.\\n- The exact OHLC of the last 5 candles is pixel-estimated (±0.5). The structural read (tight chop, no clean distribution stack) is robust across both passes.\\n- The \\"D\\" annotation is a user marker, not a system-generated signal. Its placement at the 752 wick low is consistent with the user tracking that level as significant.\\n\\n**This is an intermediate step result. It does not constitute the final answer.**", "artifacts": [], "verification_requirement": "State clearly whether the chart evidence leans toward flow exhaustion or continuation, with specific chart features cited (e.g., 'the last three sessions show higher lows with declining volume on down moves, suggesting exhaustion'). Do not assume persistence of last week's pressure without chart support.", "evidence_count": 5, "resource_status": {"context_state": "full", "message": "full context", "unresponsive_connections": []}}	[]	State clearly whether the chart evidence leans toward flow exhaustion or continuation, with specific chart features cited (e.g., 'the last three sessions show higher lows with declining volume on down moves, suggesting exhaustion'). Do not assume persistence of last week's pressure without chart support.	\N	2026-09-20 11:16:34.501862-04	2026-09-20 11:21:44.660072-04
