25	chat-80cb7910-1e35-4743-b2be-e1b9ac28bc26	# Portfolio Review — `pogicraft.github.io`\n\n**Scope:** Read-only review of `index.html`, `resume.html`, `personal-touch-cleaned.less`, `personal-touch.css`, inline JavaScript, and the project asset inventory. **No files were modified.**\n\nThe recommendations below preserve the site’s hand-built Bootstrap 5 / HTML / CSS / JavaScript character. They do **not** recommend migrating to a framework, adopting a template, adding a plugin system, or changing the repository structure.\n\n---\n\n## High-Impact Fixes\n\nThese are the changes that most directly improve mobile usability, accessibility, navigation, and long-term maintainability.\n\n### 1. Fix mobile/responsive behavior\n\nThe site currently has **no custom `@media` queries**. Responsive behavior is mostly handled by fixed `min-width` values and one JavaScript viewport check, which breaks small screens.\n\n| Issue | Observed location | Recommended fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `body { min-width: 800px }` forces horizontal scrolling on phones | `personal-touch-cleaned.less`, `body` block, lines ~37–46 | Remove `min-width: 800px`. Let Bootstrap’s responsive grid and normal document flow handle small screens. |\n| `#s-head { min-width: 680px }` forces the header wider than small viewports | `personal-touch-cleaned.less`, `#s-head`, lines ~292–330 | Remove or replace with `min-width: 0`. |\n| `#navbar { min-width: 400px }` overflows narrow screens | `personal-touch-cleaned.less`, `#navbar`, lines ~196–210 | Remove or use `max-width: 100vw`. |\n| Carousel images use fixed `height: 600px` | `personal-touch-cleaned.less`, `#div-customer-service`, lines ~468–500 | Change to `width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 600px; object-fit: cover;`. |\n| Carousel indicators are `100px × 100px` | `personal-touch-cleaned.less`, carousel indicator rules | Reduce to a smaller size, or remove the override and use Bootstrap’s default indicator sizing. |\n| Main content uses inline `width: 90%; margin-left: 15%` | `index.html`, `#main-content`, line ~38 | Replace with a Bootstrap grid pattern, such as a `row`/`col` layout, or use CSS that adapts by viewport. |\n| Viewport meta disables pinch-zoom | `index.html`, line ~4 | Remove `user-scalable=no`, `maximum-scale=1.0`, and `minimum-scale=1.0`. This is a WCAG 1.4.4 concern. |\n| One-time JavaScript viewport check with no resize handling | Inline JS, lines ~152–158 | Replace with CSS media queries. If JavaScript is retained, add a resize handler, but CSS is the simpler and more robust fix. |\n\n**Bottom line:** Remove the hard `min-width` constraints and add a few media queries around Bootstrap’s common breakpoints, such as 576px, 768px, and 992px. That would resolve most of the mobile layout problems while keeping the existing hand-built structure.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Fix navigation semantics and accessibility\n\nThe navigation is currently a custom checkbox-driven pattern rather than a standard Bootstrap 5 navbar.\n\nObserved pattern in `index.html`, lines ~16–37:\n\n- `<nav class="navbar">` is present, but there is no `navbar-expand-*`, `navbar-toggler`, or `navbar-nav` structure.\n- A hidden checkbox, `#s2`, drives the menu open/close state.\n- A `<label>` wraps the checkbox and the menu buttons.\n- The hamburger is a `<div id="ham-icon" role="button">` made from empty `<span>` elements.\n- Menu items are `<button onclick="location.href='#...'>` elements rather than links.\n- The toggle has no `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`, or `aria-label`.\n- `#ham-icon` is not keyboard-focusable because it has no `tabindex`.\n- `#menu-up` and `#menu-down` are icon-only buttons with no accessible labels.\n- The `navbar-toggle` class is a Bootstrap 3-era class, not a Bootstrap 5 pattern.\n\nRecommended fixes while preserving the custom visual style:\n\n1. Convert `#ham-icon` to a real `<button>` element.\n2. Add:\n   - `aria-expanded="false"` / `aria-expanded="true"`\n   - `aria-controls="nav-menu"`\n   - `aria-label="Toggle navigation"`\n3. Convert the menu items from `<button onclick="location.href='#section'">` to semantic links:\n   ```html\n   <a href="#div-developer">Software Development</a>\n   ```\n4. Remove the `<label>` wrapper around the menu buttons. A label should label the checkbox, not wrap unrelated buttons.\n5. Keep the checkbox-driven open/close behavior if desired, but make the checkbox a sibling of the menu list rather than an ancestor of the buttons.\n6. Remove or simplify the decorative `.hazy-black` overlay and the empty `#nav-back` div. They add stacking complexity without meaningful function.\n7. Remove or properly label `#menu-up` and `#menu-down`. If they do not perform a useful action, remove them.\n\nThis keeps the hand-built navigation feel but makes it keyboard-accessible and removes the label-wrapping-buttons problem.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Fix accessibility and content visibility\n\n| Issue | Observed location | Recommended fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `<html>` has no `lang` attribute | `index.html`, line ~1 | Add `lang="en"`. WCAG 3.1.1. |\n| Profile image has no `alt` text | `index.html`, profile image in `#s-head` | Add meaningful alt text, for example `alt="Portrait of Alexander Wayland-James"`. WCAG 1.1.1. |\n| Heading order is inverted: `h2` → `h4` → `h1` → `h6` | `index.html`, header section | Make the person’s name the single `<h1>`. Use `<h2>` for major sections and `<h3>` for subsections. Convert the byline paragraph from `<h6>` to `<p>`. |\n| Three section titles are CSS `::before` pseudo-elements | `personal-touch-cleaned.less`: `#div-developer:before`, `#div-finance:before`, `#div-customer-service:before` | Replace with real `<h2>` elements in the HTML. Remove the `::before` title rules. Pseudo-element text is not reliably exposed to screen readers. |\n| Footer text contrast is too low | `#s-foot` uses dark blue background; body text color is `#666` | Lighten the footer text, for example `color: #ccc` or `color: #e6e6e6`. Current contrast is approximately 2.8:1, below WCAG AA. |\n| `#s-head` is nearly invisible by default | `personal-touch-cleaned.less`: `#s-head { opacity: .1 }`; inline JS adds `.on-load` | Make the default state visible. If a fade-in is desired, use a CSS animation whose final state is visible, or provide a `<noscript>` fallback. |\n| Resume section is empty without JavaScript | `#div-resume` is populated by `$.load()` in inline JS, lines ~186–188 | Inline the resume content directly into `index.html`. This removes the AJAX dependency, the missing `resumeSection.js` 404, the global style leak, and the height-calculation bug. |\n| `#highlight-box` is decorative but not hidden from assistive tech | `index.html`, finance section | Add `aria-hidden="true"`. |\n| Missing semantic landmarks | Throughout `index.html` | Use `<header>` for the top identity section, `<main>` for the primary content area, and `<footer>` for the footnotes section. |\n| Hamburger toggle is not focusable | `index.html`, `#ham-icon` | Convert to a real `<button>` as described above. |\n\n---\n\n### 4. Simplify or remove brittle JavaScript\n\nAll custom JavaScript is inline in `index.html`, roughly lines ~149–185. Most of it can be replaced with CSS or semantic HTML.\n\n| Behavior | Observed location | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sticky nav using `document.onscroll` to set `#navbar` top position | Inline JS, lines ~159–162 | Remove. Replace with CSS: `#navbar { position: sticky; top: 0; }`. This removes the scroll-handler overwrite risk, missing throttling, and missing `passive` flag. |\n| Finance button hover highlight moving `#highlight-box` | Inline JS, lines ~164–175 | Remove or replace with a CSS `:hover` effect. The buttons already have Bootstrap button hover states. This removes the `mouseover`/`mouseenter` issue, missing `mouseleave`, lack of touch support, and fragile `offsetLeft`/`offsetWidth` positioning. |\n| Nav toggle class switching | Inline JS, lines ~177–184 | Simplify. Remove the dead `$('.left-offsetter')` line, because no element has that class. Remove or simplify the `.hazy-black` overlay logic. Ideally, drive the hamburger animation from the checkbox `:checked` state in CSS. |\n| One-time viewport check | Inline JS, lines ~152–158 | Replace with CSS media queries. |\n| Header reveal via `addClass('on-load')` | Inline JS, line ~151 | Replace with a CSS animation or make the header visible by default. |\n| Resume loading via `$.load()` | Inline JS, lines ~186–188 | Remove. Inline the resume content into `index.html`. |\n\nAfter these changes, the custom JavaScript can be reduced to almost nothing. Bootstrap 5’s collapse and carousel components work without jQuery, so the jQuery dependency can likely be removed entirely.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Stop compiling LESS in the browser\n\n`index.html` currently loads the LESS source directly:\n\n```html\n<link rel="stylesheet/less" href="/css/personal-touch-cleaned.less">\n```\n\nand loads a runtime LESS compiler from a CDN.\n\nThe compiled file `css/personal-touch.css` already exists, but it is out of sync with the LESS source. For example, the two files disagree on `#navbar` z-index, `#nav-area` z-index, `#s-head` background, and body display behavior.\n\nRecommended fix:\n\n1. Recompile `personal-touch-cleaned.less` once into `personal-touch.css`.\n2. Link the compiled CSS file instead of the `.less` file.\n3. Remove the runtime LESS compiler script.\n4. Keep the `.less` file as source if desired, but do not load it in production.\n\nThis removes a runtime dependency and eliminates the risk of browser-side LESS compilation issues.\n\n---\n\n## Remove or Simplify\n\nThese items are dead, redundant, or out of sync and can be removed or cleaned up with little to no functional risk.\n\n### Dead or unused files\n\n| File or group | Approximate size | Reason |\n|---|---:|---|\n| `css/bootstrap*.css` and related local Bootstrap CSS variants | ~2.5 MB | Bootstrap CSS is loaded from CDN. These local copies are not linked. |\n| `css/bootstrap-theme-darkly.css`, `css/bootstrap-theme-lumen.css`, `css/bootstrap-theme-sandstone.css` | ~750 KB | Bootswatch themes are not linked. |\n| `js/bootstrap*.js` local copies | ~730 KB | Bootstrap JS is loaded from CDN. |\n| `js/AOS.js` | 23 KB | Never referenced. No `data-aos` attributes are present in the HTML. |\n| `js/myApp.js` | 38 B | AngularJS stub. AngularJS is not loaded. |\n| `js/myCtrl.js` | 18 B | Comment-only stub. |\n| `css/barebones.css` | 83 B | Contains one unused test class. |\n| `css/dropdown-converted.css` | 2.7 KB | Unused dropdown design experiment. |\n| `css/dropdown-example.sass` | 3.2 KB | SASS source for the unused dropdown experiment. |\n| `css/personal-touch.css` | 7.3 KB | Out of sync with the active LESS file. Recompile and replace it, or delete it. |\n| `files/resume.html` | 2 KB | Duplicate of root `resume.html`. |\n| `resources/profile.png` | 2 MB | Duplicate of `files/profile.png`. |\n\n**Total removable: roughly 6 MB of unused or duplicated assets.**\n\n---\n\n### Dead or brittle CSS rules in `personal-touch-cleaned.less`\n\n| Rule or pattern | Observed location | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| `* { z-index: 0 }` inside the `:root` block | Lines ~14–35 | Remove. This global z-index reset creates fragile stacking behavior. Fix the specific negative z-index values individually if needed. |\n| `.red-box`, `.blue-box`, `.border-box`, `.dotted-box` | Lines ~14–35 | Remove. No elements in the HTML use these classes. |\n| Unused `@layer-*` variables | Lines ~1–6 | Remove. They are never referenced. |\n| Unused `@ccolor-yellow` | Line ~7 | Remove. |\n| Unused CSS custom properties: `--full-menu-height`, `--ccolor-nice-blue`, `--ccolor-solid-yellow` | Lines ~9–13 | Remove. |\n| `.rectangle-list` rules | `#div-developer` area | Remove. No HTML element uses this class. |\n| Empty `ul li {}` rule | `#div-finance` area | Remove. |\n| IE6/7-style `*list-style: decimal` hack | `#div-developer` list rules | Remove. |\n| Excessive `-webkit-`, `-moz-`, `-o-` vendor prefixes on `#ham-icon` | `#ham-icon` rules | Remove. Modern browsers do not need these prefixes for the transforms and transitions used. |\n| `justify-items: baseline` used in a flexbox context | `#div-customer-service` list rules | Remove. `justify-items` is not a flexbox property. |\n| `resume.html` inline `h5 { font-family: 'Raleway', sans-serif; }` | `resume.html` inline style | Scope the rule or remove it. `'Raleway'` is not loaded, and the unscoped `h5` rule leaks into the whole page when injected. |\n| Font references that are never loaded | `#s-head h1` uses `'Titillium Web'`; `resume.html` uses `'Raleway'` | Either load the fonts intentionally or remove the references and use the existing Roboto/system fallback. |\n| Font Awesome 5 glyph reference while Font Awesome 6 is loaded | `#s-head h4::before` references `'Font Awesome\\ 5 Free'` | Update to the correct Font Awesome 6 icon approach or replace with a real HTML icon/character. |\n\n---\n\n## Optional Polish\n\nThese are lower-priority improvements. They do not fix broken behavior or accessibility violations, but they would make the site feel more finished and professional.\n\n| Item | Recommendation |\n|---|---|\n| Resume content is placeholder text | Replace the Lorem Ipsum-style resume content with real experience, education, and project details. |\n| `**Work in Progress**` appears as literal asterisks | Remove the Markdown-style asterisks or replace with a proper badge/label. |\n| Commented-out `<li>` items remain in production HTML | Remove the commented-out placeholder list items. |\n| Empty divs remain in the markup | Remove or give purpose to `#traits-list`, `#nav-back`, `#resume-top`, and `#resume-bottom`. |\n| Empty `class=""` attributes | Remove empty class attributes. |\n| `<br>` tags are used for spacing | Replace with CSS margin or padding. |\n| Finance section has only button labels | Add short descriptions for each finance topic so the section communicates actual experience. |\n| Customer service section is only a photo carousel | Add a short paragraph describing the role, responsibilities, or relevant skills. |\n| Byline is incomplete | Update the byline to mention all major areas: software development, finance, and customer service. |\n| Footer is a development log | Replace “Started / Updated” dates with contact information, a brief closing statement, or remove it if not useful. |\n| `#div-accomplishments` contains a “Certifications” heading | Make the ID and heading consistent, or rename the section to match its content. |\n| Generic page title | Change `<title>Welcome</title>` to something more specific, such as `Alexander Wayland-James — Portfolio`. |\n| Meta description missing | Add a concise `<meta name="description">` for search engines and link previews. |\n| Google Fonts request lacks `display=swap` | Add `&display=swap` to the font request to reduce invisible-text risk. |\n| Bootstrap CSS CDN link lacks SRI | Add a Subresource Integrity hash if the CDN URL is pinned. |\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThe highest-value changes are:\n\n1. **Fix mobile layout** by removing the hard `min-width` constraints, making carousel images responsive, and replacing the one-time JavaScript viewport check with CSS media queries.\n2. **Make the site usable without JavaScript** by making `#s-head` visible by default and inlining the resume content instead of loading it with `$.load()`.\n3. **Improve navigation accessibility** by converting the hamburger to a real button, adding ARIA attributes, converting menu items to semantic links, and removing the `<label>` wrapper around unrelated buttons.\n4. **Fix basic accessibility violations**, including missing `lang`, missing image `alt` text, inverted heading order, pseudo-element section titles, low footer contrast, and missing landmarks.\n5. **Simplify brittle JavaScript** by replacing the manual sticky-nav scroll handler with CSS `position: sticky`, removing the decorative finance highlight box, and reducing the remaining inline JS to a small amount of behavior or none at all.\n6. **Stop browser-side LESS compilation** by linking the compiled CSS file and removing the runtime LESS compiler.\n7. **Delete dead assets and dead CSS**, including unused local Bootstrap copies, unused JavaScript libraries, duplicate files, unused LESS variables, unused classes, and obsolete vendor prefixes.\n\nThese changes preserve the site’s hand-built Bootstrap 5 / HTML / CSS / JavaScript character while making it more mobile-friendly, accessible, maintainable, and free of unnecessary dead code.	2026-09-14 11:34:21.090337-04
