69	chat-db565993-1068-4237-8a90-1905ec45a0bb	# SPY Calibration & Tomorrow Forecast — Final Synthesis\n\n## 1. What Was Corrected (and Why)\n\nThe prior model produced a mild 752–759 grind because of five compounding assumptions: a hard speed cap (~2 pts/day, "no single-session move >1.5%"), the F2/F3 bid treated as a holding floor, M3/M4 excluded from driving speed, sub-750 paths quarantined behind a discrete-shock precondition, and no support-break acceleration branch.\n\nThree allowed corrections — each justified by ex-ante evidence already in the frozen pre-move set — produced a model that reproduces today's realized path:\n\n| Correction | Ex-ante justification (no hindsight) |\n|---|---|\n| Remove hard speed cap → **conditional speed on structure** | F4 progressive weakening (each bounce weaker) + price at lower range + no structural support below 756 (F5+F6) |\n| Reclassify F2/F3 from **holding floor → failing/reactive bid** | Two small-bodied up-signals vs four aligned down-signals; failing-bid reading is more consistent with the structure |\n| Make **M3/M4 continuous speed drivers** (not discrete-event-only) | M3/M4 are ongoing conditions; the raw set's own A14/A11/B1 already contain the fast-break mechanic |\n\n**Corrected model's forecast for today:** open ~758–759 → break 756–757 in first 1–2 hrs → fast flush below 750 (low ~749) in first 2–3 hrs → M1 reactive dip-buy → rebound to ~753–755 → close ~754. **This matches the realized scorecard** (sub-750 break, brief, rebound to ~754.10).\n\n## 2. Diagnosis (Error Classification)\n\n| Error type | Contribution | What had to change |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Model-structure** (primary) | No acceleration branch + hard speed cap | Add conditional speed; remove cap |\n| **Weighting** (secondary) | F2/F3 over-weighted as a floor against four down-signals | Reclassify as failing/reactive |\n| **Synthesis-selection** (contributing) | Fast-break paths (A14, A11/B1) demoted to subsumed/Alt-4 | Promote sub-750 to a primary/major branch |\n| **Perception** (limited) | Outcome-chart wick resolution (2.50 gridline spacing at 709×1536 px) | Not a causal error in ex-ante reasoning; isolated to scorecard verification |\n\n## 3. Tomorrow's Forecast (Sep 18) — From the Corrected Model\n\n**Starting state:** SPY closed 754.10. The 756–757 support is broken and now overhead resistance. The sub-750 low (~749) is the reactive bid's catch zone. M3/M4 continuous pressure is still present. Price is at the lower range of the Sep 3–16 window.\n\n---\n\n### Primary Path: Continued Weakness with Reactive Bid Floor\n\n| Element | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| **Open** | ~753–754 (flat to slight gap down from 754.10) |\n| **Morning (first 2–3 hrs)** | Drifts lower through 752–753; tests the 749–750 zone (today's low) |\n| **Midday/Afternoon** | Reactive bid (M1) catches at ~749–750; weak rebound to 752–753 |\n| **Close** | **~751–753** |\n| **Intraday range** | 749–754 |\n| **Speed** | Moderate — not a fast flush (the 756–757 break already happened; this is a continuation below broken support), but not a slow grind either (M3/M4 continuous pressure + no structural support between 754 and 749) |\n| **Shape** | Down → catch at 749–750 → weak rebound → close below the rebound high |\n\n**Why this is NOT mechanically extra bearish:** The corrected model's reactive bid is real (it caught today). The primary path assumes it catches again at 749–750. The close is slightly lower than today (751–753 vs 754.10) because the bid is getting exhausted over consecutive days of M3/M4 pressure, and the 756–757 resistance caps any upside. This is the natural continuation of the corrected model's assumptions, not a penalty.\n\n**Confirmation:** SPY closes below 754 on Sep 18 AND hits 750 or below intraday.\n**Invalidation:** SPY closes above 756 on Sep 18 (reclaims broken support) OR SPY does not reach 750 intraday (bid holds higher than expected).\n\n---\n\n### Alternative 1: Bullish Reversal / M1 Proactive\n\n- **Trigger:** SPY