184	chat-fa339cc8-928b-4cd3-b0c7-6a729854cca3	Thank you for the careful review. I accept the feedback and have retained the lesson.\n\n## Acknowledgment\n\nYou're right. The cors-dummy README's top-level framing presented the repository as a coherent, finished two-part architecture (FastAPI backend + Vue frontend) when the evidence actually shows an **experimental, multi-stage troubleshooting project** that evolved over time:\n\n1. Started with a Vue frontend calling a local FastAPI service.\n2. Added permissive CORS experiments and a Flask implementation.\n3. Moved frontend experiments toward services hosted on kh22.\n\nThe checked-in `dist/` is a stale artifact from the local-backend phase that doesn't match the latest Vue source — a concrete example of a conflicting/older artifact that my top-level description flattened away. The per-file inventory was accurate, but the synthesis imposed a coherence the repository doesn't actually have.\n\n## Durable Lesson Retained\n\n> **When reconstructing project intent from a repository, use chronology, conflicting artifacts, and older/stale files to represent the project's actual evolution and current state — rather than flattening all currently present files into one clean, finished architecture.**\n\nConcretely, this means:\n\n- **Look for temporal signals**: commit order, file dates, version mismatches between source and build artifacts, references to hosts or services that no longer match the current setup.\n- **Treat conflicts as evidence, not noise**: a `dist/` that doesn't match the latest source, a Flask file alongside a FastAPI file, a frontend pointing at a remote host while a local backend also exists — these are *stages of experimentation*, not redundant copies of one design.\n- **Describe the project as it actually is**: if it's a work-in-progress with multiple approaches tried, say so. Don't narrate it as a settled architecture just because the files happen to coexist in one directory.\n- **Distinguish "what is present" from "what is current"**: presence in the tree is not the same as being the active or intended configuration.\n\nThis lesson applies to all future repository interpretation, README writing, and project-summarization work.\n\n## File Mutation\n\n**None.** No files were created, modified, or deleted. The cors-dummy README at `D:\\LOCAL_Share\\Code Projects\\cors-dummy\\README.md` (SHA-256 `935ad8e5…058daa`) remains exactly as it was. The lesson is about how I interpret and describe projects going forward, not about correcting the existing file.	2026-09-19 01:44:06.623907-04
