402	chat-3a1c2103-f75a-4477-a4b1-01d0a0d60ad2	step-02	2		**DURABLE CONTINUATION NOTE — Step 2/6: docker-compose.yml + Traefik config**\n\n**Decided (locked):**\n- Networks: `proxy` (traefik, pihole, test-http) + `backend` (pihole, devbox). Pihole on both so devbox can use it as DNS resolver.\n- Bind strategy: single `TAILNET_BIND_ADDR` env var, default `127.0.0.1`. User sets to Tailscale IP (`tailscale ip -4`) for tailnet access. Never `0.0.0.0`. Applies to all host port mappings (8080, 8443, 8081, 53/tcp+udp, 2222).\n- No Docker socket mount. Traefik discovery via **file provider** (static `dynamic.yml`), not Docker API.\n- TLS: `scripts/setup-tls.sh` (POSIX) ensures `TLS_CERTS_DIR/tls.crt` + `tls.key` exist before Traefik starts. Modes: `tailscale` (expect user-provided or `tailscale cert`), `internal-ca` (openssl self-signed), `none` (still generate a throwaway self-signed so Traefik boots; user uses HTTP only). Static config always references the cert paths.\n- Healthchecks: traefik → `wget -qO- http://127.0.0.1:80/ping`; pihole → `wget -qO- http://127.0.0.1:80/`; test-http → `wget -qO- http://127.0.0.1:8080/`; devbox → `pgrep -x sshd` (note: step-04 must ensure `procps` in image).\n- test-http: `build: ./test-service` (step-03 creates Dockerfile). devbox: `build: ./devbox` (step-04).\n- Pihole admin UI routed via Traefik only (no direct host port). DNS port 53 exposed directly.\n- Compose: no `version:` field (deprecated). `name:` from `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME`.\n- Traefik image: `traefik:v3.1` (pin for reproducibility).\n- `.env.example` needs: `TAILNET_BIND_ADDR=127.0.0.1` added.\n\n**Unresolved (notes cut off here):**\n- **File-provider env-substitution problem:** `dynamic.yml` is a plain file; `${TAILSCALE_FQDN}` is NOT substituted by compose. Options considered:\n  1. Read-only Docker socket + compose labels (labels DO get env substitution). Requirement says "least-risk practical approach" is acceptable if documented. Read-only socket is narrower than full mount.\n  2. Generate `dynamic.yml` via a script (like setup-tls.sh) that substitutes the FQDN at deploy time.\n  3. Hardcode FQDN in dynamic.yml with a "edit me" comment.\n  - **Notes were literally cut off mid-sentence evaluating option 1.** No decision made. This is the #1 blocker.\n- Devbox healthcheck: `pgrep` may not exist in the base image. Fallback: `bash -c 'exec 3<>/dev/tcp/127.0.0.1/22'`. Step-04 must resolve.\n- Traefik dashboard: always exposed on 8081 (tailnet-only via bind addr). `TRAEFIK_DASHBOARD_ENABLED` in .env is informational only (compose can't conditionally expose ports). Document that user removes the port line to disable.\n\n**Partial constructions (drafted in notes, not yet written to disk):**\n- Compose file skeleton: all 4 services, ports, volumes, networks, healthchecks, depends_on. ~80% complete in the notes.\n- `config/traefik.yml` static: log, accessLog, api (dashboard+insecure), entryPoints (web :80, websecure :443), ping, providers.file, certificates section. ~90% complete.\n- `config/dynamic.yml`: routers (pihole-admin, test-http) + services. Blocked on FQDN substitution.\n- `scripts/setup-tls.sh`: logic sketched, not written.\n\n**Branches rejected:**\n- 0.0.0.0 binding (violates requirement).\n- Full Docker socket mount (violates requirement 7).\n- Two static config files (traefik.yml / traefik.no-tls.yml) — replaced by setup-tls.sh approach.\n- Compose labels for routing (requires Docker provider → socket).\n- Binding to 127.0.0.1 only (defeats tailnet access purpose).\n\n**Exact next work:**\n1. **Resolve the FQDN-in-dynamic-config problem.** Decide between read-only Docker socket + labels vs. script-generated dynamic.yml. If socket: mount `:ro`, document as least-risk, use compose labels with `${TAILSCALE_FQDN}`. If script: extend setup-tls.sh or add `scripts/generate-dynamic.sh`.\n2. Write `docker-compose.yml` to disk (skeleton is 80% done in notes).\n3. Write `config/traefik.yml` (static).\n4. Write `config/dynamic.yml` (or the generation script).\n5. Write `scripts/setup-tls.sh`.\n6. Add `TAILNET_BIND_ADDR` to `.env.example`.\n7. Verify: `docker compose config` parses; grep for 0.0.0.0, docker.sock; confirm all 4 healthchecks; confirm network references.\n\n**Verification checklist (step-02):**\n- [ ] YAML valid\n- [ ] All services reference defined networks\n- [ ] No port bound to 0.0.0.0\n- [ ] No docker.sock mount\n- [ ] Healthchecks on traefik, pihole, devbox, test-http\n- [ ] All paths/ports from .env vars	16000	2026-09-20 12:06:25.192172-04	2026-09-20 12:47:05.88546-04
